window.GALLERY_CHAPTERS=(window.GALLERY_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"title":"Chapter 18","paragraphs":["Health (3)","As I mentioned before, capturing a mandrake was surprisingly simple.","First, pull it out of the ground. Then, if it looked like it was about to scream, beat it like a dog on the hottest day of summer.","If it still stubbornly tried to scream? Stuff its mouth with dirt. It couldn’t do anything after that.","Using that method, I first harvested the most urgent request—the Starlight Princess’s—and then slowly gathered enough for the other gallery regulars as well.","The next person I gave one to was the Heavenly Demon.","She had helped me more than anyone else.","[Wild Grylls]: Take this and replenish your vitality. Are you feeling all right now?","[Heavenly Demon]: I was only in danger back then. I’m perfectly fine now. I’m more worried about your condition.","[Wild Grylls]: Aside from my stomach hurting a few times a day—probably because of the Bigu Pill—I’m okay.","[Heavenly Demon]: That’s proof your body is expelling impurities. You never underwent Reforging the Bones and Cleansing the Marrow, so they’re leaving your body that way instead.","[Wild Grylls]: So that’s a good thing?","[Heavenly Demon]: Of course. If you want, I can give you more. You gave me something beneficial as well, after all.","[Wild Grylls]: I’m fine. Just the antidote and the medicine for tinnitus that you mentioned before are more than enough.","[Heavenly Demon]: I feel guilty, as though I’m always the one receiving.","[Wild Grylls]: That’s exactly what I should be saying.","Every time I talked to her, I couldn’t help but think how admirable the Heavenly Demon was.","Everyone teased her for being an old-timer, but whenever someone gave her something, she always repaid the favor.","This was what a true adult should be like.","Though I still had no idea why someone like her spent time in this gallery.","Then again, judging from her usual posts, she was every bit as much of a gallery addict as the rest of us.","Maybe she simply got bored living such a carefree life.","So this is the antidote... and this one treats tinnitus.","After finishing our trade, I checked the items she’d sent.","The labels were written in characters that looked similar to Chinese, so I was confused at first, but the Heavenly Demon explained them.","The gallery automatically translated conversations, but only inside the gallery itself.","Every country still had its own language.","Come to think of it, who on earth had created this gallery and even implemented automatic translation?","It was a strange world in many ways, but that wasn’t something I needed to worry about right now.","[SwordMaster]: But... I told you I don’t want to become healthier.","[Wild Grylls]: Just consider it repayment for the elixir you gave me before. If you don’t want it, you can give it to someone who’s sick. Or sell it.","[SwordMaster]: Hmm... All right. Since you put it that way, I guess I can’t really refuse.","[Wild Grylls]: Thank you.","I practically forced SwordMaster into accepting it.","I couldn’t understand why anyone would refuse something that could make them healthier.","Isn’t he going to regret this someday?","Countless people had neglected their health and paid the price.","Health was something you couldn’t simply take care of whenever you wanted.","You had to look after it consistently before problems appeared.","[PraisetheSun]: So this is that precious herb?","[Wild Grylls]: Yep. I heard it’s really valuable. You gave me that shield before, so this one’s a gift.","[PraisetheSun]: Does it... happen to improve stamina? You know, that kind of thing?","[Wild Grylls]: Uh... Since it’s an ingredient for elixirs, I guess it probably does?","So he was a guy.","Well, his username should’ve tipped me off.","[PraisetheSun]: Thanks. I’ll give you an amazing gift later.","[Wild Grylls]: You’ve already given me the shield. If I find anything else that’s good for your health, I’ll bring it to you.","[PraisetheSun]: You’re too kind. Then let’s do this—every time you give me a mandrake, I’ll give you one thing you want. Sound good?","[Wild Grylls]: Works for me.","I had more than enough mandrakes.","The colony was large enough that I could keep supplying the regulars for quite a while.","Still, I wasn’t planning to harvest them recklessly.","If I ran out when I truly needed them, I’d regret it.","It was better to think of them as an emergency reserve.","After finishing my trade with PraisetheSun, I contacted CheongguPrincess.","She’d helped me before, too, so I wanted to give her one as a gift.","[Wild Grylls]: CheongguPrincess, here’s one for you.","[CheongguPrincess]: Thank yooou! I’ll send you another uniform in return!","[Wild Grylls]: Thanks! Whose is it this time?","[CheongguPrincess]: It’s Gioni Sader, the legendary goalkeeper of Chayu!","I still had no idea who that was.","Still, a gift was a gift.","When I’d first received one of her uniforms, I’d wondered whether it would be useful at all.","Surprisingly, it had been incredibly helpful.","The material was so elastic that it never felt restrictive.","[Wild Grylls]: Thanks. Was it the Champions League? I hope you win it.","[CheongguPrincess]: Not the Champions League—the Challengers Cup! But thank yooou!","[Wild Grylls]: Right, the Challengers Cup. That’s the tournament where every club in Mephisto competes, right?","[CheongguPrincess]: Yep! It’s the greatest competition in the world! Clubs from other countries compete too, not just Mephisto’s!","I didn’t have a favorite team, but I did enjoy soccer.","Watching underdog South Korea defeat powerhouse Germany had felt like witnessing a miracle.","And when Argentina won the World Cup, all I could think was, Wow... they actually did it.","Soccer was the kind of sport where even the greatest players and strongest teams could become victims of a miracle.","Its unpredictability alone was enough to make it the world’s most popular sport.","Especially in this world, where there wasn’t much entertainment besides the gallery.","No wonder sports were so popular.","I wonder if they have something like the World Cup.","According to CheongguPrincess, the Challengers Cup—or simply the Challs—allowed clubs from other nations to participate alongside Mephisto’s.","Apparently, there were domestic tournaments as well as international competitions.","In the distant past, things had been different.","But now every team consisted of multiple races, turning competitions into battles over club pride rather than national identity.","There didn’t seem to be anything resembling a World Cup, where people rooted for their country instead of a club.","Not that it’s any of my business.","I already had enough problems of my own.","Even if I was interested in soccer, I didn’t have the luxury of worrying about it.","Still, curiosity was curiosity.","I figured I’d look into it later.","From what I’d heard, humanity’s influence had been growing stronger by the day, even beginning to shake Mephisto’s position as the founding nation.","Maybe I’ll make a post asking about it.","The gallery really was convenient at times like this.","I wanted to ask CheongguPrincess more questions, but unfortunately, time was limited.","Apparently, only the head moderator could adjust private chat time.","Maybe I should submit a suggestion.","[Allfather]: Oh! Thank you very much. How much should I pay you?","[Wild Grylls]: You gave me valuable information, so you don’t have to pay anything. By the way, have you made any progress on the antidote for the Golden Poison Frog?","[Allfather]: May I answer honestly?","Seeing those words left me puzzled.","May I answer honestly?","That didn’t sound very encouraging.","[Wild Grylls]: Thanks. Go Chayu!","[CheongguPrincess]: Thank yooou! Hope you survive another day!","Our conversation ended with me cheering for Chayu.","The only regulars left were Allfather and Passing Dwarf.","[Wild Grylls]: Hello, Allfather. I’d like to give you a mature mandrake.","[Wild Grylls]: Did the results turn out badly?","[Allfather]: Yes. Especially for you, Mr. Grylls, this information is important.","[Wild Grylls]: Hmm... Please explain.","[Allfather]: The Golden Poison Frog’s venom is far stronger than we anticipated. My laboratory nearly dissolved because of it.","[Wild Grylls]: Whoa... Are you okay?","As everyone knew, the Golden Poison Frog’s venom was extraordinarily potent.","It wasn’t even acidic, yet it could melt wood.","That alone spoke volumes.","I’d warned Allfather beforehand, but the fact that his laboratory had almost been destroyed showed just how dangerous it truly was.","If I could somehow make use of that substance, my body might eventually develop resistance to it.","[Allfather]: Yes. Fortunately, there was no accident. But the more important issue is that the poison is so powerful that even the antidote failed to neutralize it.","[Wild Grylls]: Then... ?","Did that mean I’d have to buy the Water of Life after all?","Just as that thought crossed my mind, Allfather continued.","[Allfather]: But it wasn’t a complete loss. While researching the poison sac, I discovered something else.","[Wild Grylls]: That sounds a lot more promising.","[Allfather]: Yes. If this goes well, you may be able to develop resistance to poison.","Allfather’s explanation went something like this.","After researching the Golden Poison Frog’s venom sac, he had discovered a special substance inside it.","[Wild Grylls]: Wouldn’t that be even better?","[Allfather]: However, you will need to ingest it for at least two weeks. Only then will you be able to develop resistance even to the Golden Poison Frog’s venom.","[Wild Grylls]: That sounds like you’re telling me to catch more frogs.","[Allfather]: You really are perceptive.","Good grief. The nerve of this man.","I let out a dry laugh at Allfather’s shamelessness.","Still, it was well worth trying.","He was talking about gaining resistance to poison itself. For someone in my situation, that would be especially useful.","Right now, insects are more dangerous than the frogs.","At least the Golden Poison Frog’s venom could be blocked with a shield or avoided.","But snakes, venomous insects, and poisonous plants could appear from anywhere.","I was also particularly susceptible to rashes from plants, which made Allfather’s proposal even more appealing.","[Wild Grylls]: It doesn’t sound bad. But I’d appreciate it if you finished making the medicine from what I gave you before first.","[Allfather]: I do have some sense of shame. I’ll prepare the proper dosage and send it to you within two days.","[Wild Grylls]: Thank you.","Considering how much money he possessed, his skill was probably the real deal.","Now the only one left is Passing Dwarf.","Lastly, I gifted a mandrake to Passing Dwarf.","And then that bastard turned it into liquor almost immediately.","I was utterly dumbfounded when I saw it.","I could at least have understood if he had sold it for money.","My conversation with Allfather had ended, but I still felt somewhat uneasy.","He had said it worked by gradually acclimating the body to poison rather than acting as a direct antidote.","That meant the effects would not appear immediately.","It was exactly the kind of thing that could come back to bite me.","For now, I’ll have to rely on the antidote the Heavenly Demon gave me.","I did not think Allfather intended to scam me.","If he had wanted to, he would have done it when I first handed over the Golden Poison Frog.","└ Passing Dwarf: I’m rich, lol.","└ Wild Grylls: Yeah, good for you. Your shit must be huge.","└ Passing Dwarf: Thanks for the compliment.","└ Wild Grylls: You bastard, lol.","└ I’ve got nothing to say to that, hahaha.","I should have known better than to argue.","Some people were so sick they could die any day, while others soaked valuable medicine in alcohol and called it a day.","The world really was unfair.","Though the fact that I had been dropped into the Forest of Four Seasons was unfair enough on its own.","In any case, now that I had sent gifts to all the regulars who had helped me, I moved on to my next task.","Thud! Thump!","\"Ugh. This is killing me.\"","Digging traps near the cave entrance.","I had a feeling I would regret it if I kept putting the work off, so I needed to do a little every day.","My whole body would ache the next morning?","That was still better than dying.","Times like this really make me want a shower.","For now, I had no choice but to endure it.","Even after the threat of the Golden Poison Frogs disappeared, showering every day would probably be difficult.","The problem was not disposing of the water.","It was my clothes.","To minimize contact with insects and plants, clothing was not optional.","But wearing the same clothes every day would create hygiene problems of its own.","That meant I needed to wash them from time to time, which naturally required a large amount of water.","I’m going to need a lot of soap.","In a place like this, hygiene was especially important.","If I came down with an illness, things could become dangerous very quickly.","It was not as though every sickness disappeared the moment you took medicine.","Perhaps that was why, once the sun began to set, I stopped working and bought some water.","I had been sweating, so I should at least wash the parts that needed cleaning.","Once you experienced that refreshing feeling, it was difficult to forget.","The money felt wasteful, but compared to the price of my life, it was cheap.","Is this my second day?","After giving myself a rough wash, I connected to the gallery.","I had finished everything for the day and wanted to leave a record.","I would probably end up making one every day, just like the Starlight Princess.","Title: Survival, Day 2","Wild Grylls","(Photo of a campfire)","Day two of survival complete! See you tomorrow.","└ Heavenly Demon: Rest well.","└ SwordMaster: Good work. I gave the mandrake to my mother.","└ CheongguPrincess: Thank yooou for the gift. Stay healthy!","└ PraisetheSun: Post something first thing tomorrow. I’ll be worried otherwise.","└ Don’t Abandon the Hero: Good work today!","Even the head moderator had left a comment.","Apparently, I was attracting more attention than I had thought.","I did not pay much attention to anonymous users.","Most of them were too busy venting their own desires.","└ Passing Dwarf: Hey. I made liquor with what you gave me, and now I can’t sleep, lol.","└ Wild Grylls: Just die already.","└ Passing Dwarf: Hic—hahaha!","└ Damn, I can smell the alcohol through the post, hahaha.","Maybe I had grown somewhat close to the regulars.","Most of the comments were well wishes, telling me I had worked hard.","There was one useless bastard among them, but he was still helpful, so I let it slide.","He might talk like this, but he was also the same guy who had once felt bad enough to send me alcohol as an apology.","Come to think of it, I wonder what happened to the Starlight Princess.","The lack of news was making me anxious.","I hoped she would at least make a post tomorrow.","I slowly lowered myself onto the ground.","It felt a little soft instead of completely hard.","That was thanks to the mat and pillow I had purchased from the auction house.","Apparently, they had been stuffed with straw.","It really is... kind of soft.","Perhaps because of the exhaustion from the day and the soft bedding, drowsiness slowly began to wash over me.","Unable to resist it, I gradually closed my eyes.","All while hoping that the next day would bring only good things.","***","Around the time Grylls finished his work and fell asleep, the gallery remained active regardless of day or night.","Normally, it overflowed with all kinds of pointless posts.","But lately, things had changed.","The topic was Wild Grylls, the man who claimed to have fallen into the Forest of Four Seasons.","Once it became certain that he really was there, countless people began paying attention to him.","Even the incident involving the mature mandrake, which had seemed like nothing more than a minor commotion, was beginning to take on a different meaning.","Title: Gallery User Is Screwed in Real Time ;;","My friend is a knight, and one of his superiors traded with Grylls and ordered him to bring back a mature mandrake ;;","└ Really?","└ Yeah. The guy’s pretty high-ranking.","└ This feels way too sudden.","└ Apparently, they’d been watching quietly all along. The post that dwarf made seems to have convinced them.","└ Hahahaha. At this rate, won’t even the emperor order someone to bring one back?","└ I’m more curious about how the Magic Tower will react.","└ Why the Magic Tower?","└ They control the mandrake monopoly. They’re probably watching this more closely than anyone.","└ Come on. Would they really make a big deal over something this small?","└ Don’t you remember the incident with the head moderator from two terms ago?","└ What happened?","Someone from another territory made a secret agreement with the Dwat Territory and began sending goods there without tariffs. That nearly drove the other territory into bankruptcy.","└ But Grylls doesn’t have enough supply, does he?","└ The Magic Tower lacks supply too, if you look at it that way. They don’t cultivate mandrakes. They only manage them.","└ So they have to obtain them from elsewhere too?","└ I heard they have enormous authority and monopoly rights, so their abuse of power is pretty severe.","└ Then from the Magic Tower’s perspective, Grylls must be rather inconvenient.","The atmosphere was beginning to take a strange turn."]},{"title":"Chapter 19","paragraphs":["Health (4)","As ridiculous as it sounded, even the highest levels of society kept a close eye on the gallery.","It was useful for gathering intelligence, monitoring leaks, assessing the political climate, and even observing daily life in foreign countries.","The gallery was filled mostly with nonsense posts, but every so often, something incredibly valuable could be found there.","More importantly, it was one of the few places where those in power could gauge public opinion .","Given the era, accurately understanding public sentiment was nearly impossible, making the gallery their only real window into it.","Of course, relying solely on the gallery had its drawbacks.","There had been many occasions when people in power trusted gallery opinion too much, only for protests and rebellions to erupt in the opposite direction.","Since then, they had learned to be wary of the \"loud minority\" and to separate useful information from noise.","Even so, no one could deny the gallery’s influence.","After all, everyone used it—young and old, nobles and commoners alike.","One famous story involved a noble who constantly criticized the gallery, only to be exposed as a hardcore gallery addict himself.","Status did not erase human desires.","If anything, those who had to maintain an elegant public image often vented their stress in the gallery instead.","That was why the upper class went to great lengths to hide the fact that they used it.","Even when caught, they usually insisted they only lurked without posting.","Almost nobody believed that excuse, but personal privacy was still respected.","As a result, there was an unspoken rule among nobles:","Never bring up the gallery.","Unless you were speaking privately with someone you trusted.","\"Your Highness, we cannot simply ignore this matter.\"","\"I know that. But that man is living on borrowed time. Isn’t this a bit too hasty?\"","The man speaking wore golden hair and blue eyes.","With his handsome features and well-built physique, he lacked for nothing in appearance.","Yet even he sounded reluctant.","Across from him, a middle-aged man with graying hair answered in an urgent tone.","\"That is precisely why we must secure as many mature mandrakes as possible before he dies.\"","\"Count Gorgon. I thought you were usually the cautious one.\"","\"There are times when decisive action must be taken.\"","The blond prince fell silent, considering the advice of his loyal retainer, Count Gorgon.","He was Arnold Louis Messiah, the future Emperor of the Messiah Empire.","With the current emperor bedridden due to chronic illness and overwork, Arnold was serving as acting emperor.","\"If we can establish trade with him, we can greatly weaken the Magic Tower’s influence. We could even pressure the Kingdom of Iris.\"","\"That’s an awfully optimistic scenario. The elves have been behaving unpredictably lately. We have no reason to provoke the Magic Tower as well.\"","\"But, Your Highness...\"","\"Enough. I have no desire to discuss someone who may die tomorrow.\"","\"If we supported him, wouldn’t that change the situation?\"","Count Gorgon refused to give up.","Though unusually stubborn, Arnold did not rebuke him.","Count Gorgon was famous for his remarkable foresight.","It was almost amusing to see someone like him influenced by rumors from the gallery.","That alone showed how much influence the gallery truly wielded.","\"If we support him, he may survive longer. But let me ask you something. Who exactly will handle this matter?\"","\"I know someone.\"","\"Not you?\"","\"...\"","Arnold’s blunt question immediately silenced Count Gorgon.","The count merely blinked in surprise.","Arnold chuckled to himself before waving a dismissive hand.","\"So you planned to take advantage of the gallery’s anonymity. You’re rushing this. That will be all.\"","\"Your Highness...\"","\"If you insist, I’ll leave it to your discretion. Just don’t complain when everyone assumes you’re the one buying mature mandrakes in bulk.\"","\"...\"","\"You haven’t been insulting me on the gallery, have you?\"","\"Absolutely not.\"","Yeah, right.","Arnold didn’t believe him for a second.","People cursed even their king whenever no one was listening.","The gallery was obviously no exception.","He himself had been showered with insults more than once simply because of unpopular policies.","\"It’s only been three days since this Grylls fellow entered the Forest of Four Seasons. Be patient.\"","\"...Understood. I may have been too hasty.\"","\"Good. Now go. I have work to attend to.\"","At Arnold’s dismissal, Count Gorgon quietly left the room.","Soon, Arnold was alone.","Leaning back in his chair, he stared thoughtfully at the ceiling.","It’s not as though I’m unconcerned either...","His gaze drifted toward the gallery.","At the moment, it was ablaze with rumors.","The spark had been Passing Dwarf’s photo of the mature mandrake.","Although Grylls had gifted mandrakes to those who had helped him, none of them had posted proof.","There was no reason to.","Doing so only risked revealing their identities.","As a result, many people had remained skeptical.","But Passing Dwarf’s post convinced them.","To make matters even worse, Grylls had previously uploaded a picture of an entire colony of mature mandrakes.","Anyone following the gallery naturally reached the same conclusion.","If you help Grylls, you’ll receive a mature mandrake.","This realization had spread within only a few hours after Grylls went to sleep.","***","Title: There Are Way Too Many Similar Posts for This to Be Just a Rumor","My friend serves in the Imperial Guard, and the Emperor supposedly ordered them to bring back a mature mandrake lol.","└ Seriously?","└ Yeah. The rumor’s already spread everywhere.","└ They’re probably holding meetings about it by now.","└ Come on. There’s no way that’s real.","Arnold smirked as he read the thread.","It sounded absurd.","Yet it was difficult to dismiss outright.","Count Gorgon himself had just pleaded the exact same case.","If even someone as cautious as Gorgon felt that way, many other nobles were probably thinking the same thing.","They would all try to establish trade with Grylls and earn his favor.","***","Title: Has the Magic Tower Said Anything Yet?","The Magic Tower monopolizes mandrakes. Haven’t they reacted?","└ Not yet, but they probably will soon.","└ Isn’t the Magic Tower in the Kingdom of Iris?","└ Could this end up causing conflict with the Empire?","└ Over one mandrake? Seriously?","└ Maybe not a war, but they’re bound to say something. Besides, I doubt the Magic Tower likes this situation.","└ Why not?","└ Because they have a monopoly.","***","Title: Current Situation Summary","Mandrakes are extremely rare and are essential ingredients for elixirs.The Magic Tower has traditionally managed all known mandrakes.Their monopoly generates unimaginable profits.Grylls has discovered not only mature mandrakes, but an entire colony of them.A single mature specimen is enough to make a top-tier elixir.Rather than accepting unfavorable deals with the Magic Tower, it would be far better to buy directly from Grylls.","└ Sure, but Grylls can’t keep supplying them forever. Once he harvests them all, that’s it.","└ The same applies to the Magic Tower. They don’t cultivate mandrakes—they only manage existing ones.","└ So they source them from the wild too?","└ Exactly. Their job is preserving mandrakes so they’re always healthy enough to be turned into elixirs.","└ And they built a monopoly around that? What a bunch of crooks, lol.","└ One more thing: Grylls is in the Forest of Four Seasons, so no one’s in a position to pressure him.","└ I can’t believe this is actually happening. Damn...","If someone could establish trade with Grylls and secure a steady supply of mature mandrakes, the rewards would be immeasurable.","The problem was Grylls himself.","He was far too unstable.","Living inside the Forest of Four Seasons meant he could die at any moment.","And it isn’t something money can solve...","What Grylls needed was not wealth.","He needed supplies to survive.","Since he had recently received a fortune from the regular known as Allfather, money was probably no longer a priority for him.","That meant bartering was the only viable option.","And that, too, made the situation unpredictable.","For now... it’s better to simply watch and wait.","It would be the worst of both worlds if they acted rashly.","If even one factor had been stable, it might have been worth considering, but everything about the situation was uncertain, making it difficult to commit.","Still, obtaining even a single one would be worthwhile...","If it were for personal reasons rather than official business, that was another matter entirely.","They see one thing but miss another.","Arnold shook his head.","With the Emperor’s health declining rapidly, the temptation was unavoidable.","Even the Imperial Palace’s budget struggled to afford a top-grade elixir.","If a mature mandrake could restore the Emperor’s health, Arnold’s position would become unshakable.","It wasn’t as though his siblings were competing for the throne.","Arnold had two younger brothers and two younger sisters.","One might expect at least one of them to covet the crown, but surprisingly, none of them did.","I suppose I’ve been fortunate...","His second brother was deeply interested in culture and had become the Minister of Culture.","His third brother was devoutly religious and had entered the clergy. According to rumor, he had become a Holy Knight.","As for his two younger sisters, they both married into noble families, naturally removing themselves from the line of succession.","It would be far better if Father handed me the crown himself than merely approved my succession.","Unless the Emperor personally passed on the throne, there would always be those looking for excuses to question Arnold’s legitimacy.","To prevent that from happening, he needed at least one mature mandrake.","Even so, Arnold hesitated.","It wasn’t because approaching Grylls made him uneasy.","With a sigh, he looked at his gallery username.","A name he had created in his youth, unable to restrain his childish impulses.","[UltimateZZoneArnoldRocks]","\"...Sigh.\"","It was embarrassing just to look at.","Why had he ever chosen a name like that?","He should have stayed anonymous from the very beginning.","No matter how many times he thought about it, he could not understand his younger self.","Fortunately, no one knew the truth.","If anyone ever found out, he would have abandoned his position as Crown Prince and fled long ago.","Can’t I at least change my username?","The gallery was a civilization far ahead of its time, but it was not perfect.","Over countless revisions, numerous conveniences had been added.","Changing your username, however, remained impossible.","Was there a way to become anonymous again?","There was exactly one.","Completely expel every trace of mana from your body and refill it with new mana.","It was essentially the same as completely replacing your body.","Even someone who underwent Reforging the Bones and Cleansing the Marrow couldn’t accomplish such a feat.","Once a username was registered, it was yours for life.","If I obtain a mature mandrake or help Father recover... people will inevitably figure it out.","And once that happened, his username would naturally be exposed.","He didn’t even want to imagine it.","Nor could he simply wait.","Managing mature mandrakes was extremely difficult.","There was a reason the Magic Tower had taken responsibility for preserving them.","At least he had deleted all of his old posts.","If the gallery hadn’t allowed users to delete their own posts, they would have remained as permanent black history.","Should I make my brother do it instead...?","Arnold folded his arms and pondered.","His second brother might officially be the Minister of Culture, but in reality he spent most of his time loafing around.","Whenever he had free time, he went to watch soccer or baseball.","He claimed it was far better than taking on a position that involved nothing but hard work.","For now, it’d be best to keep watching the gallery... and see who ends up with the mature mandrakes.","At the moment, that seemed like the wisest course of action.","Only three days had passed.","It was too early to make a fuss.","As Arnold browsed the gallery, he thoughtfully stroked his chin.","Still, I should at least familiarize myself with the culture.","The easiest way to do that would be by making a post.","Although his username embarrassed him, asking a simple question couldn’t hurt.","***","Title: Hello. Nice to meet you.","UltimateZZoneArnoldRocks","I’m new to the gallery. How does this place usually work?","└ Newbie?","└ UltimateZZoneArnoldRocks: Yes, I am.","└ Then stop using polite speech, dumbass.","└ You’re a newbie and you’re using honorifics?","└ Look at that username, lol.","Arnold’s eyes filled with confusion.","\"...Ugh...\"","I stretched, working the stiffness out of my body.","Thanks to the mat and pillow I’d bought at the auction house, I didn’t wake up sore all over.","I should’ve bought them sooner.","At least I realized it before it was too late.","The gallery...? What the...? Why are there so many trade requests?","My eyes widened.","A surprisingly large number of trade requests had arrived while I was asleep.","Once you logged out of the gallery, you received no notifications whatsoever.","That was great for getting a good night’s sleep, but it still left me puzzled.","Most of these are from regulars I don’t even know. Are they all asking for mature mandrakes?","That seemed likely.","Passing Dwarf had uploaded his post yesterday.","Even a single mature mandrake was worth an enormous amount.","If someone could genuinely help me survive, I was willing to trade.","One at a time.","Not in bulk.","My own survival came first.","There was no point supplying everyone else if it cost me my life.","[A Typical Gallery Initiation][118]","\"Hm?\"","One particular post caught my attention.","Not only were there a mountain of comments, it had an impressive number of upvotes as well.","What happened while I was sleeping?","I guess all the entertaining things really did happen while you were asleep.","[I’m the Crown Prince, you bastards.]","[What is wrong with you people?]","[Seriously.]","[I didn’t even do anything wrong.]","[Why is everyone insulting me?]","[No, listen to me first.]","[Is this really normal here?]","[This gallery is pretty rough.]","[Hello. Nice to meet you.]","Read from the bottom up.","***","Title: A Typical Gallery Initiation","[Welcome back, buddy.]","└ Talk about adapting fast, lol.","└ What’s with that username?","└ Looks like another old-timer wandered into the gallery.","└ Sounds like something my dad would come up with.","└ If your username has words like \"Ultimate,\" \"Zone,\" or \"Rocks\" in it, you’re probably old.","└ These days, some people actually choose names like that on purpose.","It was just another peaceful day in the gallery."]},{"title":"Chapter 20","paragraphs":["Owlbear (1)","Title: A Bright and Energetic Morning!","(Photo of a raised thumb)","If anyone asks who I am, tell them I’m Grylls!","└ Heavenly Demon: You’re awake. Did anything happen during the night?","└ Wild Grylls: No. I slept like a log. Did you sleep well, Heavenly Demon?","└ Heavenly Demon: Given my cultivation level, I have no need for sleep.","└ Wild Grylls: Ah. Right.","Even if something interesting happened while I was asleep, what I had to do remained the same.","Report that I was still alive.","It was a post announcing the beginning of another day.","The Heavenly Demon and the other familiar regulars each left greetings.","Quite a few anonymous users commented as well.","└ Grylls, did you see the posts from dawn?","└ Wild Grylls: What posts?","└ The ones saying they wanted to buy mature mandrakes from you. There were tons of them.","└ Wild Grylls: Oh, I saw those. I got a lot of trade requests too.","└ Are you going to sell them?","I wasn’t sure.","As I had already said, I didn’t have that kind of leeway.","I wasn’t short on money, nor was there anything I urgently needed.","I could buy most things through the auction house.","The people I had traded with so far had helped me out of pure goodwill, so I had gladly returned the favor.","[User XXX has requested a trade.]","[User @@@ has requested a trade.]","[User ○○ has requested a trade.]","Before long, even more requests flooded in.","I stared at them for a moment, then searched the usernames.","Most of the accounts had never made a post, and many had been created only recently.","They were probably trying to obtain mature mandrakes from me.","First, reject them all.","Then I needed to make a post.","If I simply ignored them, they might become even more annoying later.","I also wanted the head moderator to see what was happening.","***","Title: To Everyone Who Sent Me Trade Requests","Wild Grylls","I assume you’re after mature mandrakes, but I have no intention of trading them right now.","Given my current situation, I can’t afford to act carelessly, and I have no idea what you intend to offer.","So instead, make a post explaining what you want to trade.","I’ll look through them and send trade requests myself if anything interests me.","Also, please don’t ask for regular shipments.","I could die tomorrow.","└ Wait, so the rumors were true?","└ The mature mandrakes were real, so I guess it makes sense.","└ \"I could die tomorrow,\" hahaha.","└ At least he has an accurate view of his situation, lol.","└ Everyone will understand if he puts it like that.","└ PraisetheSun: If anyone tries to buy one with money, tell me. I’ll pay more than them, lol.","└ Damn, he’s rich.","└ Look at that confidence, hahaha.","└ Rich Dark Elf bro is built different.","└ Don’t Abandon the Hero: Hmm! I think I understand what’s happening! I’ll keep an eye on things!","└ Wild Grylls: Thank you. Do you need a mandrake too, Head Mod?","└ Don’t Abandon the Hero: Huh?! I haven’t done anything to help you!","└ Wild Grylls: A bribe, lol.","└ Don’t Abandon the Hero: Absolutely not!","└ He just openly called it a bribe, hahaha.","Now that the situation was more or less settled, I began my daily routine.","First, I sat cross-legged to improve my flexibility.","Three days ago, it had felt as though my entire body were being twisted apart.","Now, it was slowly becoming bearable.","I should be able to learn from the Heavenly Demon soon.","An internal cultivation method—or perhaps a mana cultivation technique.","If I could learn one, it would surely improve my condition.","The Heavenly Demon wouldn’t teach me anything dangerous.","It should make chopping wood and digging easier too, right?","The most important task at the moment was reinforcing my shelter.","I wanted to cut trees with the Heavenly Demon’s sword instead of an axe.","But if I damaged the blade, I would be in serious trouble, so I had no choice but to use the axe.","The same went for the shovel.","Every task here involved backbreaking labor.","There aren’t any interesting posts either.","Nothing particularly noteworthy had appeared since I made my post.","As usual, I ate a Bigu Pill for breakfast.","I’ll dig traps today.","After deciding to adapt to life in the Forest of Four Seasons, my routine had become simple.","In the morning and afternoon, I either explored the surroundings or repaired the shelter.","Yesterday had mostly been spent exploring because of the mature mandrake incident.","Today was for repairs.","Though \"repairs\" consisted of little more than chopping nearby trees and digging holes.","Ten minutes of either was enough to make my whole body ache, but it was necessary for my safety.","Maybe I’m lucky. I haven’t seen any sign of the owlbear.","Every time I heard something rustle, I flinched, but nothing happened.","This place was far from where the owlbear had appeared before, but I still couldn’t let my guard down.","According to the gallery, owlbears were extremely territorial.","Anything that entered their territory—beast or human—would be torn apart.","Considering that they were as large as houses, encountering one would almost certainly mean death.","Unless I can lure it back to the cave.","I stopped digging and looked toward the cave entrance.","It was just large enough for Mad Dog to pass through.","An owlbear the size of a small mountain would never fit inside easily.","With the trap I had laid near the entrance, I might even be able to kill it if I was lucky.","It would be better to know the limits of its territory first, though.","I continued digging until I checked the depth of the pit.","This should be deep enough.","Now all that remained was camouflage.","Why didn’t I place sharpened stakes or weapons at the bottom?","Because I might fall into it myself.","This wasn’t some trap far from camp.","It was directly in front of the cave and meant to serve as a final line of defense.","There should be something in the auction house I can use instead of a tarp...","I bought a piece of cloth to cover the top.","Then I stretched it tightly across the pit, held the edges down with stones, and covered it with dirt.","With that, one trap was complete.","A sense of satisfaction welled up inside me.","Why am I so proud of something like this?","A moment later, I sighed at my own situation.","It was too early to celebrate after finishing only one task.","The hardest work—logging—still remained.","Just thinking about it made the future look bleak.","Rustle—","Then I heard bushes moving nearby.","I flinched and instinctively hunched over.","Turning toward the source of the sound, I watched carefully.","\"...\"","Had I imagined it?","Nothing happened, no matter how long I stared at the bushes.","I let out a relieved sigh and entered the cave.","Naturally, I jumped over the trap before going inside.","Maybe I should put down a plank.","Having to jump over it every time could cause an accident in an emergency.","This was how I would slowly learn through trial and error.","I slung the logging axe over my shoulder and went back outside.","I have a whole new respect for lumberjacks.","How had people cut down so many trees in an age without chainsaws?","They had even used the timber to build wooden houses and ships.","Every day, I gained a greater appreciation for civilization.","That feeling would probably only grow stronger as time passed.","Could I ask the dwarf to make me a chainsaw?","The pointless thought crossed my mind, but I quickly dismissed it.","He had been drinking yesterday, so he was probably suffering from a hangover by now.","Besides, I was more curious about the Starlight Princess’s condition than the dwarf’s.","Thud! Thump!","I started with the tree I had left unfinished yesterday.","It was too thick to saw through easily.","Still, no tree could withstand being struck forever.","If I kept chopping, it would eventually fall.","I should make it fall toward the cave.","To do that, I also needed to cut into the opposite side.","After catching my breath, I walked around the tree.","Rustle—","Once again, the sound of moving grass reached my ears.","This time, there was no mistaking it.","I tensed and slowly turned around.","Rustle. Rustle.","It wasn’t my imagination.","The bushes were definitely moving.","The sound was also growing louder.","Something was approaching.","I slowly backed away, preparing to flee into the cave at any moment.","Push—","At last, the source of the sound crawled out from the dense undergrowth.","The instant I saw its face, my breath caught.","Sharp, vicious golden eyes.","A savage beak unique to a bird of prey.","And finally, a body as large as a house.","\"Grr?\"","It was an owlbear.","My body stiffened from the tension.","Fortunately, it did not attack immediately.","Perhaps this was its first time seeing a human in the Forest of Four Seasons.","It seemed to be observing me first.","I slowly stepped backward.","\"Grrrr...\"","\"Haa...\"","I glanced behind me, estimating the distance to the cave.","If I provoked it unnecessarily, I wouldn’t merely get hurt.","I would die.","Fortunately, the owlbear was so enormous that it probably couldn’t enter the cave.","I need something to distract it...","I searched my pocket and felt something round.","It was a Bigu Pill I had kept as emergency food.","Maybe I could use it to draw the creature’s attention.","Carefully, I tossed the pill onto the ground near the owlbear.","\"Sniff. Sniff.\"","\"...\"","The owlbear began smelling the pill.","Taking advantage of the distraction, I managed to reach the area near the cave entrance.","Apparently deciding that the scent was harmless, the owlbear picked up the Bigu Pill in its beak.","It spent a moment savoring the taste.","Then—","\"Kuegh! Kueeegh! Screeeech!\"","It let out a hideous shriek at the Bigu Pill’s distinctive bitterness.","The instant I heard that scream, I realized one thing.","If I didn’t get inside the cave immediately, I would be torn limb from limb.","\"Couldn’t you tell from the smell?! I thought bears had good noses!\"","As I ran, I felt a terrifying pressure behind me.","Was this what killing intent felt like?","My knees nearly gave out.","Tap!","Remembering the trap near the cave entrance, I dove over it.","My legs and knees would probably be badly scraped, but that was better than dying.","Boom!","\"Screeeeeech!\"","A tremendous impact sounded behind me.","The owlbear’s furious roar followed.","I hurriedly pushed myself up as every hair on my body stood on end.","\"Huff... Huff...\"","\"Screeeech! Screech!\"","Scrape! Scratch!","The owlbear’s razor-sharp claws tore at the ground. I watched it while gasping for breath.","Half of its enormous body had made it through.","In other words, it was stuck.","If the cave entrance had been even slightly larger, it probably would have squeezed through.","On top of that, thanks to the trap, its short bear-like legs couldn’t seem to reach the ground.","Th-This is my chance.","I didn’t have time to stand around watching.","Instead of the axe, I immediately grabbed another weapon.","The crossbow I had received from Passing Dwarf.","I loaded it with an ordinary bolt rather than a harpoon.","Even a normal bolt should be effective enough since it was dwarf-made.","Twang! Thud!","There was no need to aim precisely.","I simply fired, and the bolt struck its face.","\"Screeeeeech!\"","The owlbear thrashed violently as the bolt buried itself in its eye.","Just how strong was this thing for its movements to shake the entire cave?","My brief relief vanished when I saw the cave entrance slowly beginning to crumble under the owlbear’s monstrous strength.","I’m screwed...!","The moment the entrance collapsed, my life would be over.","Thud! Thunk! Smack!","Without hesitation, I fired the crossbow again and again.","The more bolts lodged in its face, the more violently the owlbear rampaged.","It showed no sign of calming down.","Does this bastard not have a brain?","I fired not only ordinary bolts but also the tethered harpoon.","The final harpoon struck its remaining eye.","With that, the owlbear lost its sight completely.","However, it was thrashing so wildly that approaching it was still impossible.","A spear! Right, I should buy a spear!","I hurriedly connected to the gallery and purchased a spear from the auction house.","I didn’t bother checking reviews or comparing prices.","As long as it was a spear, that was enough.","I stared at the still-rampaging owlbear and gripped the weapon with both hands.","\"Hraaah!\"","Stab!","Then I drove the spear into the owlbear’s head.","Perhaps I was lucky, because the spearhead struck the exact center of its forehead.","Before the owlbear could thrash even more violently, I pressed down with all my strength.","\"Keeeeeegh!\"","Crack!","But a spear was still a spear.","The spearhead might have been metal, but the shaft was wooden.","The owlbear’s swinging claw snapped it in half.","I nearly lost my balance, but managed to steady myself at the last second.","Rumble!","\"W-Whoa?\"","Then the thing I had feared finally happened.","The cave entrance almost completely collapsed.","While I stood there in shock, the owlbear forced its way inside.","I’m screwed.","I’m really screwed.","Even as the thought crossed my mind, I grabbed the Heavenly Demon’s sword and the Golden Shield.","The worst-case scenario had arrived, but the owlbear was already close to death.","If I waited for the right opportunity, I still had a chance.","\"Screeeeeech!\"","Boom!","With bolts and a spearhead embedded in its face, the owlbear charged straight at me.","Startled, I hurriedly raised the shield to protect myself.","SwordMaster’s post flashed through my mind, allowing me to brace in time.","Crash!","\"Kgh!\"","Even with the shield, there was no way I could completely stop an owlbear’s charge.","The difference in weight was too great.","I was a frail human, while the owlbear was still a bear.","Thud!","My feet left the ground, and I was sent flying.","Fortunately, I merely landed on the floor rather than crashing into the cave wall.","But it was too early to feel relieved.","I never took my eyes off the owlbear.","\"Screeeeeech!\"","It charged at me while I was still lying on the ground.","Even without its sight, it could probably estimate my location by sound.","That meant its attacks would be less accurate.","I focused until the very end.","...Left paw!","The owlbear raised its left foreleg.","All that remained was to determine where it intended to strike.","I opened my eyes wide and watched its attack.","The raised paw came down directly toward my left shoulder.","Bang!","I twisted my body just enough to avoid it.","Still, the deafening impact right beside my ear left me with a slight ringing sensation.","I already suffered from tinnitus, so I didn’t pay much attention to it.","What mattered was the counterattack that followed.","\"Uaaaaah!\"","With a shout, I thrust the Heavenly Demon’s sword toward the owlbear’s jaw.","I desperately hoped this would be the final attack.","Stab!","As expected of the Heavenly Demon’s sword.","It pierced through the owlbear’s jaw and drove all the way into its skull.","The moment its brain was struck, the owlbear merely convulsed.","It could no longer struggle.","Its brain had been destroyed so thoroughly that its body could no longer receive signals.","Boom!","\"Urgh!\"","The owlbear’s enormous body collapsed on top of me.","It was absurdly heavy.","Groaning and straining, I crawled out from beneath it.","As I did, I finally noticed the condition of my legs.","They’re completely scraped raw.","It was probably because of that desperate dive earlier.","Both knees had been badly torn up.","Calling them mere scrapes didn’t do the injuries justice.","The flesh had been peeled away so deeply that the muscle was nearly visible.","If the wounds had been even slightly deeper, I might have seen something white beneath them.","\"Ow... Ow...\"","As the adrenaline slowly faded, pain spread through my entire body.","That single dive had left wounds not only on my knees but all over me.","If I hadn’t been wearing clothes, my upper body would probably have been badly injured as well.","First, an elixir... Right. I don’t have one.","I would have to buy a potion.","Normally, I would have traded with the Starlight Princess for an elixir.","But she still hadn’t made a survival post.","The cooldown on trade requests hadn’t expired either, so I couldn’t contact her.","Drip—","\"Ugh...\"","I bought a reasonably priced potion from the auction house and poured it over my wounds.","True to the classic image of a potion, it was bright red.","At the very least, I could expect it to disinfect the injuries.","Afterward, I wrapped strips of cloth I had purchased separately around the wounds like bandages.","Since I was injured in so many places, I ended up wrapping cloth around each of my arms and legs.","Now all that remains is dealing with the owlbear.","Countless bolts were embedded in its face.","A bolt and a harpoon protruded from its eyes in particular.","Looking at the corpse alone made it seem a little pitiful, but it had tried to kill me.","***","Title: I Killed an Owlbear","Wild Grylls","(Photo of the owlbear’s corpse)","I seriously thought I was going to die fighting it ;;","I’ll put it up on the auction house soon, so do whatever you want.","└ Whoa. How did you kill it?","└ Wild Grylls: The cave entrance was narrow, so I lured it there. Then I wrecked its face with a crossbow.","└ Hahahaha, look at its face. It has a bolt and a harpoon where its eyes should be.","└ Are you really an ordinary person?","└ He killed an owlbear and still calls himself ordinary. Damn.","└ Heavenly Demon: Were you injured?","└ Wild Grylls: Other than a lot of scraped wounds, I’m fine.","└ Heavenly Demon: That is fortunate. Whenever I see posts like this, I feel that your basic combat ability is remarkably good. Am I mistaken?","└ Wild Grylls: I wouldn’t have been able to finish it off without the sword you gave me.","└ Heavenly Demon: Hearing that pleases me. Is there any weapon you require?","A weapon I needed.","I definitely thought having a proper spear would be useful.","Still, I had no intention of asking the Heavenly Demon for one.","As I had said many times before, depending too heavily on someone else was never a good idea.","└ Wild Grylls: Not yet. Oh! I’m getting used to sitting cross-legged now. Could you teach me an internal cultivation method?","└ Heavenly Demon: That is wonderful news. I have been organizing one in a way that will be easy for you to understand.","└ Wild Grylls: Thank you.","└ SwordMaster: That was impressive. You said you lured it to the cave entrance, correct?","└ Wild Grylls: Yes.","└ SwordMaster: You seem surprisingly quick-witted.","└ Wild Grylls: Haha, thank you.","└ SwordMaster: Someday, you’ll be able to face one head-on in a fair one-on-one fight.","└ Wild Grylls: Is there a method for fighting owlbears?","└ SwordMaster: They’re quite easy. Their claws are their main weapon, so you simply cut off their legs. When they raise a foreleg to strike, sever it as it comes down. Easy, right?","└ Wild Grylls: ;;;","It was probably easy only by her standards.","How could an ordinary person possibly understand a genius?","After scrolling through the gallery’s reactions, I dealt with the owlbear first.","The moment I listed the corpse on the auction house, it vanished.","Bidding began immediately.","The auction period was twenty-four hours.","I wonder if it’ll sell for a lot.","I had no idea.","What I needed now was rest.","Before that, though, I had to inspect the trap.","The owlbear had damaged it, so repairs were essential.","\"Hm?\"","\"...\"","But the moment I stepped outside the cave, I came face-to-face with something strange.","Bright, round golden eyes.","A bird-like beak.","A body about the size of a medium-sized dog and a face overflowing with curiosity.","\"Kyuu?\"","A baby owlbear stood before me, tilting its head."]},{"title":"Chapter 21","paragraphs":["Owlbear (2)","Every animal is cute when it’s young.","People even say that their cuteness is what earns them mercy from predators and helps them survive.","No matter how fierce the species, most animals are irresistibly adorable as babies.","\"Kyuu?\"","Just like the baby owlbear standing in front of me.","All it did was tilt its head, yet it dealt a critical hit straight to my heart.","If I had to describe the baby owlbear...","It looked like a fluffy ball of fur staring at me with wide, round eyes.","The adult owlbear had a face that was terrifying beyond words, but this little one’s face was incredibly gentle.","Still, this was the wilderness. Even an owlbear cub would have a hard time surviving here alone.","So what should I do?","\"Here, here. Come on.\"","\"Kyuu.\"","What else?","Pet it, of course.","I beckoned with my fingers, and the baby owlbear tilted its head before cautiously waddling over.","It pressed its nose against my hand and began sniffing it, acting on pure instinct.","While it was busy smelling me, I slowly raised my other hand.","Pat... pat...","\"Kyung?\"","The one thing four-legged animals could never do for themselves—","Having someone gently stroke their head.","The baby owlbear blinked in surprise at the unfamiliar sensation and looked up at me with wide eyes.","Its huge round owl-like eyes...","The little tufts of feathers sticking up from its head...","How could something this adorable even exist?","It was only about the size of a medium-sized dog, so it wasn’t particularly intimidating.","\"Grrr... rrr...\"","Apparently my petting felt good.","The baby owlbear closed its eyes and let out a strange, contented rumble.","While continuing to rub its head, I quietly opened the Gallery.","***","Title: Found a Baby Owlbear","Wild Grylls","(Photo of the baby owlbear.)","(Another photo of the baby owlbear.)","(Video of me petting the baby owlbear.)","(Video of the baby owlbear smiling.)","Killed its mom, then found this little guy. Seriously adorable.","LOL it’s so cute.","Look at that fluffy fur.","└ Completely different from the adults.","Wait... you killed the mother of something this cute? You’re evil.","The Orphan Maker strikes again.","LMAO Orphan Maker.","Wild Grylls: Excuse me?","The moderator’s authority is unstoppable.","Tyranny!","LOL.","Can I post my face too? I’m cute.","Don’tAbandonTheHero: Posts that cause psychological damage will be banned!","Look how serious they are. LOL.","?","PrincessChaenggu: What the hell? If you’ve got a problem, fight me.","Heavenly Demon: Sacrilegious. I feel like hugging it until it bursts.","Don’tAbandonTheHero: Three-hour ban.","Wild Grylls: ??? Wait, why?","Don’tAbandonTheHero: Cute things require at least ten photos and three videos.","Wild Grylls: That was a rule?","Don’tAbandonTheHero: I just made it.","Grylls, you’re an orphan too. Did you really have to make another one?","Wild Grylls: Its mom was trying to kill me. I wanted to live too.","Fair enough. Survival comes first. LOL.","Heavenly Demon: It truly is adorable. I’d like to hold that little ball of fluff at least once.","└ PrincessChaenggu: I know, right? Just like me.","...Heavenly Demon?","?","Most of the comments were filled with praise for the baby owlbear.","Honestly, anyone’s heart would melt at the sight of such a fluffy little creature.","But the wilderness was always cruel.","One particular comment caught my eye.","Who cares if it’s cute? You’ll have to kill it eventually anyway.","Why would you kill something this adorable?","Boo! Trash!","No, seriously. If you don’t kill it, are you going to raise it? The moment it gets hungry it’ll eat Grylls first.","I heard about this. A noble who raised an owlbear went on vacation and got eaten when he came back.","You can even raise one?","As long as you keep it well-fed, its loyalty is incredible. Stop feeding it, and you become the meal.","Besides, this is the wild. How are you supposed to raise it out here?","Do you really have to kill it? It’s so cute.","Judging by its size, it looks like it was just born.","After reading those comments, I looked down at the owlbear.","It was happily rubbing its face against my hand.","Just watching it made all the gloom in my heart melt away...","But a wild animal was still a wild animal.","Especially an owlbear.","Apparently they were notorious for their enormous appetites.","They even ate their own owners on a regular basis.","\"Kyuu... Kyuu...\"","This little guy?","I looked at it with a heavy heart.","To be rational, the safest option would be to kill it myself.","Some people might ask why I couldn’t just raise it...","But I was barely surviving as it was.","Even wealthy nobles struggled to keep one.","How was I supposed to?","’And it’s not like you can easily buy food for something like this at the auction.’","If it were that easy, I would’ve bought it long ago.","It was a shame, but there was no helping it.","Still...","Killing it left a bad taste in my mouth.","It would be better to release it back into the wild.","I made up my mind.","Wild Grylls: I’ll just let it return to the wild. I’m barely feeding myself as it is.","So you have no sense of responsibility?","Wild Grylls: Its mom tried to kill me. What responsibility?","...Fair point.","Fastest agreement ever. LOL.","Just buy meat at the auction. Aren’t you rich now, Grylls?","Wild Grylls: If it were that simple, I’d have bought meat for myself already.","Come on, you’ve got money. Can’t even feed one baby?","Wild Grylls: Why should I raise it? I’m trying to save money in case something happens.","How much money do you even have?","Let’s see...","After getting paid so generously by Allfather, I did have a comfortable amount of money.","But raising an animal cost a fortune.","Especially not a dog or cat—","A bear .","Even if it was still a cub, its appetite would only get worse.","Wild Grylls: I do have money, but spending it on this is...","Are you an idiot? Just keep the owlbear as your bodyguard.","Wild Grylls: What are you talking about?","You know how strong adult owlbears are. Once it grows up, nothing beats having one beside you. Treat it like your personal knight.","...That’s actually convincing.","Not gonna lie, that’s a really good idea.","Yeah, raising it sounds better.","The argument was surprisingly persuasive.","I looked at the baby owlbear.","This adorable little puffball would eventually grow into that terrifying monster.","And as long as I kept it well-fed, it would supposedly be fiercely loyal.","...It would be nice to have company, too.","The Gallery was nice, but it wasn’t the same as interacting with a living creature.","The baby owlbear stared back at me with curious eyes.","Maybe...","Keeping it as a companion wasn’t such a bad idea after all.","If I ever ran short on money, I could always sell a mandrake or hunt more golden poison frogs.","’But... what does this thing eat?’","Bears were omnivores that would even eat carrion.","But this wasn’t an ordinary bear.","It was an owlbear.","To find out what it liked to eat, I made another post.","***","Title: What Do Owlbears Eat?","Wild Grylls","Pretty much anything.","Yeah, same as the comment above. Their diet’s basically identical to a regular bear’s.","Wild Grylls: Do they like honey?","They absolutely love it. LOL.","Perfect.","Then I’d test it myself.","I opened the auction house and searched for honey.","Just to be safe, I carefully read the reviews.","Apparently the seller’s family had been running an apiary for three generations.","Their proof was... something else.","How do we even know that’s real honey?","(Photo of the seller’s face swollen from countless bee stings.)","...Alright. I’ll buy two jars.","Now that’s convincing proof. LOL.","Something like that.","Thanks to those reviews, I bought it without hesitation.","After purchasing the honey, I also bought a large wooden spoon.","I scooped up a spoonful of honey and held it out to the baby owlbear.","\"Kyuu?\"","\"Go on. It’s delicious.\"","\"Sniff... sniff...\"","The little owlbear hesitated, apparently seeing honey for the first time.","Watching the thick honey drip off the spoon felt almost wasteful.","Still, its keen sense of smell soon won over its caution.","Before long, it slowly opened its mouth wide.","\"Yum.\"","\"Is it good?\"","\"...\"","After taking a bite of the honey, the little creature froze for a moment.","\"Kyuuuuuu!\"","\"H-Huh?\"","\"Kyuaaaa!\"","It let out a bizarre cry and began devouring the honey in a frenzy.","Startled, I set the jar on the ground and backed away a couple of steps.","\"Chomp, chomp, chomp, chomp!\"","It sure knew how to make food look delicious.","It was also fascinating to see such a long tongue emerge from that short beak.","The baby owlbear was completely entranced by the sweetness of honey, something it had never tasted before.","I hadn’t even gotten a single bite.","Had I known this would happen, I would’ve tasted some first.","Anyway, it seemed to like it, so that was a relief. It would take a while to finish the whole jar.","’What should I name it?’","I had decided to raise it for the sake of my survival and mental well-being.","I’d never owned a pet before, but even I knew that choosing a name was important.","’It’s a fluffy ball of fur, so... Fluffy?’","Was that too lazy?","Still, no other name suited it better.","Asking the Gallery to name it seemed like a bad idea.","They would probably come up with all sorts of ridiculous names.","\"Fluffy.\"","\"Chomp, chomp, chomp!\"","\"Fluffy?\"","\"Chomp, chomp, chomp!\"","Was it ignoring me because it was too busy eating honey?","Well, I’d already decided on the name. I could slowly teach it to respond later.","Before that, I had to upload a picture.","How could I possibly keep something this cute to myself?","***","Title: Decided on a Name","Wild Grylls","(Photo of the baby owlbear eating honey.)","Its name is Fluffy because its fur is fluffy. Objections will not be accepted.","You really put zero effort into that name. LOL.","How is that any different from naming a dog Brownie? LOL.","LMAO.","Wild Grylls: Then you guys come up with something.","Heavenly Demon: Since it is a round ball of fur, how about Wonmo, meaning \"Round Fur\"?","Wild Grylls: Ma’am?","Of course the old-timer would suggest something like that. LOL.","It does roll off the tongue, though. Wonmo!","Your name is Wonmo from now on. LOL.","SwordMaster: Fluffy isn’t bad. It’s cute.","Wild Grylls: Can’t you think of anything else?","SwordMaster: Is it male or female?","Wild Grylls: Give me a second.","The moment I read that, I cautiously moved behind the owlbear.","Then I lowered my head and spotted two round balls.","It was unmistakably male.","There was no more reliable way to check.","Wild Grylls: Male.","SwordMaster: Alexander II. What do you think? Sounds cool, right?","Wild Grylls: ...","Isn’t that the name of a general?","Yeah, a famous general from Messiah. LOL.","If it were female, she’d have named it Alexandria. LMAO.","PrincessChaenggu: How about Naldo?","Who’s Naldo?","Some famous football player.","PrincessChaenggu: You caught me.","Caught you doing what? LOL.","Look at how shameless she is. LOL.","PraiseTheSun: Sultan VII. You can tell at a glance that he has the face of a king.","What part of that fat thing looks royal?","PraiseTheSun: Pigs have traditionally been considered one of the faces of royalty.","Really?","PraiseTheSun: Absolutely. I swear on my son.","Why are you betting your son on it? LOL.","Naturally, my opinion was ignored, and they started a vote without me.","See?","All kinds of bizarre combinations were already appearing.","It would be better to simply call him Fluffy than let the Gallery decide.","Unfortunately, the Gallery users had other plans.","There are too many names. We should settle it with a vote.","So the five choices are Fluffy, Wonmo, Alexander, Naldo, and Sultan?","Any more suggestions? If not, I’ll post the poll right away.","Shouldn’t Grylls be the one to post it?","No way. He’ll obviously rig it so Fluffy wins.","Wild Grylls: ??? I’m the owner! Why are you deciding this without me?","***","Title: Vote for the Baby Owlbear’s Name","Fluffy: 1%Wonmo: 39%Alexander: 21%Naldo: 19%Sultan: 20%","By the principle of majority rule, his name is officially Wonmo! Decision finalized!","This was absurd.","I was the one raising him, so why were they naming him however they pleased?","But who were the Gallery users?","A bunch of people who never listened to anyone else.","Heavenly Demon: Everyone has excellent taste. I am pleased.","SwordMaster: Why did Wonmo win? That name sounds so old-fashioned.","PrincessChaenggu: I refuse to accept this.","PraiseTheSun: What a shame. He truly has the face of a king.**","Wild Grylls: I keep telling you, he’s my pet. Why are you deciding his name?","Heavenly Demon: If you dislike it, then use whatever name you desire. This lady shall respect your decision.","You can feel the disappointment radiating from that comment.","Grylls, the elder is asking so nicely. You’re not really going to refuse, are you?","If you refuse, you’re seriously a terrible person.","Wild Grylls: ...","What a rotten situation.","Now I had no choice but to name him Wonmo.","The Heavenly Demon had helped me many times, so it was hard to reject her suggestion.","I rubbed my face and sighed.","Why was I letting the Gallery control me like this?","’Still, Wonmo isn’t that bad of a name... is it?’","Wonmo.","It sounded like the sort of name people used in old countryside villages.","It felt rustic to the point of sounding a little dim-witted.","’At least they didn’t name him Dolsoe.’","Although...","Would Dolsoe have been better?","I honestly couldn’t tell anymore.","I looked at the baby owlbear, who was still eating honey and had now somehow become Wonmo, before quietly calling out.","\"Wonmo.\"","\"Kyuu?\"","Wait.","You didn’t look up when I called you Fluffy.","Why did you immediately react to Wonmo?","I stared at the baby owlbear—Wonmo—with an incredulous expression.","The longer I gazed into those round eyes, the calmer I felt.","’Ah, whatever.’","I approached him.","Honey was dripping from his beak.","I stroked his head and firmly imprinted the name into his mind.","\"From now on, your name is Wonmo. Got it?\"","\"Kyuu!\"","He gave me a bright smile, as though he loved it.","But why?","***","Meanwhile, at around the same time...","\"Hehe.\"","The Heavenly Demon, Yu Sowol, smiled proudly.","The name she had suggested, Wonmo, had become the baby owlbear’s official name.","The Gallery was already clamoring for more pictures of Wonmo.","That alone proved how powerful Wonmo’s appeal was.","What could possibly be more satisfying than this?","’To think the name received such an enthusiastic response even in the Gallery. Grylls must be delighted as well.’","Had Grylls heard that, he would have started foaming at the mouth."]},{"title":"Chapter 22","paragraphs":["Owlbear (3)","Now that the name had been decided, all that remained was to bond with Wonmo.","Giving him honey had raised his affection toward me considerably, but he was still only a cub.","He couldn’t yet tell right from wrong, and with his mother dead, I would have to take care of him.","But then the biggest problem occurred to me.","’How am I supposed to raise him?’","Even back home, I had never owned a single pet.","I had barely been able to take care of myself, so raising an animal had never even crossed my mind.","At least I had seen enough dogs and cats to have some idea of how to handle them.","An owlbear, however, was a completely different matter.","Aside from the fact that they had enormous appetites and were extremely ferocious, I knew absolutely nothing about them.","’The most important thing is making him recognize me as his owner.’","I watched Wonmo scurry around the cave.","Perhaps because he was still young, he was overflowing with curiosity.","\"Sniff. Sniff, sniff.\"","He wandered around the place where his mother had died for quite some time.","Judging by the way he kept sniffing the ground, he seemed to remember her scent.","Unfortunately, the mother owlbear had already been shipped off to America...","No, to the auction house.","People were still steadily bidding on it, so I would soon receive a large sum of money.","’But that tiny thing is really going to grow that big?’","The mother owlbear had been, with only slight exaggeration, about the size of a house.","But look at Wonmo.","The round little fellow was only the size of a medium-sized dog.","Even the pale color of his fur suggested that, just as the Gallery users had said, he had only recently been born.","\"Kueeeek!\"","\"Oh dear.\"","He was far too curious for his own good.","Why would he try eating the fasting pills inside the sack?","With his sharp sense of smell, he should have noticed their bitter scent.","Why had he still eaten one?","\"Kuaaaak!\"","Rip!","Yet even as a cub, his ferocity remained intact.","The moment Wonmo swung his claws, the sack tore open.","I nearly screamed when the fasting pills inside came spilling out.","\"Hey! Park Wonmo! You can’t do that!\"","\"Kyuu? Kyuu?\"","\"No matter how bad they taste, you can’t just tear the sack apart!\"","Even as I scolded him, I hurried to deal with the mess.","I laid the torn sack on its side so the remaining pills wouldn’t spill out.","Then I bought another sack of a suitable size from the auction house and transferred them into it.","’Didn’t they say owlbears would even eat rotting corpses?’","Just how disgusting were these fasting pills for every animal to react the same way?","I had grown used to them, but apparently animals couldn’t tolerate them.","’First, I need to make him understand that this is his home...’","That raised another question.","Why had the mother owlbear brought her cub here?","Owlbears were highly territorial animals, which meant they were extremely sensitive about their domains.","In other words, they normally avoided entering another creature’s territory.","Even if she had been scouting the area, there was no reason for her to bring along a newborn cub.","’Did something drive them out of their original territory?’","No.","That probably wasn’t it.","The mother owlbear had been in perfect condition when she encountered me.","She hadn’t immediately tried to tear me apart either. She had first examined the area.","Perhaps they had simply been moving...","I couldn’t be sure.","The best way to find out would be to locate their nest.","’That’s impossible right now.’","Just look at that ball of fur staring at me with those huge round eyes.","He was sitting on the straw-filled mat, gazing blankly at me.","\"Come here, you little cutie.\"","\"Kyuu.\"","He was so adorable I could hardly stand it.","How could anything be this cute?","I showered Wonmo with affection, scratching beneath his chin and stroking his head to my heart’s content.","Right.","How could I possibly leave him behind?","Even if I did go somewhere, I couldn’t leave the cave unattended until he understood that this place was his home.","’Then repairing the cave is probably my best option...’","It was a little disappointing, but it wasn’t a bad choice.","The greatest problem, however, was still water .","I could manage my own hygiene, but Wonmo was another matter.","There was no telling what kind of disease he might bring back, so bathing him was essential.","’Washing him in the creek would be difficult.’","The golden poison frog wasn’t the issue.","The problem was that I had no idea where Wonmo might run off to.","If he crossed to the opposite bank, it would be a disaster.","And if the terrain changed at the exact moment he crossed, it would become an even greater disaster.","’Isn’t there a better way?’","I stared at Wonmo, who was watching me blankly, then silently picked him up.","His fur was this fluffy, yet I hadn’t been allowed to name him Fluffy.","I’m sorry, little guy. Your owner failed you.","As though he understood my feelings, he rubbed his face against me.","Grrrrumble.","Then a strange noise reached my ears.","It definitely hadn’t come from my stomach.","I slowly set Wonmo down and stared at his face.","\"Kyuu...\"","\"Are you hungry?\"","\"Slurp.\"","Don’t lick your lips while staring at me.","That’s terrifying.","Before Wonmo could go berserk, I hurriedly opened the auction house.","It sold all kinds of goods, so I could easily buy some suitable meat.","’They even sell monster meat?’","Orcs, goblins, gnolls, trolls, and more.","I had no idea why anyone would list that sort of thing at the auction house.","Apparently monster meat was so tough and foul-tasting that nobody ate it unless they were desperate.","The sellers had probably listed it simply because they didn’t know what else to do with it.","Its price was also comparatively low.","\"Here. Try this.\"","\"Sniff, sniff, sniff.\"","I bought some orc meat and placed it in front of Wonmo.","He sniffed it curiously before taking a huge bite.","\"Nom, nom, nom.\"","\"Is it edible?\"","\"Nom, nom, nom, nom. Crunch! Chomp!\"","He ate it without hesitation.","As expected of an owlbear, his diet appeared to be close to that of an ordinary bear.","I placed a bowl of water beside him, then went outside.","It would take him a while to finish all that, so I intended to complete the rest of my work.","Thwack! Thwack!","After chopping away with the axe for some time, the tree had begun to wobble slightly.","The sound was no longer a dull thud but closer to the noise of splitting firewood.","After checking the tree’s position relative to the cave, I kicked it hard.","The tree slowly tipped over before collapsing with a series of loud cracks.","Craaaack!","Thud!","It was so massive that merely falling produced an enormous amount of noise.","Surely that wouldn’t irritate any nearby animals.","Fortunately, the greatest threat in the area—the owlbear—had already been sold through the auction house.","’Should I cut it into three sections?’","I walked over to the fallen tree and estimated its size.","A tree this large could probably provide enough material for three or four sections of barricade.","The problem was that I still had to split and shape the thick trunk.","’Why did I do this?’","One problem after another.","There was still an overwhelming amount of work left.","I should have learned an internal energy cultivation technique first, just as I had originally planned.","I had gotten bored, started doing something unnecessary, and only created more work for myself.","After letting out a deep sigh, I decided to begin by removing the smaller branches.","There were so many that I wouldn’t have to worry about firewood for quite some time.","Once I had roughly cleared away the branches, I planned to cut the trunk into smaller sections.","’A sword probably won’t work. I’ll need to buy a saw...’","Just thinking about sawing through it made me dizzy.","Still, I couldn’t give up now.","Before buying the saw, I returned to the cave to rest.","\"Grrrrr...\"","When I entered the cave, I found Wonmo asleep on the mat.","He had completely finished the monster meat I had given him earlier.","No matter the species, babies tended to spend most of the day sleeping.","I watched Wonmo, curled up into a ball, then silently opened the Gallery.","***","Title: Our Wonmo Is Sleeping","Wild Grylls","(Photo of Wonmo curled into a ball while sleeping.)","Isn’t he adorable?","Ah... This is so healing...","More! Give us more!","He really looks like a ball. LOL.","The more I see it, the more I think Wonmo was the perfect name.","I seriously want to hug him at least once.","The responses were overwhelmingly positive.","Anyone who could look at this and remain unaffected couldn’t possibly be human.","As I proudly read through the comments, one in particular caught my attention.","Passing Dwarf: Is that emergency food? Looks tasty.","Wild Grylls: Are you insane?","Passing Dwarf: I drank yesterday and just woke up. What happened?","It was Passing Dwarf.","Apparently he had only just woken up after drinking himself to sleep.","How could anyone look at Wonmo and call him emergency food?","I thought the dwarf was an idiot in more ways than one, but the other Gallery users were even worse.","So Grylls became a pet servant. LOL.","I’m telling you, the moment he gets hungry, he’ll eat you first. LOL.","Wild Grylls: You people are seriously insane.","Right.","This was the Gallery.","I let out a hollow laugh.","Since Passing Dwarf was here, I decided to ask him something.","Wonmo isn’t Grylls’s emergency food. Grylls is Wonmo’s emergency food. LOL.","Passing Dwarf: Really? So you’ve taken in a master.","Wild Grylls: Dwarf, can you get me a good saw?","Passing Dwarf: A saw? Oh, did you cut down a tree?","Wild Grylls: Yeah. But just thinking about sawing it makes my balls tremble.","Passing Dwarf: Unless it’s made of adamantium, one saw is about as good as another. It’s better to chop into it with an axe first, then start sawing.","Wild Grylls: That’s still too exhausting.","Passing Dwarf: Did you think it would be easy? That kind of work normally takes at least two people.","It was infuriating, but I couldn’t argue with him.","Nothing was ever easy.","The best option would be to learn an internal energy cultivation technique from the Heavenly Demon.","If I could use mana, surely the work would become easier somehow.","Until then, I had no choice but to brute-force it through sheer effort.","Passing Dwarf: Or sell the log at the auction house and buy a fence or barricade. Wouldn’t that solve it?","Wild Grylls: There aren’t any.","Passing Dwarf: Why not?","That wasn’t the only strange thing.","Why weren’t there any?","I had searched too, but couldn’t find what I needed.","There were a few fence-like structures, but none in the form I wanted.","Wild Grylls: Why are you asking me? If there aren’t any, there aren’t any. And wouldn’t they be expensive?","Passing Dwarf: Even if they are, they’d still be cheaper than the log you cut down. Do you have any idea how valuable wood grown in the Forest of Four Seasons is?","Wild Grylls: Of course I don’t. I told you I came from another world.","Passing Dwarf: Wasn’t that just drunken nonsense?","Wild Grylls: You bastard. LOL.","Hard to blame him for not believing you. LOL.","LMAO.","Wild Grylls: Why didn’t you tell me sooner?","Passing Dwarf: So you’d suffer a little.","Wild Grylls: You son of a bitch.","Passing Dwarf: Sawing isn’t the end of it. You need to dry out the moisture, plane the wood, and do a bunch of other things.","Wild Grylls: What happens if I don’t remove the moisture?","Passing Dwarf: Mold everywhere!","Wild Grylls: Ha...","Looks like reality just hit him. LOL.","At least you gained knowledge. Have a drink!","No.","Why did everyone seem so untrustworthy?","I really wanted a drink now.","Had I known this, I would’ve at least asked the Gallery before starting.","Just as the dwarf said, it seemed better to list the log at the auction house.","’In that blocky world, they made things so easily.’","That was only because the protagonist over there had absurd abilities.","As long as he had the materials, he could instantly craft anything from a sword to a pickaxe.","That was what made him incredible.","Why had I been dropped into this hellish world without a single useful ability?","The situation made me want to sigh endlessly, but at least I had the Gallery.","’Should I ask the dwarf to make it?’","He was irritating, but no one I knew was better at this kind of work.","After thinking for a moment, I asked Passing Dwarf.","Passing Dwarf: Except when I’m drunk. LOL.","Wild Grylls: What are you holding right now?","Passing Dwarf: Beer.","Wild Grylls: You son of a...","Passing Dwarf: It’s basically a soft drink to a dwarf. Got a problem?","That is technically true. LOL.","It’s the kind of truth that deserves a beating. LOL.","Wild Grylls: Then if I give you the log, can you make me a suitable barricade?","Passing Dwarf: Just buy one at the auction house. I checked earlier and saw a few. Drying the wood alone takes several weeks.","Wild Grylls: The auction house doesn’t have the kind I want.","Passing Dwarf: Fair enough. They might sell fences, but probably not proper barricades. I’ll see what I can find.","Wild Grylls: You’re not messing with me, are you?","Passing Dwarf: I don’t joke about this kind of work.","That was a relief.","My head was spinning.","What kind of alcoholic lunatic was this?","Still, he didn’t seem to be joking, so I looked through the auction house again.","As expected, there were no barricades in the shape I wanted.","Once a barricade was built, it tended to remain in place, so demand was probably low.","Even if someone needed one, they would likely cut and process nearby timber rather than buy it.","’I should list the log first.’","I registered the fallen log at the auction house.","I had no idea how much it would sell for, but I hoped it was as valuable as the dwarf claimed.","If it fetched a high price, every tree around here would become a savings account.","’I’ll have to wait for the barricade.’","The dwarf said he would list one soon, so I could buy it when he did.","Until then, I planned to improve the area around the cave little by little.","’It’s not like I’m going to live here forever, but...’","First, I marked the trees that needed to be cut down.","I planned to dig a moat after installing the barricade.","Once I had roughly marked the trees with my axe, I returned to the cave to rest.","Wonmo was still deep in dreamland.","He was truly adorable.","I smiled warmly and opened the Gallery again.","Many more comments had appeared in the meantime.","Among them, a comment from the familiar named user PraiseTheSun stood out the most.","PraiseTheSun: Hey. Have you brushed Wonmo’s fur?","Wild Grylls: Why would I need to brush him?","PraiseTheSun: Animals with thick fur need regular brushing. Either that or a bath. Try brushing him once.","I didn’t really understand, but I should probably follow the advice.","It seemed that PraiseTheSun also raised animals.","I bought a fine-toothed comb from the auction house and approached Wonmo.","Then, careful not to wake him, I gently began combing through his thick fur.","\"...What is this?\"","Now I understood why PraiseTheSun had brought it up.","Something was wriggling between the teeth of the comb.","It looked absolutely disgusting.","\"T-Ticks?\"","I desperately needed water.","Right now."]},{"title":"Chapter 23","paragraphs":["Water (1)","Had I underestimated the wilderness, or had I simply been too optimistic?","The moment I saw the ticks crawling between the teeth of the comb, I realized something.","When it came to hygiene, the wilderness was far more dangerous than I had imagined.","To properly maintain cleanliness, I needed to secure a large amount of water somehow.","’Does water have some kind of personal grudge against me?’","In any case, washing Wonmo clean came first.","I should probably take a bath while I was at it.","It was fortunate that I had been wearing clothes. Otherwise, I would almost certainly have been bitten by ticks too.","First, I wanted to thank PraiseTheSun and ask for advice.","Wild Grylls: Holy crap... What are all these ticks? Things could’ve gone seriously wrong if I’d ignored them.","PraiseTheSun: At least you noticed now. Washing him with hot water should do the trick.","Wild Grylls: I’m in an environment where getting water is difficult.","PraiseTheSun: Then apply insect repellent to your body. A hot bath would still be the best solution, though.","According to PraiseTheSun, an owlbear’s hide was too thick for ticks to cause it much harm.","The real problem was me, since my skin was comparatively thin and I was constantly beside him.","I took off my clothes, shook them out thoroughly, and applied insect repellent all over my body.","Fortunately, I didn’t find any ticks on myself.","’I need to start wearing long pants.’","The uniform PrincessChaenggu had given me only had long sleeves.","For the time being, I would have to rely on insect repellent.","’No wonder people in survival documentaries always cover their entire bodies.’","Thanks to this, I finally understood the importance of proper clothing.","Long sleeves and long pants were essential.","After carefully applying the repellent without missing a single spot, I looked at Wonmo.","He was still sleeping soundly, completely unaware of what had happened.","’Right. It’s not your fault.’","I changed my clothes and thought things over.","Water had become even more urgent than before.","Unfortunately, the golden poison frogs had firmly occupied the creek, making things difficult.","Still, the creek was the closest water source, so abandoning it would be a waste.","’Should I dig a water channel instead? It’s not that far away.’","It wasn’t a bad option.","The only downside was the physical labor involved.","As I had mentioned before, the creek wasn’t very far from the cave, so perhaps it wouldn’t be that difficult.","However, I had no idea how to dig a proper channel, so I would need advice.","***","Title: Dwarf, Help Me","Wild Grylls","I’m thinking of digging a water channel. Give me some advice.","Passing Dwarf: For free?","Wild Grylls: Want one of the frogs? They’re expensive.","Passing Dwarf: I was joking. LOL.","More than anything else, I was concerned that the water might become contaminated.","There was a limit to how much joking one person should do.","Suddenly, I became curious about his age.","Considering how knowledgeable he was, he probably wasn’t young.","Yet he behaved like someone who had never fully grown up.","Passing Dwarf: Are you planning to live there permanently?","Wild Grylls: Not really, but getting water is too difficult. Those frogs are making it a nightmare.","Passing Dwarf: If you’re not settling there permanently, don’t dig a channel. The workload is insane.","Wild Grylls: Is it really that bad?","Passing Dwarf: Yeah. And if you can’t prevent erosion, you’ll end up with nothing but filthy water. Better not to do it.","Erosion was that phenomenon, wasn’t it?","The process where rock was gradually worn away by various factors.","There was no need to explain what would happen to soil, which was far softer than rock.","Wild Grylls: Then is there no other way?","Passing Dwarf: Roughly how far away is the creek?","Wild Grylls: About ten to twelve minutes on foot?","Passing Dwarf: At that distance, it’d be better to carry the water yourself.","Wild Grylls: So I can get eaten by a snake on the way? LOL.","Passing Dwarf: Hey. Wait, wait, wait.","He’s suddenly desperate. LOL.","He can’t even drink water freely. LOL.","Nothing is ever easy for him. LOL.","It wasn’t as though I hadn’t considered carrying the water myself.","But I had no idea what dangers I might encounter along the way, and drawing the water itself would be difficult.","The moment I put my hand into the creek, golden poison frogs would come swarming out.","As though I could casually collect water under those conditions.","I had hands and a functioning brain too.","But this was the wilderness.","A single mistake could cost me my life, so I had no choice but to prioritize safety as much as possible.","Passing Dwarf: There is one method, but you’ll have to build something. You okay with that?","Wild Grylls: Yeah. That’s fine.","Passing Dwarf: First, where is the creek relative to you? Uphill or downhill?","Wild Grylls: I have to go uphill to reach it.","Passing Dwarf: Oh. Then this should be easy. It might be expensive, though. Is that okay?","Wild Grylls: Could it possibly cost more than my life?","Passing Dwarf: Good. I’ll make a post soon.","Starlight Princess.","A familiar named user who had gone silent for some time.","I had been worried that something might have happened to her, so seeing the message immediately put me at ease.","[Wild Grylls: Starlight Princess? Is that really you?]","[Starlight Princess: Hello, Mr. Grylls! Yes! It’s really me!]","Passing Dwarf had said he would post an explanation, so I only needed to wait patiently.","At the same time, I felt uneasy.","If the method was complicated enough to require an entire post, it must involve a fair amount of work.","Would I really be able to secure a stable water supply?","Water always seemed to become an obstacle for me.","[Starlight Princess has requested a trade. Would you like to accept?]","\"Huh?\"","I had been absentmindedly browsing the Gallery when the notification appeared.","My eyes widened as I stared at the message.","Even through the text, I could feel her cheerful energy.","Once a Gallery nickname was chosen, it could never be changed.","That meant the person requesting the trade truly was Starlight Princess.","With a broad smile, I sent her a reply.","[Wild Grylls: Have you fully recovered?]","[Starlight Princess: Yes! Thanks to the gift you gave me, I made a complete recovery! Thank you so much!]","I was relieved to hear she had recovered.","I had been deeply worried that something had happened to her.","There would be no need to worry about that anymore.","Her incurable illness had been cured.","[Wild Grylls: That’s wonderful. Congratulations.]","[Starlight Princess: It’s all thanks to you, Mr. Grylls. I couldn’t post anything because I was undergoing medical examinations...]","I could roughly understand what had happened.","After finally obtaining the health she had longed for so desperately, she must have wanted to undergo a thorough examination.","The fact that she had returned after only a day meant she was almost certainly fully cured.","[Starlight Princess: Yes. Honestly, I feel like running around right now. Unfortunately, my parents won’t allow it.]","[Wild Grylls: They’re worried about you, so don’t push yourself too hard.]","[Starlight Princess: I think this every time we speak, but you truly are a kind person, Mr. Grylls. People like you are rare in the Gallery.]","I tilted my head when she called me kind.","People seemed to say that about me surprisingly often.","Considering the Gallery’s culture, perhaps it was true.","’I’m not really sure.’","Maybe it simply meant that this world was so terrible that basic decency stood out.","Given the era, human rights were probably treated like something to be chewed up and spat out.","Combine that with the Gallery’s uniquely unhealthy culture, and there was no need for further explanation.","[Starlight Princess has registered an item for trade.]","[Starlight Princess: This is the elixir I mentioned before. I kept only enough for emergencies and sent you the rest, so there should be plenty.]","[Wild Grylls: Thank you so much. You’re not feeling any discomfort, are you?]","[Wild Grylls: Helping someone else ultimately means helping yourself. And you’re kind too, aren’t you? You could’ve simply ignored your promise, yet you still repaid me like this.]","[Starlight Princess: Those are wise words. Do you still wish to leave the Forest of Four Seasons?]","[Wild Grylls: Yes. I want to leave immediately.]","[Starlight Princess: I may not be able to do much, but I’ll help you find a way out. I might not look it, but I’m rather intelligent.]","[Wild Grylls: Or you could just come here instead?]","[Starlight Princess: Ah. That’s a little... haha.]","[Wild Grylls: LOL.]","The words had slipped out automatically.","It definitely wasn’t because I was a hopelessly doting owner.","Wonmo really was that cute.","Of course, I had only been joking.","Who would tell someone who had been at death’s door just yesterday to come to a place where they would almost certainly die?","I had heard that no one who entered the Forest of Four Seasons had ever escaped.","That was why it was easier to treat Starlight Princess’s promise as comfort rather than something she genuinely intended to accomplish.","[Starlight Princess: Oh! That reminds me, I saw the owlbear photos.]","[Wild Grylls: Cute, isn’t he?]","[Starlight Princess: Yes. But the name is a little... questionable. Wonmo? What kind of name is Wonmo?]","[Wild Grylls: Did you have another name in mind, Lady Starlight?]","[Starlight Princess: Since it means a healthy child...]","Starlight Princess paused for a moment before revealing the name she had thought of.","[Starlight Princess: Gym Newbie. How does Gym Newbie sound?]","[Wild Grylls: Oh...]","It sounded like the kind of name that would eventually evolve into Gym Maniac.","How could every single named user have such terrible naming sense?","The more I thought about it, the more Fluffy seemed like the best name by far.","[Wild Grylls: I think I’ll have to keep calling him Wonmo for now. They held a vote without even telling me.]","[Starlight Princess: Can’t you just ignore it?]","[Wild Grylls: The Heavenly Demon chose the name, so it’s hard to dismiss it so casually.]","She was one of the named users who had helped me, and the Heavenly Demon herself had personally chosen it.","I couldn’t simply ignore that.","If she became disappointed and distanced herself from me, I would be the one losing out.","Starlight Princess seemed to understand that as well. Though she complained, she ultimately accepted it.","[Starlight Princess: That’s a shame. So what are you going to do now?]","[Wild Grylls: I’ll probably work on drawing water from the creek. The dwarf said he’d upload a post explaining how soon.]","[Starlight Princess: I see. If you ever need help, please tell me. I’ll be waiting.]","[Wild Grylls: Thank you.]","[Starlight Princess: Good luck!]","Our conversation ended there.","I felt both warmth and bitterness at the same time.","I was happy that Starlight Princess had fully recovered, but nothing had changed for me.","Unless I escaped this hellish place, living an ordinary life was out of the question.","’I can escape... right?’","It was a thought that crossed my mind every day.","Could I really leave the Forest of Four Seasons?","If dangerous plants and animals were the only problem, perhaps I could somehow fight my way out.","But the forest’s greatest danger was that space itself changed constantly.","Getting lost was dangerous enough, yet even the terrain shifted unpredictably.","The thought alone was overwhelming.","’As for the elixirs... Whoa. She gave me seven?’","Starlight Princess had sent me seven elixirs in total.","Judging by their different colors, they seemed to be of different grades.","I had heard that paler colors indicated lower quality, so sorting them was easy enough.","’Wonmo might break them. I should hide these.’","I stored the elixirs inside the box Passing Dwarf had previously given me.","Just in case Wonmo went rummaging through it, I pushed the box into the farthest corner of the cave.","’Come to think of it, did the dwarf upload his post?’","Next, I checked whether Passing Dwarf had posted his explanation.","After refreshing the Gallery a few times, his post finally appeared.","***","Title: Grylls, Read This","Passing Dwarf","(A rough drawing showing how to draw water from a stream.)","(A photo of a natural-rubber hose.)","(A photo of a valve.)","Set it up like the drawing above.","Suck on the end of each hose until the water starts flowing.","Oh, and don’t lie down while sucking on it. Stay upright. The pressure difference will make the water gush out.","Attach a valve to the final hose so you can open and close it.","Understand?","Wild Grylls: I get the general idea, but what’s that mesh for? Filtering impurities?","Passing Dwarf: Yeah. You’re surprisingly quick.","Wild Grylls: Of course. I understand things instantly. LOL.","Passing Dwarf: Now I suddenly don’t want to give it to you.","Wild Grylls: I am a complete idiot.","That attitude changed fast. LOL.","Watching these two interact never stops being funny.","You two get along well. LOL.","Passing Dwarf: Anyway, connect the hoses properly and maintain the correct slope. Then it won’t be difficult.","Wild Grylls: You said it would be expensive. Is the hose the costly part?","Passing Dwarf: Yeah. It’s made of rubber, so it’s ridiculously expensive.","Rubber is expensive?","The question crossed my mind, but the answer soon became obvious.","Judging from what I had read in the Gallery, factories had only recently begun operating in this world.","Apparently, there were also locomotives powered by mana, though they weren’t commonly used.","’They said people usually just use warp gates, right?’","It was fitting for a fantasy world.","Sports such as football and baseball were widely developed, yet science seemed slightly behind.","Still, it made sense if magic filled the role of science.","Warp gates were expensive, so I had heard that commoners used locomotives instead.","’The uniform PrincessChaenggu gave me must be incredibly expensive too.’","Considering what it was made of, that was only natural.","After listening to Passing Dwarf’s various explanations, I asked the question that mattered most.","But then another problem arose.","The Gallery’s trading rules.","Once a user completed a trade, they couldn’t trade again for twenty-four hours.","Passing Dwarf had traded with someone after noon yesterday, which meant he couldn’t directly trade with me yet.","Passing Dwarf: I can list it as an instant-purchase item at the auction house, but I’ll put it up for 1,100 gold. Is that okay?","Wild Grylls: Just list it.","Passing Dwarf: LOL.","Wild Grylls: Then how much is it actually worth?","Passing Dwarf: If I’m giving you a discount, around 500 gold total. That’s including the processed rubber and the valve.","Five hundred gold was definitely expensive.","Still, I had money left from what Allfather had paid me.","It made my blood run cold, but there was no helping it.","Water was urgently needed.","This was no time to worry about money.","I might compare prices for a barricade or fence, but not for water.","I immediately opened the auction house and checked the item Passing Dwarf had listed.","[Title: Grylls Is an Idiot]","[Price: 1,100 Gold]","\"This bastard.\"","I’d remember this.","I let out a hollow laugh and bought it.","Someone else could theoretically snatch it first, but the price was so absurdly high that nobody would.","Even if someone did, I could simply buy another one from the dwarf.","\"Now that everything’s ready...\"","It was time to go get water.","As a precaution, I equipped both my sword and shield.","I slung the tightly rolled hose over my shoulder.","All that remained was the work itself.","’As soon as I get the water, I’ll wash Wonmo first.’","I looked at Wonmo, who was sleeping peacefully.","What if he woke up while I was gone?","Would he come outside looking for me?","That would be extremely dangerous.","’I need to finish as quickly as possible.’","It was time to put my practical skills to the test."]},{"title":"Chapter 24","paragraphs":["Water (2)","All the preparations for drawing water from the creek were complete, but several problems remained.","The first—and biggest—was avoiding the golden poison frogs somehow.","They leaped out the instant I put my hand in the water, making them an enormous nuisance.","The second problem was the depth of the creek.","It was deep enough to submerge more than half my arm.","That meant it would be difficult to secure the hose in place with stones.","I checked the items Passing Dwarf had given me.","’I just need to cover this with the mesh and connect it to the hose...’","I alternated between looking at the gleaming funnel and the mesh that was supposed to cover it.","Connecting the funnel to the hose was simple.","The difficult part was securing it in place.","’Do I have no choice but to dig a shallow hole with the shovel?’","That seemed like the best option.","I carried the equipment to the creek, then went back for the shovel.","Fortunately, I didn’t encounter any dangerous animals while traveling back and forth.","The Mad Dog pack had died long ago, and the owlbear had recently been shipped off to the auction house.","I probably wouldn’t encounter another predator-class creature for some time.","At this point, insects like ticks frightened me more than predators.","Shhhhhhh—","Once I had brought the shovel, all the preparations were finally complete.","I looked at the fast-flowing creek and slowly got to work.","First, I carefully began digging into the bank with the shovel.","Thud! Thump!","Fortunately, no frogs leaped out.","Still, I kept checking my surroundings between each strike, just in case.","Rushhhhh—","Eventually, I created a space large enough to insert the funnel.","To increase the force of the current, I placed stones around the area I had dug.","The water was flowing strongly enough now.","All that remained was connecting the hose.","I covered the funnel with the mesh, then attached it to the hose.","Instead of cable ties, I firmly secured the connection with metal ties.","Since plastic hadn’t been invented in this world, they apparently used iron as a substitute.","’Wouldn’t these be difficult to make too?’","The hose was made from natural rubber, so it made sense for it to be expensive.","But to me, these metal ties looked as though they should cost even more.","’Maybe it’s because a dwarf made them. Whatever.’","After confirming that everything was firmly secured, I moved to the next location.","One hose wasn’t enough.","Because of the distance, I needed to connect several hoses along the route.","\"Sluuuurp!\"","Just as Passing Dwarf had instructed, I sucked hard on the end of the hose.","When I carefully lowered it, the water began flowing much more strongly than before.","I connected that hose to another one and tightly fastened them together with a metal tie.","After repeating the same process several times, I eventually reached the shelter.","Finally, I connected the end of the last hose to the valve.","The work was complete.","Rushhhhh—","\"Perfect. This is perfect.\"","The water flowed beautifully.","Just looking at it filled me with satisfaction.","Still, the job wasn’t entirely finished.","As I had emphasized countless times, this was the wilderness.","An animal could bite through the hose, so covering it with soil was essential.","After roughly two hours of work, everything was finally done.","The fact that I no longer needed to worry about water filled me with pride.","\"Kyuu?\"","\"Oh. You’re awake?\"","Coincidentally, Wonmo seemed to have woken up.","He stared at me with his usual bright, wide eyes.","I wanted to pick him up, but his body was crawling with ticks.","’Bath first.’","I also needed to clean myself while I was at it.","I bought a large iron tub from the auction house and filled it with water.","After rinsing it several times and checking for debris, I filled it to the brim.","Then I lit a fire beneath it to warm the water.","’I should give him a dewormer too, right?’","I needed to do laundry as well.","I was incredibly busy.","Since things had come this far, I might as well set up a drying rack too.","Simply having access to water whenever I wanted greatly expanded what I could do.","While the water in the tub heated, I made a post in the Gallery.","***","Title: I’m Rich Now","Wild Grylls","(Video of water gushing from the hose.)","I’m rich in water now.","Oh. You succeeded?","LMAO.","Now you can finally take a bath.","Wild Grylls: I’m washing Wonmo first. He had a ridiculous number of ticks.","Passing Dwarf: You finished surprisingly quickly. No problems?","Wild Grylls: Nothing major. Want a mandrake later?","Passing Dwarf: Oh, I’d appreciate that. Straight into a bottle of liquor. LOL.","Wild Grylls: Screw you. You’re not getting one.","He’d use such an expensive mandrake to make infused liquor?","What kind of dwarf is this? LOL.","Heavenly Demon: Now that you have secured water, what do you intend to do next?","Wild Grylls: I’m not sure. Once I get a barricade from the dwarf, there won’t be much left. Maybe cutting trees or exploring the area?","Heavenly Demon: If that is the case, it may be time for you to learn an internal energy cultivation technique from this lady.","Wild Grylls: I’d be happy to. Let me wash Wonmo first, then I’ll contact you.","Heavenly Demon: I shall wait. This lady is looking forward to it as well.","SwordMaster: An internal energy technique is important, but have you been practicing your swordsmanship?","Wild Grylls: I’ve been studying it consistently. I still only know the basics, though.","SwordMaster: Excellent. Grow strong quickly and marry me.","Wild Grylls: Ma’am?","SwordMaster: I was joking.","That didn’t sound like a joke.","Her true feelings slip out surprisingly often.","Is she that desperate to get married? LOL.","Hmm...","As expected, the Gallery was filled with strange people.","Still, there was no denying that SwordMaster’s advice was helping me grow stronger each day.","When I fought the owlbear, recalling her posts had saved my life.","Otherwise, I would’ve died.","\"Hmm. This should be warm enough. Wonmo?\"","\"Kyuu?\"","The water in the tub had become pleasantly warm.","Steam wasn’t rising from it, but considering the forest’s temperature, it was more than sufficient.","I dragged the tub over to Wonmo.","Rather than being tall and narrow, it was wide from side to side to suit his body, making it the perfect size.","\"Get in. It’s time for a bath.\"","\"Kyuuu.\"","Could he really understand what I was saying?","Wonmo stared at the tub with his usual sparkling eyes, then cautiously placed a paw inside.","The warm water seemed unfamiliar, because he flinched at first.","Fortunately, once he realized it wouldn’t hurt him, he carefully lowered his fluffy body into the tub.","\"Kyuuuuuu...\"","\"Feels good, doesn’t it?\"","He closed his eyes and relaxed completely.","I chuckled and began washing every part of his body.","Along the way, I carefully applied insect repellent to various places and removed all the ticks.","’Won’t this become pointless once he starts roaming around again?’","I would simply have to accept that.","I scrubbed him thoroughly with soap.","Wonmo seemed to enjoy my touch, because he kept his eyes closed the entire time.","Unfortunately, the bathwater became unbelievably filthy.","That couldn’t be helped in the wilderness.","It was something I had to endure.","’Still, I can’t resist taking a picture.’","I uploaded a photo of Wonmo bathing to the Gallery.","Only his face was sticking out of the water, making him look incredibly adorable.","***","Title: Gave Wonmo a Bath","Wild Grylls","(Video of Wonmo bathing.)","Cute, right? Give me an upvote if you agree.","His face is practically cheating.","That little thing is going to become a tyrant someday?","Just watching this is healing.","Ugh, disgusting.","Your face is more disgusting.","I was talking about the water. Is your face dirty or something?","LOL.","How did twisted people appear even under a post this cute?","I had only uploaded it to show Wonmo off, so I didn’t care much.","I was still vigorously scrubbing him when—","\"Kyuuuuuuu...!\"","Shiver, shiver.","Wonmo suddenly began trembling.","The abrupt reaction startled me.","\"Wonmo? Are you uncomfortable?\"","\"Kyuuuu.\"","\"No? Then...\"","What was happening?","Just as I began wondering—","Float...","Something rose to the surface of the filthy bathwater.","It was dark brown, almost black, and round...","\"...\"","\"...Wonmo. Did you poop?\"","\"Kyuu!\"","\"GYAAAAAH! Get out right now! Hurry!\"","It seemed potty training would have to come first.","***","After washing Wonmo, I learned something important.","Whether it was a person or an animal, washing someone else was incredibly exhausting.","So much filth came out of him that I had to replace the bathwater several times.","By the time it was finally my turn to wash, the sun was already beginning to set.","\"Nom, nom, chomp.\"","\"Is it tasty?\"","After finishing Wonmo’s bath, I dried him as thoroughly as possible with a towel.","A hair dryer would have been useful, but since I didn’t have one, I had to rely on the campfire.","I also gave him a deworming medicine.","As expected of an owlbear that ate practically anything, he swallowed it without hesitation.","’Someone gets to eat meat while someone else survives on fasting pills. How unfair.’","I bought Wonmo’s meal from the auction house.","Just like that morning, it was monster meat.","Monster meat was the cheapest option available. It was practically useless, so it cost less than ten gold.","I grimaced as I put a bitter fasting pill into my mouth.","No matter how many times I ate one, it was still unbearably bitter.","’My stomach always hurts after eating these too.’","Potty training Wonmo was simple.","He was never allowed to relieve himself inside the cave.","And if he needed to go, he had to give me some kind of signal. Then I would stand guard beside him.","Strangely enough, I couldn’t tell whether Wonmo was exceptionally intelligent or whether all owlbears were naturally like this, but he understood everything.","The claim that owlbears became fiercely loyal as long as they were well-fed hadn’t been an exaggeration.","’Now that I’ve roughly finished eating, all that’s left is learning the internal energy cultivation technique.’","Sitting cross-legged no longer hurt as much either.","It hadn’t even been a week, yet I felt as though my flexibility had improved dramatically.","I wondered whether that was even possible, but decided not to question something beneficial.","Even if I thought deeply about it, I wouldn’t find an answer.","***","Title: Heavenly Demon, Are You There?","Wild Grylls","I’d like to start learning the internal energy cultivation technique. Are you here?","Heavenly Demon: I have been waiting.","Wild Grylls: ???","Whoa. The post went up ten seconds ago, but she commented after only two seconds.","Isn’t that basically stalking?","That’s a little scary.","The Heavenly Demon had often been the first to comment on my posts, but never this quickly.","’Uh... Is she really that bored?’","More likely, this was her way of repaying the favor I had done for her.","How should I put it?","She felt like a veteran player who had finally found a newbie to teach.","Thinking of it that way made me feel more comfortable.","Wild Grylls: You were here. As I mentioned before, please post the instructions as private comments.","Heavenly Demon: Very well. First, sit in the lotus position.","I was just as bewildered as everyone else.","How had she commented the instant I uploaded the post?","Following her instructions, I crossed my legs.","They still ached a little, but the discomfort was now bearable.","Only three days ago, I had screamed like a little girl while trying this.","I had already made tremendous progress.","’Can I finally use mana—or internal energy—now?’","I was genuinely excited.","I was about to wield a mysterious power that normally appeared only in fantasy stories and martial arts novels.","I hoped I would eventually be able to fire palm blasts too.","Palm blasts had always been excellent for keeping enemies at a distance.","Wild Grylls: If I train enough, will I be able to fire palm blasts?","Heavenly Demon: Why do you ask?","Wild Grylls: For ranged attacks?","Heavenly Demon: Do not do that. Only fools waste their energy in such a way.","Wild Grylls: Okay.","He sounds so disappointed. LOL.","Palm blasts are every man’s dream.","There are entire wag\"1\">"]},{"title":"Chapter 25","paragraphs":["Breathing Technique (1)","The continent had countless long-standing \"versus\" debates, not just arguments over who was the strongest.","Elves vs. demons.","Dogs vs. cats.","Summer vs. winter.","West vs. East.","There were many others, but most people avoided discussing them because they tended to cause conflict.","Of course, people only restrained themselves in everyday life.","The Gallery showed no mercy.","Whenever they had the chance, users wasted time fighting over which side was better.","When things occasionally became too heated and turned into outright hatred, the Moderator would personally step in.","And among all these disputes, one subject caused more controversy than any other.","Title: Mana Cultivation Method vs. Internal Energy Cultivation Method","Vote for whichever one you think is better.","Mana Cultivation Method: 50%Internal Energy Cultivation Method: 50%","└ Wow, how are they both exactly fifty percent?","└ None of you know anything. Mana cultivation is obviously better.","└ Cut the crap. How is it better? LOL","└ You’re from the Central Plains, aren’t you?","└ No? I’m from the Messiah Empire.","└ Then you must be a noble.","└ I’m not a noble. I’m a knight. LOL","The debate was none other than mana cultivation methods versus internal energy cultivation methods.","It had continued uninterrupted since ancient times and remained an ongoing controversy even now.","Title: The Origins of Mana Cultivation and Internal Energy Cultivation","The accepted theory is that both were taught according to the teachings of Ares, the Goddess of War and younger sister of Aragon, the God of Magic.","Of her two disciples, one took charge of the West, while the other took charge of the East.","The West gradually fragmented into many different nations, but the East still retains the name \"Central Plains.\"","However, Ares herself developed her technique by analyzing and researching the breathing method of her older brother, Aragon.","So technically, both are basically versions of Aragon’s breathing technique.","That concludes today’s mythology lesson!","└ Was Ares pretty?","└ You lunatic, LOL. Do you want to get arrested for blasphemy?","└ This is the Gallery anyway. LOL. So, was she pretty?","└ Unfortunately, there are no records saying she was beautiful. Apparently, she always wore a helmet because she was constantly at war.","└ Allfather) According to my research, the prevailing theory is that she was beautiful.","└ What evidence is there?","└ Allfather) Aragon, the God of Magic, once said this: \"She may be my damn little sister, but she is pretty.\"","└ Aren’t they just a completely normal pair of siblings? LOL","└ If a real brother admitted his sister was pretty, that says everything.","└ That suddenly sounds incredibly credible. LOL","└ Allfather) The two of them apparently fought quite often. Whenever they did, mountains were blown away and seas overturned.","└ Holy crap.","└ Gods really are something else...","└ Allfather) And every time, the Chief God smacked them both on the back.","└ So it was just a sibling quarrel on a larger scale. LOL","└ Why do they sound so human? LOL","Just as the myths suggested, mana cultivation methods were dominant in the West, while internal energy cultivation methods were dominant in the Central Plains.","However, as time passed, an interesting theory emerged.","Title: Geography Changed the Fate of Breathing Techniques in the West and East","The West is surrounded above and below by dangerous races—demons, elves, and various others—so it needed to produce as many capable fighters as possible.","That was why easy-to-learn mana cultivation methods were spread as widely as possible to strengthen the overall military force.","The problem was that this also made it easy for undesirable people to learn mana cultivation.","As a result, whenever a rebellion broke out, there were frequent cases of peasants beating knights half to death.","This was also one of the reasons the Western nations fragmented into their current state.","Meanwhile, in the East—in other words, the Central Plains—the great families tightly controlled their internal energy cultivation methods.","Their culture was also extremely conservative, and the geography was favorable enough that they faced relatively few internal or external threats.","Therefore, internal energy cultivation methods were taught only to trusted individuals, while most peasants did not even know what they were.","The academic consensus is that geography caused mana cultivation and internal energy cultivation to develop separately.","└ Oh. Knowledge gained.","└ A lot of people in the East use mana cultivation these days. Is it because of increased cultural exchange?","└ That too, and because mana cultivation is easier to learn. Its depth still seems relatively shallow, though.","└ Meanwhile, Western nobles tend to use internal energy cultivation methods. That way, they can widen the gap between themselves and commoners.","└ So internal energy cultivation is basically reserved for important people.","└ Yeah, pretty much.","└ Not necessarily. Knights are often taught internal energy cultivation methods too.","Mana cultivation methods were easy to learn but shallow.","Internal energy cultivation methods were difficult to learn but profound.","These were among the most deeply rooted perceptions surrounding the two types of breathing techniques.","They were half true, but also contained many inaccuracies.","Title: The Best Breathing Technique Is Whatever Suits You","Just look at Ash from the Messiah Empire. She reached the position of the strongest using only a mana cultivation method.","└ Isn’t she just an abnormal exception?","└ Yeah, she is. But even if the process is different, isn’t being strong all that matters?","└ Doesn’t the Hero use mana cultivation too?","└ I heard the Holy Kingdom has its own unique internal energy cultivation method for the Hero.","└ In the end, strong people are simply strong.","Title: Upvote If You’ve Ever Gotten Useful Advice from a Mana vs. Internal Energy Argument","I’ll start. LOL","└ Seriously, all kinds of useful tips come out during those arguments. LOL","└ I was stuck at a bottleneck, but thanks to them, I broke through. LOL","└ While whales fight, the shrimp get fat. LOL","└ I hope they keep arguing forever. LOL","Regardless of the method, a strong person was strong.","That was practically an absolute truth.","Even so, neither side could easily back down because the debate involved the pride and history of their respective factions.","That was why the argument turned into a versus match whenever the opportunity arose.","For those who wielded mana, the subject was especially tied to personal pride.","Perhaps because of that, whenever people argued, they often unintentionally revealed all kinds of valuable tips.","There were plenty of users who occasionally spouted nonsense, but most people knew how to filter them out.","Nothing made people expose the limits of their knowledge more easily than a discussion about breathing techniques.","’Oh. Is she finally going to teach him an internal energy cultivation method?’","Ash, the strongest person in the Messiah Empire and the current stay-at-home security guard, became curious.","As usual, she had been lying around while browsing the Gallery.","The Heavenly Demon had begun teaching Wild Grylls an internal energy cultivation method.","At first, Ash did not think much of it.","The Heavenly Demon she knew would never teach an internal energy cultivation method incorrectly.","Even if she truly were a scammer, it would not matter.","The moment Grylls posted, \"The Heavenly Demon was a fraud!\" in the Gallery, the truth would be exposed.","Of course, they also had to consider the possibility that Grylls had no talent, or that the Heavenly Demon lacked the aptitude to teach others.","From Ash’s perspective, she simply had to watch quietly and enjoy the show.","At first, that was what she thought.","└ Wild Grylls) Heavenly Demon, I followed your instructions, but my nose started bleeding.","└ Heavenly Demon) What?!","\"What?!\"","Just as the Heavenly Demon had been shocked, Ash could not help but jump in surprise.","It was extremely rare for someone to suffer a nosebleed while practicing abdominal breathing.","After questioning Grylls in detail, Ash realized something.","’Don’t tell me Grylls is the same...?’","Ash had experienced the exact same phenomenon.","She possessed a constitution that accumulated mana simply by breathing.","Every time she inhaled, several times more mana than an ordinary person’s would gather inside her mana hole—her dantian.","Because of that, merely practicing controlled breathing had been enough to give her nosebleeds, just like Grylls.","At the time, no one had understood what was happening, so the matter had been brushed aside.","After all, it was a phenomenon no one had ever heard of.","Since it happened during the most fundamental stage of training, people initially assumed she simply lacked talent.","However, once she overcame that stage, her growth became explosive.","Ash could say so with certainty because she herself had experienced it.","’Could it be true? Is he really...?’","Ash bombarded Grylls with question after question.","The more she asked, the more she realized that his constitution was similar to hers.","They were not completely identical, of course. Grylls was currently carrying mana accumulated through an elixir.","Even so, they were alike in that a massive amount of mana entered their bodies with every breath.","’Is it because he’s in the Forest of Four Seasons?’","That was probably the most likely explanation.","The mana density in the Forest of Four Seasons was several—or perhaps even dozens of—times higher than in other regions.","It was merely a hypothesis proposed by scholars, but it was highly credible.","\"The existence of a fully mature Mandrake already proves it.\"","Their environments might have been different, but the conditions were similar.","That was why Ash made up her mind.","She would raise Grylls somehow.","Judging by his actions so far, his talent did not seem particularly bad either.","More importantly, he had more than enough reasons to become stronger.","He was in a situation where he had to grasp at any straw he could find just to survive.","’What if he becomes even stronger than me...? Hehehe.’","Ash smiled wickedly.","It was a feeling she had not experienced in a long time.","Everyone she had trained until now had either failed to satisfy her or run away.","Grylls was different.","He was trapped in the Forest of Four Seasons, so there was nowhere for him to flee.","His only way out was to become stronger on his own.","It was perfect.","’First, I should teach him how to break through to the next stage.’","Grylls’s body was currently oversaturated.","When he tried to draw in more mana while in that state, his body had instinctively activated its defensive mechanisms.","Ash had intended to teach him a useful trick to resolve the problem, but an unexpected obstacle appeared.","\"This woman is seriously frustrating.\"","Ash’s beautiful face twisted slightly.","Her expression seemed to be a mixture of dissatisfaction and exasperation.","’Does she really have to be this stubborn?’","The obstacle was the Heavenly Demon.","The moment Ash offered to teach Grylls a breathing technique, the Heavenly Demon began objecting to everything she said.","Her attitude was practically, \"I already claimed Grylls, so stay away from him.\"","’I can understand it, since she’s from the Central Plains...’","People from the Central Plains were extremely sensitive about master-disciple relationships.","They even said that a master was both teacher and parent, while a disciple was no different from one’s own child.","Internal energy cultivation methods were secret arts that would never be taught to someone who was not deeply trusted.","’That must mean she trusts him that much.’","Had the Heavenly Demon stubbornly insisted on some ridiculous argument, Ash would have fought her to the bitter end.","However, the Heavenly Demon refuted Ash’s points one by one with surprisingly sound reasoning.","In the end, Ash chose to take a step back.","Fighting here would not help Grylls in any way.","Even so, they still needed to open a path for him.","That was why she made one final proposal.","└ SwordMaster) Then I’ll only teach Mr. Grylls my techniques until he can circulate his mana. In the Central Plains, you call it energy circulation and breathing, right?","└ Heavenly Demon) If thou merely intendest to aid him through energy circulation and breathing, then this lady has no objection. However, this lady shall be the one to teach him the mnemonic verses that follow.","└ SwordMaster) I have no intention of going that far either.","Ash was not lying.","That was what she said aloud, at least.","Internally, she had other plans.","Internal energy cultivation methods were difficult.","Extremely difficult.","The process was identical for both types of breathing techniques until one reached mana circulation.","However, a large difference appeared in the mnemonic verses that followed.","Unlike mana cultivation methods, internal energy cultivation methods contained rather philosophical teachings.","For example, while a mana cultivation method might simply instruct the practitioner to direct mana toward a specific area, internal energy cultivation methods were far more complicated.","’The water rising from the valley flows into the sea... Ugh, how frustrating.’","However, they did not have only disadvantages.","Just as carp raised in a river grew differently from carp raised in a lake, breathing techniques worked in a similar way.","Mana cultivation methods were severely lacking when it came to attaining \"enlightenment,\" while internal energy cultivation methods were not.","Their mnemonic verses contained various insights, making it easier to advance to the next stage.","└ Wild Grylls) Is everything the same up to that energy circulation and breathing part?","└ Heavenly Demon) Indeed. However, didst thou not say that thou hadst already sent internal energy into thy middle and upper dantians as well? That is what this lady heard earlier.","└ Wild Grylls) I’m not sure about that part, but some strange energy passed through my heart and brain, then spread throughout my entire body. After that, it returned to my lower abdomen.","└ Heavenly Demon) How peculiar. Perhaps fortune truly arose from disaster, for those pathways have already opened. It may be that thou possessest potential comparable to this lady’s own.","└ Wild Grylls) Does that mean I’ll be able to shoot hurricane-level palm strikes from my hands too?","└ Heavenly Demon) Good grief.","└ Heavenly Demon) For now, it would be best for thee to begin energy circulation and breathing. Listen carefully to the advice of this lady and that jagged stone.","└ Wild Grylls) I’ll take it to heart.","└ SwordMaster) Surely that \"jagged stone\" isn’t referring to me, right?","└ Heavenly Demon) At least thou seemest to possess a conscience.","\"Pfft!\"","Ash burst out laughing.","For the Heavenly Demon to react with such utter exasperation...","That only proved how absurd Grylls could be.","Still, it was nice to see him staying positive.","’She’s not wrong.’","Ash nodded inwardly.","However, she had no intention of giving up.","Sooner or later, Grylls would come looking for a mana cultivation method.","’He’ll definitely complain that internal energy cultivation is too difficult.’","Grylls was an ordinary person.","A polite ordinary person, but ordinary nonetheless.","By Ash’s standards, ordinary people—peasants, in other words—were people who had barely managed to learn how to read.","She did not know much about Grylls’s upbringing, but she already knew it had not been a good one.","His parents had died in an accident, leaving him to live alone.","In that kind of environment, he must have been too busy trying to survive.","There was a high chance he had never received a proper education.","That meant an internal energy cultivation method would probably be difficult for him to understand properly.","’He claims he came from another world, but could that possibly be true?’","That kind of character setting was extremely common in the Gallery.","He claimed that a single bomb from his world could destroy an entire city.","Who would believe something like that?","Apparently, Ash’s concerns had been unfounded.","Whether Grylls’s stomach was unusually weak or unusually healthy, situations like this happened quite often.","└ Heavenly Demon) Energy circulation and breathing is simple. Thou needest only repeat what thou experienced earlier.","└ SwordMaster) The same thing as before might happen again, so you should leave a longer interval between each breath.","└ Heavenly Demon) It would be best to endure it even if thy stomach begins to hurt. If thou art careless, thou mayest fall prey to an inner demon.","└ Wild Grylls) It’s a natural bodily function. You can suffer qi deviation because of that?","└ Heavenly Demon) Of course. There was once a fool who fell into qi deviation merely because someone asked him how to breathe.","└ Wild Grylls) What kind of idiot does that...?","Ash and the Heavenly Demon shared various useful tips through private comments.","Grylls appeared to begin the breathing exercise after reading them, because he stopped replying.","For a very long time.","More than ten minutes passed without a single comment.","Just as Ash grew anxious and prepared to leave another reply—","└ Wild Grylls) Ah, damn. My stomach suddenly started hurting really badly... I’ll keep going.","└ Seriously, his stomach hurts whenever he gets the chance. LOL","└ What a poop machine. LOL","It might have sounded ridiculous, but this was actually a well-known issue.","Mana circulation—energy circulation and breathing—required an extraordinary degree of concentration.","Even someone speaking to the practitioner could easily break that concentration.","└ Wild Grylls) I’ll keep trying for now. How long did you say I should continue?","└ Heavenly Demon) Until thou feelest the internal energy circulating throughout thy entire body.","└ SwordMaster) The Heavenly Demon is right.","└ Wild Grylls) Okay. Thank you.","For the first time in her life, Ash encountered an impossible problem.","\"...What kind of nonsense is this?\"","The Heavenly Demon apparently felt the same way."]},{"title":"Chapter 26","paragraphs":["Breathing Technique (2)","With the help of the Heavenly Demon and SwordMaster, I somehow managed to sense mana.","It worked fairly well when I treated it as simply repeating the phenomenon I had experienced at the beginning.","But the problem came afterward.","Every time the mana completed a full circuit after starting from my lower abdomen, my stomach began to hurt.","It might have been manageable once or twice, but the pain struck every single time the mana completed a circuit, making it impossible to endure.","It was so bad that I wondered whether I needed to build a separate toilet nearby. Going somewhere far away every time was difficult.","’Why am I sweating so much?’","I did not feel particularly exhausted, yet sweat was pouring from my entire body.","And it was not ordinary sweat.","It was pitch-black.","It looked like the filthy grime-water I had only ever heard people describe.","\"Ugh!\"","The smell was horrible too.","I nearly threw up.","It was as though every kind of waste imaginable had been mixed together.","\"Kyuueeek! Kyuueeeek!\"","Wonmo, whose sense of smell was far sharper than mine, was practically having a seizure.","The moment he caught the scent, he moved as far away from me as possible.","Judging by the way he had wedged himself into a corner of the cave and was growling, the smell must have been truly unbearable.","It seemed I would have to wash myself again.","Wonmo might kick me out of the cave otherwise.","The sun had already set, but sleeping like this might make me sick.","’What in the world is happening?’","I filled the tub with water and lit a fire beneath it.","It would take too long to wait for the water to boil, so I climbed in immediately.","The moment I submerged myself, the refreshing chill unique to stream water spread throughout my body.","After letting out a groan of relief, I decided to ask the Gallery for help.","Title: Is Mana Circulation Normally Like This?","Wild Grylls","I’m circulating mana like you advised, but every time it completes one full circuit, I need to take a dump. Is this normal?","└ Heavenly Demon) This is the first time this lady has heard of someone needing to relieve himself whenever he practices energy circulation and breathing.","└ SwordMaster) Same here. Isn’t there simply something wrong with your intestines?","└ Wild Grylls) I haven’t eaten anything. And it’s not even diarrhea.","└ Ugh. Disgusting.","└ I’m eating curry, and you’re talking about poop.","└ The truth is, you’re eating poop that tastes like curry. LOL","└ Oh, come on—","It was admittedly a filthy topic, but I was being serious.","Had it been diarrhea, I could have understood it to some extent.","That would have meant I was sick.","But it was not, so I could not help becoming suspicious.","The only thing I had eaten until now was fasting pills.","Still, I explained that the two seemed to have a complementary relationship, so it was probably better to take care of my body.","└ Heavenly Demon) The only explanation that immediately comes to mind is that thy body is expelling accumulated impurities.","...Is there perhaps something wrong with thy body?","└ Wild Grylls) Well, I’m not a pig, at least.","To be honest, my body was close to being overweight.","I was neither skinny nor noticeably fat.","However, because I had lived almost entirely on instant noodles to save money, I had probably accumulated a fair amount of visceral fat.","└ Heavenly Demon) Aside from that, are there any other symptoms?","└ Wild Grylls) I’m sweating black liquid, and it smells horrible.","└ Heavenly Demon) It truly does seem that impurities are being expelled from thy body.","└ Wild Grylls) Is that a good thing?","└ Heavenly Demon) It goes beyond merely being good. It is abnormal. Normally, one must reach at least the Supreme Realm before such a thing occurs.","└ Wild Grylls) It isn’t bad, right?","└ Heavenly Demon) It is not bad, but just in case, it would be best for thee to focus only on energy circulation and breathing for the time being.","└ Heavenly Demon) Considering what happened whenever thou consumed the fasting pills, that is the only explanation this lady can think of at present.","└ SwordMaster) Or it may genuinely be caused by your constitution.","└ Wild Grylls) Does the same thing happen when fat people learn breathing techniques?","└ If that were true, I would have learned one ages ago. LOL","└ You can become healthy just by breathing? I’d start immediately. LOL","Apparently, learning a breathing technique did not alter one’s physique.","Changing the body’s shape fell under external cultivation, while breathing techniques belonged to internal cultivation, or something along those lines.","In the end, my training came to a halt at mana circulation.","They said they would teach me the mnemonic verses later.","I had no reason to object, so I accepted it without complaint.","My stomach hurt every time I completed a circuit of mana.","There was nothing I could do about that.","’It isn’t nutrients being expelled instead of impurities, is it?’","The thought made me anxious enough to want another fasting pill.","However, doing that might make my Johnson explode, so it was probably better to resist.","\"Whew.\"","Why did nothing ever go according to plan?","Then again, the real problem was being dropped into this damn forest in the first place.","After lamenting my situation for a while, I raised my head and looked at the sky.","The night sky was breathtaking, embroidered with countless stars.","’...Right. There’s no need to rush.’","The water was gradually warming.","I scrubbed every part of my body thoroughly with soap and finished washing.","I planned to dispose of the water left in the tub the next day.","It was too dark to do so safely now.","After drying myself completely with a towel, I browsed the Gallery while waiting for my hair to dry.","Even late at night, the Gallery remained lively.","Most of it was overflowing with pointless posts.","[Gallery User Is Screwed in Real Time]","[I Really Want to Quit My Job]","[This Counts as a Blue Ocean, Right?]","[The River Water Is Warm These Days]","[Those Damn Elves Planted Trees Again]","[EMERGENCYYYY!]","It was all like this.","I was so accustomed to it that I had even begun to feel fond of it.","After browsing the Gallery for a while, I uploaded a simple post.","As always, it was the post that marked the end of my day.","Countless comments appeared immediately, but I skimmed through them and closed the Gallery.","Perhaps because I had learned a breathing technique today, sleepiness overwhelmed me.","’Where should I go tomorrow? Repair work? Breathing practice? Exploration?’","Whatever I chose, one thing was certain.","I would suffer.","Before closing my eyes, I checked on Wonmo.","He was lying right beside me, preparing to sleep.","At least having him around made me feel less lonely.","’I’ll have to gather plenty of wood, even if only for the money.’","I slowly closed my eyes.","As drowsiness washed over me, my thoughts stopped functioning properly.","I had worked hard today, so I should rest comfortably for tomorrow.","’I’ll be able to get out... right?’","I held on to the hope that was gradually fading away.","***","Sleep was extremely important to every animal.","Humans were no exception.","The desire for sleep far surpassed both hunger and sexual desire.","Failing to sleep properly was enough to ruin the entire following day.","Conversely, a full night of deep sleep meant waking up feeling more refreshed than ever.","Title: Another Strong and Energetic Morning!","Wild Grylls","If anyone asks who I am, I’m Wild Grylls!","└ Heavenly Demon) Thou art awake. Is there anywhere in thy body that feels uncomfortable?","└ Wild Grylls) Not at all. I actually feel much more refreshed than usual.","└ SwordMaster) It’s probably because of the breathing exercise. It should be even more effective if you do it as soon as you wake up.","└ Heavenly Demon) It is likely due to the breathing exercise. It would be beneficial to practice once before sleeping and once after waking.","└ Heavenly Demon) Thou insolent wretch. This lady was about to say that first.","└ SwordMaster) You were too slow.","└ Heavenly Demon) Faster is not always better. Accuracy is what matters.","└ SwordMaster) I agree with that part, but speed is more important.","└ Heavenly Demon) Those who pursue speed are the ones who fall into qi deviation.","└ Starlight Princess) You’re awake. Does anything hurt?","└ Wild Grylls) Not really. You’re truly all right now, aren’t you?","└ Starlight Princess) Yes. I went outside the estate and ran as soon as I woke up.","└ Wild Grylls) You really have recovered.","└ So Grylls is the only one left now?","└ What will poor Grylls do all alone? LOL","└ Will he break the young lady’s record?","└ Starlight Princess) You people are truly awful. I’ll help make sure he does not break that record, so please do not worry too much.","The Heavenly Demon and SwordMaster began bickering first thing in the morning, while the now-healthy Starlight Princess left a comment of her own.","I tried to remember how many recovery-wishing posts I had uploaded for the Starlight Princess.","As far as I could recall, it had been around 110 days.","That was roughly three or four months.","Would I be able to escape by then?","’At that point, I won’t be adapting anymore. I’ll just be living here.’","I browsed the Gallery for only a little while before checking on Wonmo.","He was still a baby, so even though I had woken up, he remained fast asleep.","Moving around carelessly might wake him, so I checked the auction house first.","’Let’s see... The things I listed yesterday...’","The items I had put up yesterday were the owlbear’s corpse and some wood.","I had listed both through bidding.","Because of the brutal fees, auctions were structured so that the seller usually ended up losing out.","But fees or not, selling them mattered more to me, so I was simply curious.","[Owlbear Corpse: 200 taels of silver]","[Wood from the Forest of Four Seasons: 10 gold]","\"Oh?\"","They had fetched surprisingly high prices.","The wood was valuable enough, but the owlbear’s price was especially impressive.","Silver taels were the currency of the Central Plains, and I had heard that one tael of silver was roughly equivalent to ten gold.","That meant the owlbear’s corpse was worth around two thousand gold.","’Why is it so expensive? Because of the gallbladder?’","An owlbear was still a kind of bear, so its gallbladder was probably valuable.","Even if that was not the reason, I did not care as long as it sold for a high price.","’The wood is pretty expensive too.’","Ten gold every time I chopped down a tree?","I was confident I could become an environmental criminal.","’Though I’d probably wreck my body first.’","At the very least, I would need to become strong enough to fell a tree with a single swing of an axe.","Until then, I planned to avoid logging purely for money.","’I need the wood for the barricade anyway.’","After roughly organizing what I needed to do, I sat down cross-legged.","Following the advice of the Heavenly Demon and SwordMaster, I began breathing.","Once in the morning, once at noon, once in the evening, and once before bed.","Apparently, practicing about four times a day was standard.","There was one exception.","Whenever one consumed an elixir.","Since the elixir’s energy had to be properly gathered and refined, circulation was absolutely necessary.","’Then do I have to do this every time I eat?’","The fasting pills were said to be equivalent to elixirs, so it was probably mandatory.","I closed my eyes and practiced the breathing technique just as I had learned the day before.","’Starting from the lower abdomen and making one full circuit through the entire body...’","At first, controlling the mana had been difficult, but after that it became easier.","The problem was that every completed circuit caused my stomach to hurt sharply.","I was worried that the same thing might happen today.","’Through the heart and head, then back to the lower abdomen.’","The Heavenly Demon had told me that it was dangerous for a beginner to pass energy through the heart and head.","Apparently, those pathways could normally be opened only after one reached a certain level.","Yet mine had opened from the very beginning.","I had suffered a nosebleed because of it, but I had never fallen into any truly dangerous situation.","’Back to the lower abdomen.’","The mana that had circulated through my entire body returned to my lower abdomen.","Unlike yesterday, my stomach did not hurt at all.","Perhaps everything that needed to be expelled had already left my body.","I completed several more circuits before slowly ending the exercise.","\"Whew.\"","I exhaled and gradually opened my eyes.","The first thing I saw was a pair of bright golden eyes.","As I stared into them, the furry creature tilted its head.","\"Kyu?\"","It was Wonmo.","He must have watched me the entire time I was breathing.","The fact that he had not disturbed me showed that he was quite perceptive.","I stared at Wonmo for a moment, then chuckled and asked,","\"Are you hungry?\"","\"Kyu!\"","\"It almost feels like you understand everything I say.\"","\"Kyu?\"","\"Maybe not?\"","Either way, it did not matter.","I bought a suitable piece of meat from the auction house.","When I gave it to Wonmo, he devoured it with great enthusiasm.","He might be thirsty too, so I decided to give him some water.","Drip, drip, drip—","\"Hm?\"","But the water was barely flowing.","It was coming out, but the pressure was far too weak.","Something must have happened to the hose overnight, or perhaps there had been some change in the river.","\"What a pain.\"","I was not going up there immediately.","Water was still coming out, at least.","I gave Wonmo some water and ate a fasting pill for breakfast.","From now on, I would eat one per meal instead of three.","The bitterness was exactly the same even with just one.","One might actually be better.","’I can test it right away, can’t I?’","The moment I activated the cultivation method, a different reaction occurred.","Something clumped together inside me broke apart and merged with the mana.","That dissolved substance was probably the energy of the fasting pill.","I circulated the mana in that state.","Nothing changed dramatically.","My stomach did not hurt, and I felt completely fine.","’Maybe my body got used to them because I ate too many before.’","That could be it.","In any case, breakfast was done, so it was time to go repair the hose.","I equipped my sword and shield, then looked at Wonmo.","As though he knew I was leaving, he stared back at me.","\"You have to stay here. Got it?\"","\"Kyu.\"","\"Oh, and if your stomach hurts, do it outside. Don’t poop inside the cave.\"","\"Kyu.\"","Wonmo answered adorably.","His response sounded almost as if he understood.","Even if he did not, there was no need to rush.","I could potty-train him gradually.","After petting Wonmo several times, I stepped outside the cave.","’Do the sword and shield feel lighter? Or am I imagining it?’","Perhaps it was because I had slept well, but both weapons felt lighter than before.","Not only that, my entire body felt remarkably good.","The change was so sudden that I could not help thinking of the internal energy cultivation method I had practiced yesterday.","Still, it might only be temporary.","I should not get my hopes up too much.","’I wish I felt like this every day.’","With that thought, I headed toward the river.","When I arrived at the place where I had set up the hose, what I saw was—","Splash! Splash!","\"What is that now?\"","A single red fish was completely blocking the waterway.","’It looks like Magikarp.’","That was more or less what it resembled."]},{"title":"Chapter 27","paragraphs":["Thief (1)","I stared at the red fish completely blocking the channel.","I had placed stones around the channel to control the current.","Since I had dug the makeshift waterway myself with a shovel, it was not very deep.","It seemed the fish had entered the channel by sheer bad luck and then failed to escape.","The current itself was extremely strong, and its body fit the passage almost perfectly, so getting back out would have been difficult.","’Why is it so huge?’","It was large enough to fill the entire channel.","When I first saw it, I thought it was a catfish rather than an ordinary fish.","However, aside from its red body, it looked like a perfectly normal fish.","Most fish were relatively narrow, but even this one’s width was enormous.","I would need both hands to lift it.","I did not know much about fish, but I could say with certainty that it was not a catfish.","’It should be safe to eat, right?’","I watched the fish as it continued to thrash around.","It desperately flopped about in an attempt to escape, but unfortunately, the water was too shallow.","Judging by the way its mouth protruded above the surface and opened and closed repeatedly, it seemed to be having trouble breathing.","Flop! Flop! Flop!","\"You’re pretty strong too.\"","I wrapped both arms around the violently struggling fish and lifted it.","It was nearly as large as my torso, making it difficult even to keep my balance.","It would be troublesome if it managed to leap back into the river, so I moved as far away from the water as possible.","For now, I planned to carry it back to the cave with both hands and keep it inside the tub.","’I should run, just in case.’","Running into a wild animal along the way would be a serious problem.","If that happened, I would use the fish as bait and escape.","Fortunately, nothing like that occurred, and I returned safely.","\"Kku?\"","\"No. You already ate.\"","Wonmo immediately showed interest when he saw me carrying the fish.","I pushed him back and placed the fish inside the tub.","Since the tub was empty, I did not forget to fill it with water.","Once I added water, the red fish finally calmed down somewhat.","Seeing it like this made its size even more impressive.","The tub was normally large enough for either Wonmo or me to bathe in, yet the fish nearly filled it by itself.","Title: Caught a Monster","Wild Grylls","(Photo of a red fish about the size of a shield)","The water wasn’t flowing properly through the hose today, so I went upstream and found this thing blocking it.","It’s seriously huge.","I already ate breakfast, so I’m planning to have this guy for lunch.","Looks like I’ll finally get to feast again after a long time. Haha.","└ Heavenly Demon) Oh my. It is indeed enormous. Judging only by its size and color, it is comparable to a Sunfire Carp.","└ Wild Grylls) What’s that?","└ Heavenly Demon) A spiritual creature containing the energy of the sun. It is exceedingly rare. However, this lady merely said that it looks similar. The chances of it truly being one are low.","└ Wild Grylls) How do I check whether it’s real?","└ Heavenly Demon) Thou shouldst first determine whether it possesses an inner core.","└ Seriously, a spiritual creature appears every time he does anything. LOL","└ Is that actually a Sunfire Carp?","└ Who knows? Grylls has to check.","└ Wasn’t there something similar to a Sunfire Carp too?","└ Heavenly Demon) If thou art referring to the Ten-Thousand-Year Fire Carp, then yes. As the name suggests, it is a carp that has lived for ten thousand years.","└ Starlight Princess) In the past, I would have told you to cut it open immediately, but there is no need for that anymore.","└ By \"the past,\" don’t you mean yesterday?","└ Starlight Princess) It feels like the distant past to me. Every day felt like an entire year.","└ I guess it could feel that way.","└ Maybe it feels like she was born again?","└ Waaah. I’ve been reborn. Feed me.","An inner core—wasn’t that something similar to the way oysters produced pearls?","I was not entirely sure, but I imagined it had effects similar to an elixir.","Of course, I did not truly believe this fish was a spiritual creature.","Even if it was, I did not care.","I had already decided that it would be today’s lunch.","└ Starlight Princess) You people never change. You are all such idiots~","But right now, it was my lunch.","No matter what anyone in the Gallery said, this fish was going to become my meal.","That meant it would probably be better to spend the morning repairing the shelter rather than exploring.","Wonmo might eat the fish while I was gone.","Even now, he was staring intently at the metal tub containing it, clearly waiting for an opportunity.","\"Hey!\"","I warned Wonmo just as he was about to reach for the fish.","Wonmo looked up at me with eyes so wide they were practically bulging.","His expression seemed to ask what he had done wrong.","His innocent face made him look even cuter.","\"You can’t eat that. I’ll give you honey after lunch.\"","\"Kyu.\"","\"That’s right. Our Wonmo is such a good boy.\"","I stroked Wonmo’s head several times and looked around.","If I wanted to build a defensive wall, clearing the trees had to come first.","Perhaps because of that, my chest already felt tight.","How long would it take me to clear all of them?","’They say small efforts eventually become a mountain. I have to do it.’","Grumbling inwardly, I walked toward a tree.","Why did it have to be so thick?","Still, I felt good today.","I gripped the axe tightly and swung it with all my strength.","After swinging it several times before, I had apparently learned the proper technique, allowing me to use the strength of my waist more smoothly.","Crack!","\"Huh?\"","The moment the axe struck the tree, a puzzled sound escaped my mouth.","The reason was simple.","The situation was far too different from yesterday.","Yesterday, I had needed to hack at the tree repeatedly before the axe could barely penetrate its surface.","Today was different.","The axe blade sank deeply into the trunk.","Even the sound was different.","’What is this? Is this tree weaker than yesterday’s?’","The axe could not have changed overnight.","I was in unusually good condition today, and perhaps this tree was also weaker.","That still did not answer all my questions, but since the situation benefited me, I decided not to dwell on it.","’A good thing is a good thing.’","Crack! Crack! Thunk!","After striking the tree about three more times, I examined the middle of the trunk.","Amazingly, I had almost cut straight through its center.","It looked as though the tree would fall if I only chopped the opposite side.","’Already?’","Until yesterday, I had spent the entire day swinging an axe just to cut down a single tree.","Then I had encountered the owlbear and nearly lost my life.","It was difficult to dismiss all these doubts by simply saying that this was a different tree or that I happened to feel better today.","However, there was one obvious difference between yesterday and today.","’Is it really because of the breathing technique?’","That seemed highly likely.","It was the only thing that had changed since yesterday.","There was no downside to becoming stronger anyway.","In an environment like this, physical strength was especially important.","’I’ll have to practice even harder from now on.’","It was amazing that a single breathing technique could shorten my working time this much.","What a strange world.","The world was a fitting mixture of fantasy and martial arts, and it was filled with superhumans capable of blowing up mountains.","Yet these people refused to believe that a single bomb could wipe out an entire city.","Their very existence was basically equivalent to a nuclear warhead.","’I really am curious about the outside world.’","The world shown through the Gallery was narrow.","It was also extremely subjective.","Though the poor reputation of Albenheim, the elven nation, seemed to be universal across every country.","After letting my thoughts wander, I moved to the opposite side of the tree.","If I chopped only this side, the tree should fall in the direction I wanted.","Crack! Crunch! Creak!","After several swings, the tree began to sway.","I checked the direction and shoved it with my foot.","The towering tree slowly began to fall with a loud creak.","Boom!","I had felled an entire tree in less than ten minutes.","The work speed was absurdly fast.","I stared at the fallen tree and checked my condition.","I was slightly tired, but not enough to need a break.","’I’ll do a little more before resting.’","After cutting down one more tree, I finally began to feel somewhat tired.","But it was only a sense of fatigue.","Cutting down another tree would not have been too difficult.","In the end, I felled three trees in total and finished listing them at the auction house.","’The area is starting to open up.’","Perhaps because I had cut down four trees in total by now, the space around the cave had become noticeably wider.","I smiled with satisfaction for a moment before entering the cave to take a proper rest.","Huff... huff...","When I entered, Wonmo was taking a nap.","As I had mentioned before, Wonmo was still a baby.","He would probably sleep most of the day.","’The fish is still fine too.’","It remained quiet inside the metal tub, no longer thrashing around.","I set down the axe and accessed the Gallery to see whether anything had happened while I was working.","Nothing particularly notable stood out, but one thing caught my attention.","’The Moderator has been less active.’","The Moderator, who managed the Gallery, had been unusually inactive.","Normally, posts containing explicit images, grotesque pictures, or excessively abusive language would be deleted immediately, and the users responsible would be banned.","[Photos of Older Sisters]","[All Elves Should Die]","[Warning: Graphic—Photo of My Hand]","Those posts were still up even though ten minutes had passed since they were uploaded.","Normally, they would have been removed instantly.","The users saw this as an opportunity and began unleashing their desires without restraint.","Pretending not to care, I discreetly opened one of the posts too.","Since I was stranded in the wilderness with nothing around me, the Gallery was my only source of entertainment.","Of course, it was not an urgent need.","It was merely something pleasant to look at.","I was too busy struggling to survive to have time for anything beyond that.","[Mr. Grylls, Please Read This.]","After refreshing the page several times, a title caught my eye.","’Allfather?’","Normally, I might have ignored it, but the author was a familiar named user.","I opened it immediately.","Title: Mr. Grylls, Please Read This","Allfather","The item I promised you is ready. Please initiate the trade whenever it is convenient.","It seemed the medicine he had mentioned before was finally complete.","The medicine made from the Golden Poison Frog.","He had said that consuming it would permanently grant resistance to poison, so I absolutely needed it.","└ Wild Grylls) Have you finished the medicine you mentioned before?","└ Allfather) Yes. I have prepared enough for ten days. I believe I will need more specimens for the remainder.","└ Wild Grylls) I’ll send you another Golden Poison Frog as soon as I catch one.","└ Allfather) Thank you. I shall await it.","If I gained resistance to poison, my chances of survival would increase dramatically.","To accomplish that, I would need to hunt another Golden Poison Frog.","I had already rested at just the right time, so I picked up the crossbow resting against the wall.","The arrows I had embedded in the owlbear’s head last time were still in perfect condition.","’It really is strange.’","I had been in such a hurry at the time that I listed the entire corpse at the auction house with the arrows still stuck in its head.","However, the arrows apparently had not been considered part of the corpse, because they had fallen out on their own.","I had nearly lost the arrows and harpoon bolts that I had worked so hard to obtain.","Creak—","I pulled back the crossbow string.","It drew back easily.","Before, I had needed to use all my strength.","Now, all it took was gritting my teeth slightly.","’My strength really has increased.’","That confirmed it.","I had not simply happened to choose weaker trees.","My physical strength had genuinely increased.","All because of a single breathing technique.","The change was so dramatic that I felt more confused than impressed.","It would be best to post about it in the Gallery soon and ask the Heavenly Demon or SwordMaster for advice.","’Everything is ready...’","I checked on Wonmo, who was sleeping soundly, and the fish inside the metal tub.","There did not seem to be any problems.","All I had to do now was hunt the Golden Poison Frog.","Just in case, I also took my sword and shield with me.","I did not forget to put several fasting pills in my pocket either.","After finishing all my preparations, I stepped outside the cave.","’Surely no thief will break in, right?’","With that pointless thought in mind, I headed toward the river.","***","It was after Grylls had left for the river to hunt.","The only sounds inside the cave were the occasional splashing of the fish and the soft breathing of the adorable baby owlbear.","Aside from those noises, the surroundings of the cave were perfectly still.","Birdsong could occasionally be heard, but it was nothing worth paying attention to.","Rustle—","At that moment, a sound came from between the dense trees.","At first, it seemed like nothing more than the wind.","But it was not.","Slowly—","An animal emerged from between the closely packed trees.","Its arms were unusually long compared to its short legs.","Long, vicious claws extended from the tips of its hands.","The creature, covered from head to toe in fur, moved forward very slowly.","Extremely slowly.","Using its long arms to support itself against the ground like a gorilla, it headed toward a very clear destination.","Splash! Splash!","The metal tub containing the fish.","Its advance was painfully slow, but no one was standing guard.","No matter how long it took, it would eventually reach the tub.","The animal moved with the same leisurely pace suggested by its relaxed-looking face.","\"What are you?\"","That was, had Grylls not returned after realizing he had forgotten the antidote.","The animal had nearly reached the metal tub when it heard his voice and turned its head.","Even the act of turning its head was unbearably slow.","Standing face-to-face with the unexpected thief, Grylls muttered quietly,","\"...A sloth?\""]},{"title":"Chapter 28","paragraphs":["Thief (2)","A sloth.","An animal whose name was associated with both trees and laziness.","True to its name, it was famous for how painfully slow every one of its movements was.","Apparently, sloths were so slow that even zoologists who had studied them for two years became frustrated enough to give up.","At first glance, that seemed like an enormous disadvantage in the wild, but sloths were surprisingly efficient animals.","It was the beauty of slowness.","Moving slowly meant consuming less energy.","’But this is the Forest of Four Seasons.’","I had no idea whether that philosophy of slowness worked in the Forest of Four Seasons.","Even now, it had come face-to-face with me, yet it was still moving at a leisurely pace.","The thing it had been after was clearly the fish inside the tub.","However, I was not sure whether sloths were omnivores.","This was exactly when the Gallery came in handy.","Title: What Is This Thing?","Wild Grylls","(Photo of a sloth caught trying to steal the fish)","I went up to the river and came back down, and this thing was here.","It looks like I caught it trying to steal my fish. Do sloths eat meat?","└ Heavenly Demon) Its very expression exudes composure. Be careful.","└ ??? You don’t know what a sloth is?","└ She’s telling him to be careful of a sloth. LOL","└ This is ridiculous. LOL","└ Heavenly Demon) Thou fools will regret thy mockery only after being pierced by those vicious claws.","└ Allfather) I did not know sloths lived in the Forest of Four Seasons. They should normally inhabit jungles.","└ Wild Grylls) Sloths don’t eat fish, right?","└ Allfather) Their primary diet consists of leaves. Furthermore, sloths cannot walk and must crawl. Yet that specimen is supporting its body with both arms like a gorilla. It may not actually be a sloth.","└ Wild Grylls) (Video of the sloth moving extremely slowly)","└ Allfather) It is a sloth. What the hell is that thing?","└ Wild Grylls) I don’t know either.","└ Even the professor is suffering cognitive dissonance after watching the video. LOL","└ It’s a species even he’s never seen before. Damn.","└ Isn’t this basically a new research subject?","└ Allfather) It certainly is, but please be careful. Every plant and animal inhabiting the Forest of Four Seasons possesses at least one weapon of its own.","Both the Heavenly Demon and Allfather warned me to be careful.","The difference was that Allfather’s warning came from caution toward the unknown, while the Heavenly Demon seemed to be relying on instinct.","Either way, it did not hurt to be careful around this absurdly slow sloth.","’To be honest, I could just catch it.’","It was slow enough that I could grab it with my bare hands.","Still, I had no intention of doing so.","Touching it unnecessarily might expose me to disease or parasites.","Wonmo was fine because I had scrubbed him thoroughly, but this creature was different.","’I should chase it away first.’","Since it had gone after my fish, I had no intention of letting it off without doing anything.","Still, killing it felt a little excessive, so I planned to frighten it away.","\"Shoo. Shoo. Go away.\"","I tapped it lightly with the back of my sword rather than the blade, and the sloth slowly backed away.","Even the act of retreating was so sluggish that watching it made me feel frustrated.","However, that fish was meant to be my lunch.","I could not give it away, even to a sloth.","\"Go eat leaves. That’s what you normally eat, isn’t it?\"","\"You look like you don’t want to. Why not? Go climb a tree. There’s plenty of food up there.\"","The sloth’s perpetually relaxed expression changed slightly.","Its face shifted so subtly that it almost looked annoyed.","It seemed to be saying through its expression, You’re the one who cut down the trees.","If that was really what it meant, then I was sorry.","But I still was not giving it the fish.","\"Making that face won’t help. Hurry up and leave.\"","\"...\"","\"Tsk. This isn’t working.\"","Now, even when I pushed it with the back of my sword, it refused to retreat.","I looked around and picked up a suitable branch.","Poke. Poke. Poke.","When I prodded it with the branch and told it to leave, the sloth finally began backing away again.","Perhaps if I pushed it all the way to a tree, it would return to where it belonged.","Grab—","\"Huh?\"","But the world rarely went the way I wanted.","The sloth caught the end of the branch with one hand.","After a brief moment of surprise, I pulled backward to retrieve it.","Grip—","\"What kind of strength is this...?\"","It would not come free.","The sloth was far stronger than it looked.","Perhaps that was only natural for an animal that spent its life climbing trees. Its arms had to be powerful.","Rather than getting into a pointless contest of strength, it would probably be easier to find another branch.","’Or should I just put on my gloves and pick it up?’","That might actually be better.","The gloves were inside my pocket.","I put them on and moved behind the still-slow sloth.","It barely moved before I got behind it.","Even when I grabbed its back, it reacted no faster.","\"Heave-ho.\"","The moment I lifted it, the sloth’s expression shifted into surprise.","Even its facial expressions changed as slowly as its movements.","It was fascinating that such a relaxed-looking face could make an expression like that.","After carrying the sloth to a tree and setting it down, the matter finally seemed settled.","Now I only had to retrieve the antidote and leave to hunt the Golden Poison Frog.","’Surely it isn’t coming back this way.’","Feeling doubtful, I turned around.","Sure enough, it was approaching me with all its might.","It was moving so earnestly that I almost felt sorry for it.","What was so special about that fish that it was this obsessed?","A sigh escaped me.","’...This won’t do.’","Words—if they could even be called that—were clearly not enough.","I needed to threaten it more convincingly.","After all, this sloth was a thief trying to steal my precious meal.","I aimed the crossbow at the sloth as it carefully crawled toward me.","Killing it outright felt wrong, so I planned to shoot the ground and frighten it.","Slowly... slowly...","’...This is driving me insane.’","I was wasting this much time because of one sluggish animal.","Had I been more ruthless, I would have put a hole through its head already.","However, the sloth had not directly harmed me.","Every animal I had killed until now had threatened my life first.","I aimed the crossbow at the ground and fired far enough away that the sloth would not be hit.","Twang! Thunk!","The bolt shot forward at high speed and embedded itself in the dirt.","The sloth slowly lowered its head.","It stared calmly at the bolt sticking out of the ground, then raised its head again.","Slowly... slowly...","\"This is driving me crazy.\"","What in the world was inside that thing’s head?","Even after all this, it showed no intention of retreating.","In the end, my frustration drove me to ask the Gallery for help.","Title: Someone Tell Me How to Chase This Thing Away","Wild Grylls","(Video of the approaching sloth)","It keeps trying to take my fish.","I picked it up and carried it back to a tree, but it’s still doing this.","I even threatened it with the crossbow, yet it keeps coming. Any advice?","└ Heavenly Demon) What extraordinary perseverance. Thou shouldst learn from it.","└ SwordMaster) Why not just give it the fish? It looks like it’ll keep bothering you otherwise.","└ Wild Grylls) Teachers, I want to eat a proper meal too. Wonmo eats better food than I do.","└ That’s genuinely pitiful. LOL","└ Why the hell is that thing acting like that? Is there something special about the fish?","└ Wild Grylls) I think it’s because I destroyed its home.","└ Why did you destroy its home?","└ Wild Grylls) I cut down a tree, and apparently that was its house.","└ That sloth can talk?","└ Wild Grylls) No, it’s just a hunch. LOL","└ So you were just talking nonsense. LOL","└ Grylls, are you really going to become a man who loses to a sloth?","└ Wild Grylls) No, but killing it feels a bit much.","└ Just kill it and eat it, or feed it to Wonmo. That would be better.","└ Wild Grylls) Does it taste good?","└ I heard it tastes terrible. That’s probably why it survived humans.","└ Allfather) I have never seen a sloth behave like that before... Fascinating.","└ Even you’ve never seen one like this, Professor?","└ Allfather) I do not know much about the Forest of Four Seasons either. Nor would I ever want to go near it.","There was not much useful advice.","Most people simply suggested killing the sloth.","However, sloths supposedly tasted awful, and their hides were worthless, so I would not be able to sell it either.","It might be fine if Wonmo ate it, but dealing with the remains afterward would be troublesome.","’Still, I can’t give it the fish.’","Judging by that idiotic persistence, it would steal the fish eventually, no matter how long it took.","I finally had a chance to eat a proper meal after so long, and they expected me to give it up?","Not a chance.","I loaded another bolt and aimed at the sloth.","This time, I would not shoot the ground.","I intended to make the threat unmistakable.","No matter how slow it was, surely it would understand the danger if a bolt passed right beside its head.","’If I accidentally kill it...’","I would probably feel a little guilty.","I aimed beside the head of the slowly approaching sloth.","The moment it took another step, I pulled the trigger without hesitation.","Twang!","The bolt narrowly grazed past the side of its head.","Despite nearly dying, the sloth’s expression remained as relaxed as ever.","Did it genuinely not realize how close it had come to death, or was even its reaction simply slow?","Its shamelessness was becoming almost comical, and a hollow laugh escaped me.","’This isn’t working.’","I abandoned the idea of frightening it away.","Perhaps it would only come to its senses after I put a hole through its body.","I needed to hunt the Golden Poison Frog, and this had already delayed me far too long.","I steadied myself and aimed at the sloth’s shoulder.","The bolt was already loaded.","All that remained was to fire.","’Don’t come back again.’","I muttered the words inwardly and pulled the trigger.","There was no hesitation.","I had already given it plenty of chances.","Twang!","The bolt shot forward like lightning, heading directly for the sloth’s shoulder.","A single hit had been powerful enough to drive even an owlbear into a frenzy.","Since this creature’s hide was much thinner, the bolt would probably pass straight through it.","At least, that was what should have happened.","Whoosh!","The sloth twisted its body slightly and dodged.","It moved at the very last moment, just before the bolt could strike.","There was nothing slow about it.","Its movement had been astonishingly agile.","\"Huh?\"","Having witnessed it in real time, I could only let out a stupid sound.","What had I just seen?","Had I really watched a sloth dodge a crossbow bolt?","After a brief moment of stunned disbelief, I hurriedly loaded another bolt.","The first time must have been a coincidence.","Perhaps it had moved so slowly that I had simply misjudged its path.","I reassured myself and aimed the crossbow again.","The sloth had already returned to its usual sluggish movements.","Twang!","Another bolt flew.","Swish!","As if to prove the first time had not been an illusion, the sloth dodged again with a burst of lightning-fast movement.","That alone was absurd enough, but what it did next was even more unbelievable.","As though nothing had happened, it resumed its painfully slow approach toward me.","’...This thing is dangerous.’","I narrowed my eyes and raised my guard.","It was absolutely not something I could take lightly.","It had seen the bolts coming and dodged them.","And it had done so with barely any movement.","A bolt launched from a crossbow traveled extremely fast.","Reacting after seeing it was nearly impossible.","Title: Can Anyone Here Dodge an Arrow After Seeing It?","Wild Grylls","Isn’t that extremely difficult?","Heavenly Demon and SwordMaster, please don’t answer.","└ Heavenly Demon) Why art thou excluding this lady?","└ Wild Grylls) Because if I ask you, you’ll probably just say it’s easy.","└ Heavenly Demon) Thou hast come to understand this lady well. How gratifying.","└ SwordMaster) It’s surprisingly easy. You just watch it and dodge.","└ Wild Grylls) Sigh...","└ You don’t really dodge after seeing the arrow. You predict its trajectory.","└ Yeah, and you watch the archer’s hands. That makes it easier than you’d think.","└ Easy, my ass. LOL. It hits you almost the instant the archer releases the string.","└ Most people calling it easy are probably holding shields. LOL","└ You caught me. LOL","└ Why are you asking, anyway?","└ Wild Grylls) The sloth dodged a bolt after seeing it.","└ What?","└ ???","└ What kind of nonsense is that now?","└ Wild Grylls) I wish it were nonsense too.","Even the Gallery agreed that it was difficult.","They said an ordinary human could not visually track an arrow once it left the string.","And when I told them a sloth had done exactly that, none of them believed me.","’I saw it with my own eyes, and I still don’t believe it.’","While I was distracted, the sloth drew even closer.","Judging by the distance, it was now about ten meters away.","At this range, dodging after seeing the bolt should be impossible.","I aimed the loaded crossbow at the sloth.","Now that I knew it was dangerous, there would be no more mercy.","’This time, I’ll aim for the head.’","Without the slightest hesitation, I pulled the trigger.","The instant I did, the sharp bolt shot directly toward the sloth’s head.","At this rate, it would pierce the center of its skull and kill it instantly.","But this was the Forest of Four Seasons.","A place inhabited by every kind of bizarre and extraordinary plant and animal.","Grab!","\"...Holy shit.\"","The sloth caught the bolt aimed at its face with one hand.","It slowly lowered the hand covering its face and stared calmly at me.","Its unbearably relaxed expression seemed to be saying only one thing.","Too slow."]},{"title":"Chapter 29","paragraphs":["Thief (3)","The sloth—or rather, I should start calling it the Speed Sloth now.","The Speed Sloth looked at me with an expression that radiated leisure and quiet disdain.","Oddly enough, I didn’t feel angry.","Instead, my sense of danger shot through the roof.","Snap!","The arrow it had caught in one hand broke cleanly in half.","What worried me far more than that were its claws.","Those vicious, overgrown claws.","The moment those hit me, my life is over.","There was no way I couldn’t be tense.","I don’t know when it’ll attack.","If it possessed that kind of agility, why did it usually move so slowly?","Maybe it was something like this.","\"I knelt only to build up momentum!\"","Ordinary sloths move slowly to conserve energy.","That’s what Allfather had explained.","But surviving in the Forest of Four Seasons probably made that impossible, so perhaps they’d evolved in another direction—","Displaying overwhelming speed only when faced with danger.","It was a surprisingly plausible theory.","This world was seriously insane.","Shuffle... Shuffle...","The Speed Sloth began moving again.","After witnessing that explosive burst of speed earlier, even its sluggish movements looked different now.","It wasn’t slow.","It was composed.","There had been a reason both the Heavenly Demon and Allfather warned me to be careful.","Can people really tell something’s this dangerous just by watching a video?","I wasn’t sure.","But one thing was certain.","Their instincts had been right.","So... how am I supposed to deal with this thing?","I lowered my crossbow.","Even if I fired, it’d either dodge the bolt or catch it with its hand.","There was no point.","Hand-to-hand... honestly, I think I’d lose.","It completely outclassed me in speed.","It had caught an arrow with its bare hand.","Me?","I could barely even follow an arrow’s trajectory with my eyes.","There was no choice but to stay on edge.","The moment I let my guard down, those claws might punch straight through my throat.","...No.","If it wanted to pierce my throat, it would’ve done it already.","That left only two possibilities.","Either this Speed Sloth was a pacifist...","Or it simply had no intention of killing me.","The first option would be great.","The second was potentially even more dangerous.","Something that fast and agile would always be a threat.","...Or maybe it’s just playing with me.","Maybe it was acting so relaxed because it didn’t see me as any threat at all.","As I watched the Speed Sloth slowly approaching, I glanced behind me.","Inside the iron barrel were the fish I’d caught this morning.","Maybe I should just give them to it and let it leave peacefully.","It wasn’t a bad option.","The odds of winning a fight were practically nonexistent.","I’d received an elixir from Starlight Princess, but that only mattered if I wasn’t instantly killed.","If those claws struck a vital spot, the elixir probably wouldn’t save me.","After agonizing over it, I slowly picked up my shield.","Not my sword.","I had a different plan in mind.","Keeping the shield pointed at the creature, I carefully walked toward the iron barrel.","Even then, the Speed Sloth continued approaching at its usual slow pace.","Scrraape... Scrraape...","Before long, I was dragging the heavy barrel full of fish with one hand.","It really seemed like the creature wanted the fish.","The Speed Sloth continued its signature slow approach toward me.","Yeah.","It definitely wanted the fish.","But that only raised another question.","Why?","I’d heard sloths mainly lived on leaves.","So why was it after fish?","Had the animals of the Forest of Four Seasons evolved different diets as well?","Or... is there something special about the fish?","Something the Heavenly Demon had once said suddenly came back to me.","The fish I’d caught resembled spirit beasts —","The kind that possessed internal cores.","I still didn’t know if that was actually true.","After thinking it over, I dragged the barrel all the way inside the cave.","It made quite a racket.","Even so, Wonmo slept through it like nothing had happened.","One of us was facing a life-or-death crisis...","The other was sprawled out sleeping peacefully.","Life really wasn’t fair.","Well... he’s still just a baby.","Meanwhile, the Speed Sloth entered the cave.","There was nowhere left to run.","I gripped my sword and shield, remaining on full alert.","There was only one chance.","Attack the moment it reached for the fish.","I had no idea when those murderous claws might come for my throat.","I intended to finish it before that happened.","\"...\"","Then—","The Speed Sloth suddenly stopped.","It had never stopped before.","Slow, yes.","But never completely still.","Naturally, I found it strange.","The creature stared intently at something.","I followed its gaze.","It was looking...","At the sack containing my fasting pills.","Shuffle... Shuffle...","\"H-Huh?\"","Not the fasting pills.","Anything but those.","Panicking, I rushed toward the sack.","The moment I grabbed it, the Speed Sloth quietly looked up at me.","Tap... Tap...","Without changing its expression, it casually flexed those terrifying claws.","Anyone could tell what it meant.","It wanted one.","And if I didn’t hand one over...","It looked suspiciously like a death threat.","\"...Should I give you one?\"","\"...\"","It simply stared at me.","Honestly, I preferred this.","If its attention had shifted from the fish to the fasting pills...","And I still had plenty of pills left...","Then maybe this wasn’t so bad.","Carefully, I took out a single fasting pill.","\"T-This?\"","\"...\"","Tap... Tap...","\"...You want another one?\"","\"That might be a little diff—\"","Whoosh!","Without a sound—","(Not that it could talk in the first place.)","Its claw stabbed straight into the fasting pill.","Then it slowly carried it to its mouth.","Even that action was agonizingly slow.","Watching it somehow made me nervous.","\"...Hmm.\"","The Speed Sloth slowly moved its jaw as though savoring the flavor.","Even the owlbear—and Wonmo—had spat the fasting pills out immediately because they were so bitter.","Heck, even I only forced myself to eat them to survive.","Never because they tasted good.","Yet this thing carefully chewed every bite.","Its relaxed expression never changed.","Just as I was about to complain that I barely had enough food for myself—","The Speed Sloth’s claw was suddenly inches from my throat.","Had it moved even a little farther...","There would’ve been a gaping hole in my neck.","Every drop of blood in my body turned ice cold.","I hadn’t even seen it move.","Tap... Tap...","As I swallowed hard, the Speed Sloth gestured with its other hand.","The meaning was obvious.","Hand it over... or die.","\"...Ha. Fuck.\"","What a miserable world.","Cursing under my breath, I reluctantly handed over another fasting pill.","Only then did it retract its claws.","After eating the second pill, it looked completely satisfied.","Thankfully, two seemed to be enough.","It didn’t ask for a third.","It also seemed to have completely lost interest in the fish.","I quietly let out a sigh of relief.","Shuffle... Shuffle...","\"Huh? Wait... what are you doing?\"","But the Speed Sloth wasn’t done surprising me.","Without warning...","It started climbing onto me.","It was careful not to stab me with its sharp claws, so it didn’t hurt at all.","\"...\"","\"...\"","Finally—","The Speed Sloth rested its chin on top of my head.","Did it think I was some kind of tree that grew leaves?","I was so dumbfounded that I couldn’t even speak.","I wanted to shake it off, but I couldn’t.","I’d only hurt myself if I tried to force it off.","Those vicious claws alone made it impossible to remove the creature by force.","At least it barely weighed anything.","Strangely enough, it didn’t smell bad either.","If anything, it smelled pleasant.","This thing probably has ticks too...","Still, I should wash it just in case.","I let out a deep sigh.","It hadn’t even been a week, yet I’d already gone through all kinds of bizarre incidents.","There was only one place where I could vent about this.","Title: Getting Mugged by a Sloth in Real Time","Wild Grylls","I’m the registered user who posted the sloth earlier. This bastard ate a fasting pill, then threatened me with its claws and demanded more. TTTT","What a miserable world. Never thought I’d live to see the day I got mugged by a sloth.","└ Heavenly Demon: You yielded merely because it pointed its claws at you?","└ Wild Grylls: This bastard can see and catch arrows... It nearly stabbed me in the throat at that speed too.","└ Heavenly Demon: Hmm. In that case, I can understand to some extent. It may even make an excellent sparring partner.","└ Wild Grylls: You want me to spar with a sloth?;;","└ Heavenly Demon: You said you were slower than the sloth, so it would not be a poor choice.","└ Wild Grylls: Ha...","└ SwordMaster: What’s the sloth doing right now?","└ Wild Grylls: It’s hanging from my back.","└ SwordMaster: What kind of bullshit is that?","└ Wild Grylls: Sounds like bullshit, right? It’s true. I’ll upload a picture later.","└ Never thought I’d hear about a sloth mugging someone and then clinging to them. Hahahaha","└ This is legendary. Hahaha","└ Is that thing even really a sloth?","└ Wild Grylls: I decided to call it a Speed Sloth. ᄋᄋ","└ Speed Sloth. Kekeke","└ Better than Fluffy. Hahaha","└ Wild Grylls: What’s wrong with Fluffy?","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero: It’s lame!","└ The Moderator is here?","└ Appears out of nowhere and drops facts. Hahaha","└ Wild Grylls: Where have you been all this time?","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero: I was being chased, so I had to run away for a while! I’m safe now! Though I still have to sleep outdoors!","└ Ah...","└ Aah...","└ Aaaaah...","└ Wild Grylls: Why not come here instead? It’s surprisingly abundant here.","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero: I’m sorry! The Goddess would never forgive suicide!","└ Wild Grylls: That’s too harsh.","└ Allfather: A Speed Sloth... Perhaps you have discovered an entirely new species. Scholars may take an interest in it.","└ Wild Grylls: Normal sloths have lots of ticks too, right?","└ Allfather: They don’t have ticks. Instead, moths and beetles live in their fur and eat the ticks.","Ah.","Fuck.","└ Allfather: Furthermore, the fungi growing on it are probably protecting it from infection.","└ Wild Grylls: So none of that benefits me in the slightest?","└ Allfather: Correct. It’s filthy. Extremely so.","So I had to wash it somehow.","But I wasn’t sure whether the creature would willingly climb down.","At least it didn’t feel particularly unpleasant.","As I said earlier, it didn’t smell bad either, so it was tolerable.","For now, I guess I’ll have to catch the Golden Frog like this.","I’d catch the Golden Frog, trade with Allfather, and eat fish for lunch.","The sudden appearance of the Speed Sloth had thrown my plans off a little, but things were fine now.","With the Speed Sloth still on my back, I gathered my equipment.","Normally, I would sling the crossbow over my back, but the Speed Sloth was in the way—","Slide.","\"Hm?\"","When I tried to put the crossbow on, the creature quietly shifted aside.","Once the crossbow was secured, it climbed back on top of it.","It really was an intelligent animal.","I’d sensed it when it threatened me earlier, but it seemed to possess fairly high intelligence.","Does it understand what I’m saying, like Wonmo does?","Probably not.","It was likely just smart.","I carefully adjusted the crossbow so that the Speed Sloth couldn’t accidentally pull the trigger.","Perhaps it understood my intention, because it moved toward the front and hung there in a way that wouldn’t interfere with me.","Thanks to that, I ended up face-to-face with it.","Its expression looked undeniably stupid.","And yet this was the same creature that could catch a flying arrow.","The Forest of Four Seasons was truly bizarre.","Hissss...","I was making my way toward the river where the Golden Frog lived when an ominous sound reached my ears.","It sounded like a snake flicking its tongue.","I’d already suffered badly at the fangs of a Steel-Scaled Snake, so I immediately scanned my surroundings.","But I couldn’t see anything.","For a moment, I wondered whether I’d imagined it.","\"Shaaa!\"","Something brown that had clearly looked like a tree branch suddenly opened its jaws wide.","At the same time, its brown body turned green.","Two razor-sharp fangs protruded menacingly from its mouth.","It wasn’t a branch.","It was a venomous snake.","A-A chameleon?!","A snake imitating a chameleon’s camouflage?","What kind of grotesque combination was that?","I was so startled that I failed to react properly.","I’d genuinely mistaken it for a branch, so I hadn’t noticed it at all.","Slash!","However, there was an animal that moved before I did.","It happened so quickly that I couldn’t follow the process.","But I saw the result clearly with my own two eyes.","\"Shaaa! Shaaa!\"","\"...\"","Claws even more vicious than the snake’s fangs had pierced straight through its head.","The venomous snake trembled violently, its skull impaled on the claw.","It wrapped its body around the claw in a desperate attempt to escape, but the effort was pointless.","It was considerably smaller than the Steel-Scaled Snake I’d encountered before.","And the moment its head was pierced, its fate had already been sealed.","Riiip!","The Speed Sloth grabbed the snake with its free hand and pulled hard.","The venomous snake’s head split vertically.","Thud.","The snake was thrown to the ground, still twitching.","Its vertically torn head was utterly revolting.","Just in case, I stabbed it with my sword so it couldn’t bite me.","Before long, the snake’s body went limp.","Its torso occasionally twitched, but there was no doubt that it was dead.","I looked at the Speed Sloth hanging behind me.","As always, it wore its calm, leisurely expression.","It looked so peaceful, as though nothing had just happened.","\"...Want another fasting pill?\"","Node.","The Speed Sloth nodded.","As expected, even that movement was painfully slow."]},{"title":"Chapter 30","paragraphs":["Inner Core (1)","Thanks to the Speed Sloth’s help, I made it to the riverside safely.","The first thing I did after arriving was check the hose.","I looked to see whether another fish had been caught like before, and sure enough, my prediction was right.","Splash! Splash!","\"Another one got caught.\"","Another fish had been trapped in that short span of time.","This one was red too.","It was about the same size as the fish from earlier.","Judging by that, this seemed to be the average size of the fish inhabiting this river.","I’ll deal with this one later.","The Golden Frog was more important right now.","My trade with Allfather came first.","That meant I needed to get the Speed Sloth off my back.","I patted it on the back and asked,","\"Can you get down for a moment? This is urgent.\"","\"...\"","Shuffle... Shuffle...","As though it understood me, the creature slowly climbed down.","Then it stared at me with that stupid-looking face.","It almost felt like it was urging me to hurry up.","That was probably just my imagination.","Time to lure out a Golden Frog.","The one that seemed to be their leader had appeared the moment I dipped my hand into the river.","Would the others react the same way?","I carefully placed my hand in the water.","About three seconds later, I heard a splash from the middle of the river.","\"Croak.\"","A Golden Frog.","It climbed onto a rock in the middle of the river.","It was smaller than the one I’d seen before, but still quite large.","The moment it appeared, I retreated without hesitation.","I also remembered to raise my shield, just in case.","\"Kyaaaak!\"","The Golden Frog tilted its head back.","It even made a sound like it was gathering phlegm.","It looked ready to spit poison.","But I had already moved far away.","The only one still sitting there blankly was the Speed Sloth.","\"Hey! What are you—?!\"","\"Ptooey!\"","Before I could finish shouting, the Golden Frog spat its poison.","A glob of purple mucus shot forward at high speed.","Its target was the Speed Sloth.","The Speed Sloth calmly watched the poison coming toward it.","Then it tilted its head slightly.","Sssssss!","The poison narrowly passed beside its face.","It struck a tree and immediately began melting the bark.","I’d more or less expected it, but its agility was still incredible.","Now.","While the Golden Frog’s attention was focused on the Speed Sloth, I prepared my crossbow.","I loaded a harpoon bolt and aimed at the Golden Frog.","\"Kyaaaak!\"","\"Kyaaak!\"","\"Croooak!\"","Meanwhile, more Golden Frogs climbed onto the rocks.","I had already hidden myself, but the Speed Sloth remained seated there without the slightest concern.","Even if it was the Speed Sloth, dodging several consecutive attacks should be diffic—","\"Ptooey!\"","\"Ptui!\"","\"Ptoo!\"","Whoosh—Whoosh, whoosh!","...Apparently not.","Even though it stayed in the same spot, it avoided every attack merely by twisting its body with effortless ease.","Its expression was so relaxed that it looked like some reclusive master.","Does that bastard have Observation Haki or something?","There was no other explanation.","I let out a breath of disbelief.","Still, that was that, and this was this.","My preparations were complete.","I aimed at one of the Golden Frogs and pulled the trigger.","Twang! Thud!","The harpoon pierced the Golden Frog cleanly, knocking it into the rushing river.","I immediately began pulling the rope.","The other Golden Frogs didn’t attack me in the meantime.","They seemed greatly shocked that one of their companions had been struck.","Of course, that was only my guess.","But judging by the way they all stopped attacking at once, they at least seemed capable of understanding what had happened.","Every creature living in the Forest of Four Seasons was extraordinary in one way or another.","Splash!","Perhaps deciding to retreat, the group of Golden Frogs leaped back into the river.","They probably wouldn’t pose a threat for a while.","All that remained was cleaning up.","I pulled hard on the rope connected to the harpoon.","Previously, it had felt like I was locked in a tug-of-war.","Now, I only needed to exert a little strength.","\"Heave-ho.\"","The Golden Frog I dragged out of the water was quite large.","Not as large as the one I’d caught before, but about the size of a small puppy.","All that remained was trading it to Allfather.","Before that, though, I needed to deal with the fish.","I’ll tie this to my waist for now.","This was something Allfather had taught me.","If purple liquid began pouring out, it meant the poison sac had ruptured.","No purple liquid was leaking right now.","That meant it was safe.","With the frog hunt finished, the only thing left was the fish.","I had no idea what it ate to grow so large.","Today’s haul is generous.","With this, both lunch and dinner were secured.","I lifted the fish, which was still thrashing wildly.","There’s no way I could catch this thing with a fishing rod.","It was so strong that it was still trying to slap me in the face with its fins.","Afraid I might drop it, I hugged the fish tightly with both arms.","Had my strength not increased, I would’ve lost my grip long ago.","Shuffle... Shuffle...","The Speed Sloth climbed onto my back again, completing my preparations to return.","\"It’d be nice if you tasted good, but that’s probably asking too much.\"","Taste didn’t matter.","In my situation, caring about flavor was a luxury.","Besides, I could buy seasoning from the auction house, so it would probably be fine.","Splash!","After returning to the cave, I placed the fish inside the iron barrel.","It was still so powerful that the barrel trembled slightly.","It was probably better not to try catching one of these with a fishing rod.","At this rate, I might end up being the one dragged into the water.","A trap or fish basket seemed like a safer option.","Just looking at the two massive fish made me feel secure and happy.","Time to trade with Allfather.","After organizing my belongings, I made a post in the Gallery.","I wrote that Allfather should send me a trade request if he was online.","[Allfather has sent you a trade request. Would you like to accept?]","It didn’t take long for him to contact me.","I gave the Speed Sloth another fasting pill and accepted the request.","[Allfather: Hello. I saw your post and sent a trade request.]","[Wild Grylls: Hello. I’ll put the item up right away. The poison sac hasn’t ruptured.]","[Allfather: Thank you. This should make my research much easier.]","[Wild Grylls: That’s good to hear. Ah, there’s also something I’m curious about.]","[Allfather: Go ahead.]","[Wild Grylls: The Speed Sloth climbed onto me and refuses to get off. Do you know why?]","[Allfather: Are you referring to the sloth that supposedly caught an arrow?]","[Wild Grylls: Yes. Hard as it is to believe, it really did catch one.]","[Allfather: To be honest, I don’t know either. No such specimen has ever been documented in academia.]","Even Doraemon Allfather didn’t know what species it was.","Just what kind of place was the Forest of Four Seasons?","As I sighed inwardly, Allfather offered his own theory.","[Allfather: Still, I can make a guess. You said in your post that it extorted you?]","[Wild Grylls: It didn’t take money, but it did steal my fasting pills.]","[Allfather: Perhaps it thinks of you as a tree.]","[Wild Grylls: A tree?]","[Allfather: Is it still hanging from you?]","[Wild Grylls: Yes. It doesn’t seem interested in getting off.]","[Allfather: Then yes. To it, you may simply be a tree that produces food.]","[Wild Grylls: That sounds kind of...]","[Allfather: Ridiculous, yet strangely plausible? I think so too.]","Allfather said it exactly as it was.","Even he seemed to find the theory absurd.","Still, it was reasonable enough that there wasn’t any better explanation.","[Allfather: Since it doesn’t seem hostile, keeping it might not be a bad idea.]","[Wild Grylls: I don’t completely dislike it either. I almost got bitten by a snake today, and this guy helped me.]","After chatting about this and that, Allfather and I completed the trade.","I gave him the Golden Frog’s corpse, and he gave me a pill that would increase my resistance to poison.","[Allfather: It would be best to take it after a meal. Proper digestion is important.]","[Wild Grylls: Should I absorb this using the breathing technique too?]","[Allfather: Yes. You can think of it as a kind of inner core.]","An inner core.","I remembered the Heavenly Demon’s explanation.","A crystal formed when energy accumulated inside the body of a spirit beast.","The mention of inner cores made me curious about something, so I asked Allfather.","[Wild Grylls: Have you ever eaten an inner core before?]","[Allfather: I’ve never eaten an inner core, but I have consumed a Dragon Heart.]","[Wild Grylls: What’s that?]","[Allfather: Exactly what it sounds like. The heart of a dragon. It contains an immense amount of mana.]","I had a rough idea of what dragons were.","They were mentioned in the Gallery from time to time.","They were powerful enough to treat humanity as insignificant, though they weren’t completely unrivaled.","More importantly, I’d heard their numbers were so low that they were considered endangered.","Could there be dragons in the Forest of Four Seasons too?","If there were, they’d be disasters incarnate.","I was only a weak human.","How was I supposed to catch something that could fly freely through the sky and breathe fire?","[Allfather: Thank you, as always, for another excellent trade. Feel free to ask me whenever you encounter an unusual animal.]","[Wild Grylls: I saw something that looked like a cross between a chameleon and a snake too.]","[Allfather: What was that?]","[Wild Grylls: I thought it was a tree branch, but it turned out to be a snake. It changed the color of its body in an instant.]","[Allfather: Oh! This place truly is overflowing with fascinating creatures!]","[Wild Grylls: Want to come here?]","[Allfather: This old man’s knees aren’t what they used to be. I’ll have to decline.]","[Wild Grylls: TT]","That was where our conversation ended.","Apparently, even Allfather wanted nothing to do with the Forest of Four Seasons.","Well, who would willingly come to a hellhole like this?","I was lucky, at least.","Most other people trapped here couldn’t even access the Gallery.","\"Hmm.\"","I stared at the pill resting on my palm.","It was round and pale purple.","This was the medicine I’d received from Allfather.","According to his explanation, eating it would grant me resistance to poison.","I should eat lunch first.","I placed the pill in my pocket and walked over to the iron barrel containing the fish.","There were only two fish inside, yet they filled the entire barrel.","How am I supposed to cook these?","I’d lived alone back home, so I knew how to cook.","But that was with ingredients that had already been cleaned and prepared.","I’d never had to butcher a fish myself.","There was only one thing to do in situations like this.","Ask the Gallery.","It was better to gain at least a little knowledge than charge ahead blindly.","Title: Need Help Cleaning a Fish!","Wild Grylls","(Photo of the fish inside the iron barrel)","Anyone have advice? These things are fucking huge too.","└ Professionals pierce the brain with a knife or awl to kill it instantly. If you’re inexperienced, just cut the whole head off.","└ Hit its head with the back of a knife before cutting it. That’ll stun it. Make your move then.","└ Removing the guts is easy. Just cut open the belly.","Since I was inexperienced, I decided to use the method of striking its head first.","I was going to grill it immediately anyway, so there was no need to worry about aging the meat or anything like that.","\"Kyuu.\"","\"Wonmo, wait just a little longer.\"","Wonmo had woken up with perfect timing the moment lunchtime arrived.","Just look at those bright, expectant eyes demanding food.","I wanted to toss him a chunk of meat immediately, but cleaning the fish came first.","I wrapped both arms around one of the fish and lifted it out of the barrel.","Flop! Flop!","The fish thrashed wildly as if demanding that I release it, but that wasn’t happening.","I placed it on the stone slab I’d prepared in advance.","The fish was so large that even the broad slab looked small beneath it.","They said to hit the head hard, right?","Because of its size, an ordinary knife wouldn’t be enough.","This was exactly when I needed the Heavenly Demon’s sword.","I wasn’t using the blade, so I swung it down without holding back.","Bang! Bang! Bang!","After striking it three times in succession, I got a reaction.","Just as the Gallery comments had said, its mouth and gills opened wide.","It had been properly stunned.","I immediately began cleaning it.","Since I might injure myself, I used an ordinary dagger rather than the Heavenly Demon’s sword.","The dagger was quite sharp, so it sliced through the fish’s flesh easily.","\"Wonmo, want this?\"","\"Kyuu!\"","I cut off the head and gave it to Wonmo.","He ate it with great enthusiasm.","He could eat rotting corpses, so a fresh fish head was probably nothing to him.","The Speed Sloth was more interested in fasting pills than fish, so I didn’t need to worry about it.","Now to cut open the belly.","Whenever blood came out, I rinsed it away with water.","I slowly sliced open the belly of the now-silent, headless fish.","The sensation against my fingertips wasn’t pleasant, but it was something I’d have to get used to.","Would Wonmo eat the organs too?","With the belly opened, I could see the densely packed organs inside.","I just needed to remove all of them and wash the cavity with water.","I reached inside to pull them out.","\"Hm?\"","My hand caught hold of something.","At first, I thought it was the heart.","But it was far too hard to be one.","I fumbled around and finally managed to pull it out.","It was a small bead roughly the size of one segment of my finger.","Its color was red, just like the fish.","What’s this? Could it really be an inner core?","Surely not.","Spirit beasts that possessed inner cores couldn’t be that common.","Still, considering that fully grown Mandrakes were practically lying around here, I couldn’t completely dismiss the possibility.","I’d even discovered a New Moon Spirit Herb right at the beginning.","Hmm...","I stared at the red bead for a while before making a decision.","It would be best to ask the Gallery.","More specifically, an expert.","And the obvious expert was the Heavenly Demon, the first person who had mentioned inner cores to me.","She wasn’t the type to secretly steal it either, so I could ask her without worry.","Title: Heavenly Demon, I Have a Question","Wild Grylls","(Photo of the red bead)","I found this while cleaning a fish.","It looks similar to the inner core you mentioned before. Can you tell what it is?","If the photo isn’t enough, I can send it to you through a trade.","└ Heavenly Demon: You found it inside a fish?","└ SmartCultist: Ha...","└ SwordMaster: Aren’t pearls made by shellfish, not fish?","└ Exactly. She’s confidently saying something completely ignorant. Hahaha","└ Even for an old fossil, that’s a bit much.;;","└ Isn’t she just stupid?","└ I’m embarrassed just reading this.","She replied only three seconds after I posted.","Her response speed was truly terrifying.","The sudden discussion of the Heavenly Demon’s lack of basic knowledge made me slightly uneasy.","Still, she was the person who had taught me the breathing technique, so I could trust her with this.","└ Wild Grylls: I’ll send you a trade request. You only need to check whether it’s an inner core.","└ Heavenly Demon: If it truly is an inner core, what do you intend to do with it?","└ Wild Grylls: Eat it, obviously. You said it was good for the body, didn’t you?","└ Heavenly Demon: I do not recommend that. As I told you before, your internal energy is already oversaturated. Consuming an inner core as well may cause serious trouble.","└ Wild Grylls: Yes. I found it while removing the organs.","└ Heavenly Demon: Hmm. It is difficult to tell from the photograph alone. It may simply be a pearl.","└ Wild Grylls: Can fish make pearls too?","└ Heavenly Demon: I was under the impression that they could.","I nodded at the Heavenly Demon’s advice.","Too much of a good thing could indeed be harmful.","Eating an inner core in my current state might cause a serious problem.","That left only one option.","Give it to the Heavenly Demon.","SwordMaster would probably refuse, claiming that she didn’t want to become healthier.","└ Wild Grylls: Then would you like to eat it?","└ Heavenly Demon: Inner cores can no longer raise my cultivation. I passed that stage long ago.","└ Wild Grylls: Then what should I do with it?","└ Heavenly Demon: The answer is simple.","The Heavenly Demon’s response was straightforward.","└ Heavenly Demon: Why not put it up for auction?","What an incredibly carefree suggestion.","Should I?","And I found myself gradually leaning toward that carefree idea."]},{"title":"Chapter 31","paragraphs":["Inner Core (2)","The daily life of the Heavenly Demon, Yu Sowol, was so simple that it bordered on monotonous.","She sat upon the highest throne of the Heavenly Demon Divine Cult, a seat meant only for the heavens themselves.","From there, she browsed the Gallery and organized whatever enlightenment she had gained.","That was all.","She had no need to sleep.","She had no need to bathe either.","At her level of cultivation, her body always remained in perfect condition.","And so, every single day, she sat on her throne and browsed the Gallery.","One might ask what kind of ridiculous lifestyle that was, but reality was reality.","Anyone who saw it might have asked a question like this.","Title: Does the Heavenly Demon Have a Job?","If she does, what kind of work does she even do? I’m kind of curious.","└ What job would an old fossil who browses the Gallery all day have? Hahaha","└ Even if she has one, isn’t she basically role-playing as an unemployed shut-in?","└ Judging by the way she talks, maybe she’s some kind of adviser?","└ Heavenly Demon: I sit upon the throne.","└ That’s it?","└ Heavenly Demon: My majesty is displayed through that alone.","└ So you’re just unemployed. Kekeke","└ How is that any different from being a shut-in? Hahaha","└ Heavenly Demon: Do not compare me to those who abandon their duties and hide away. I am at least revered as the heavens themselves.","└ What a load of bullshit. Hahaha Does she think she’s some kind of god? Hahaha","└ Wouldn’t that get her arrested for blasphemy?","└ Heavenly Demon: I personally crush the heads of those who mock me.","└ Damn, this role-play is seriously intense.;;","└ Just leave her alone. She’s always been like that.","Wasn’t the Demonic Cult a place that regarded the Heavenly Demon as the heavens themselves?","Then how was she any different from a shut-in?","The problem was that they literally worshipped her as the heavens.","What was the sky?","A symbol of divinity that had existed since humanity first came into being.","Very few people could face such an existence directly and plead for their wishes.","Even those who wished to make a request had to go through the Demonic Brain, the true administrator of the cult.","At first glance, that might make the Heavenly Demon seem like a mere figurehead.","But that couldn’t have been further from the truth.","Even the Demonic Brain would not escape unharmed if he displeased her.","The moment one fell out of favor with a Heavenly Demon who had surpassed the Transformation Realm and reached the Profound Realm, it was over.","Title: Can Usernames Be Duplicated?","A lot of registered users have surprisingly simple names.","The Heavenly Demon is especially famous throughout the Central Plains, right?","Did no one ever claim that username before?","└ Usernames probably can’t be duplicated. Semi-registered accounts can use them, though.","└ Even semi-registered accounts can’t use one if a registered user already claimed it.","└ What’s the difference between semi-registered and registered accounts? Is it that yellow mark beside the name?","└ That’s part of it, but registered users can also list items in the auction house and conduct private trades.","└ The Moderator can track their location too, though. Hahaha","└ The former former former Moderator did that, killed someone, and went to prison.","└ Damn, that’s terrifying.","└ So because the Heavenly Demon claimed it as a registered username, no one else can use it?","└ ᄋᄋ Exactly.","└ You’re saying no one had ever registered the name Heavenly Demon before?","└ Someone probably did, but they were likely all semi-registered accounts. Who in their right mind would register Heavenly Demon as a permanent username? Hahaha","└ The current Moderator is nice. The former former former one would’ve sold your address for money. Hahaha","└ But what if she turned out to be the real Heavenly Demon?","└ Then the Demonic Cult would’ve been ruined for a completely different reason.","└ Heavenly Demon: There is no need for concern. As long as I exist, the Demonic Cult will never fall.","└ That’s exactly the problem, ma’am.","└ If someone like that were really the Heavenly Demon, the cultists would have an existential crisis. Hahaha","└ How is she browsing the Gallery twenty-four hours a day?;;","So that she could reply the moment her benefactor made a post.","Most matters concerning the Demonic Cult were handled by the Demonic Brain, leaving her with little to do.","All sorts of rumors circulated about her, but it was true that Yu Sowol had become completely immersed in the Gallery.","Recently, she had even encountered a benefactor who could only be described as a fortuitous encounter.","Worried that something might happen to him, she remained in the Gallery at all times.","As always, she was browsing through the Gallery.","Yu Sowol sat idly upon her throne, staring intently at something.","A tiny red bead rested between her slender fingers.","It was the item Wild Grylls—her benefactor and fortuitous encounter—had traded to her so she could determine whether it was an inner core.","Having surpassed the Transformation Realm and entered the Profound Realm, identifying it was easy.","It is an inner core.","The red bead Grylls had given her was indeed an inner core.","Though it looked like an ordinary marble, the energy contained within it was anything but ordinary.","However, it is lacking in many respects.","For an inner core, it was deficient in several ways.","First, the absolute amount of energy it contained was too small.","Normally, consuming an inner core could allow a Supreme Peak martial artist to enter the Transformation Realm.","This one contained only enough energy to raise someone from the Peak Realm to the Supreme Peak Realm.","It was likely the inner core of a spirit beast that had lived for several centuries rather than several millennia.","Still, it is not bad.","To Yu Sowol, who had already entered the Profound Realm, it was little more than a medicinal treasure beneficial to the body.","Of course, that was only from Yu Sowol’s perspective.","To anyone else, it was an object surpassing treasure.","Considering how rare even Supreme Peak martial artists were, its true value was easy to imagine.","If this were released onto the market—especially through the Gallery’s auction house—it would undoubtedly cause an uproar.","It is too much for my benefactor to consume. What a pity.","But Yu Sowol did not dwell on that.","There was something more important.","Grylls had only just begun learning an internal cultivation technique.","By some stroke of fortune, he had opened both his middle and upper dantians, but he was still inexperienced.","If he consumed the inner core as well, his body might be unable to withstand it and burst apart in the worst-case scenario.","Even if he survived, he would likely suffer from fever and pain for several days.","That was not an outcome someone focused on survival like Grylls would prefer.","But leaving the inner core unattended was not an option either.","The energy within an inner core dispersed over time.","Since it had originally existed inside the body of a spirit beast, that was only natural.","What a remarkable forest. To think that fish containing inner cores can be caught so easily.","A New Moon Spirit Herb.","A fully grown Mandrake.","And now, even a fish containing an inner core.","Each one alone would be enough to shake the entire world, yet the Forest of Four Seasons seemed to have them lying around everywhere.","Even so, entering the forest was no different from suicide.","The space itself constantly shifted, and access to the Gallery was normally impossible.","Grylls was surviving only because, for some strange reason, he could still access it.","An ordinary person wouldn’t last two days.","Was that how the Demonic Brain explained it?","Yu Sowol stared at the inner core for a moment before accessing the Gallery.","Now that she had confirmed its quality, all that remained was to inform Grylls.","Because they had just completed a trade, she could not immediately return it.","Still, there were ways to preserve the energy within an inner core, so there was no need to worry.","Title: Benefactor, Read This","Heavenly Demon","As you requested, I have verified the authenticity of the inner core.","It is genuine.","└ Isn’t she trying to scam him?","└ So she can sell it at a higher price. Hahaha","└ Now even inner cores are appearing. Hahaha","└ Heavenly Demon: Believe me or not as you please. I have not spoken a single falsehood.","She ignored all the pointless comments.","The only person who mattered to Yu Sowol was Grylls.","Still, playing along with the others for a moment didn’t seem so bad.","Unlike her, who remained in the Gallery at all times, Grylls was busy.","As she idly traded jokes with the other users, Grylls finally left a comment.","└ Wild Grylls: Oh. It’s actually real?","└ Heavenly Demon: Indeed. What will you do with it now?","└ Wild Grylls: What would happen if I ate it?","└ Heavenly Demon: In the worst case, your body may burst. Even if that does not happen, there is a high chance you will suffer from a severe fever for several days.","└ Wild Grylls: So basically, I have to give it to someone else.","└ If it’s real, give it to me. I’ve hit a wall and I’m still stuck at First-Rate.","└ Give it to me. I’m stuck at Intermediate Expert.","└ Give it to me give it to me give it to me give it to me give it to me","└ Cultistcultistcultistcultistcultistcultist!","└ Heavenly Demon: What a pathetic spectacle.","Perhaps he needed time to think, because Grylls did not reply for a while.","Or perhaps something else had happened in the meantime.","The Heavenly Demon waited silently.","She could already predict what kind of comment would appear.","He will most likely choose to give it either to me or to someone else.","└ Wild Grylls: Then you can eat it, Heavenly Demon, or give it to someone around you.","└ Heavenly Demon: Is there anything you desire in return?","└ Wild Grylls: Yes. Could you give me more fasting pills?","Just as expected, Grylls left such a comment.","He was proposing to exchange the inner core for fasting pills.","At his suggestion, Yu Sowol unconsciously smiled.","It was a smile worthy of a painting, but unfortunately, there was no one there to see it.","The Heavenly Demon sat alone upon the throne in the audience hall.","└ Heavenly Demon: An inner core is a precious medicinal treasure. Though this one is somewhat lacking, an inner core is still an inner core. Even if it takes time, it would be better for you to consume it eventually.","└ Wild Grylls: But I don’t know when that will be. If necessary, I can just catch another one.","└ Heavenly Demon: Hmm? There is another one?","└ Wild Grylls: I caught one just now. I don’t know whether it has an inner core, but since it looks exactly the same, there’s probably a good chance, right?","└ Heavenly Demon: What a wondrous forest.","└ He caught another one? Is that for real?","└ Wild Grylls: ᄋᄋ I’ll probably install a fish trap soon.","└ Won’t the fish tear the trap apart?","└ Wild Grylls: Then I’ll just ask the dwarf for help.","└ Passing Dwarf: Why me?","└ Wild Grylls: Did you make the barricade?","└ Passing Dwarf: Forgot. Kek.","└ Wild Grylls: You fucking bitch.","└ Passing Dwarf: What?","└ Wild Grylls: ...Is what I obviously shouldn’t say, right?","└ Look at this shameless bastard. Hahahahaha","└ This lunatic. Hahahahahahaha","Fasting pills.","Yu Sowol fell into thought.","She had previously given him an entire sack, so could he already be running low?","That was unlikely.","Even if he ate three per meal, she had packed plenty for him.","He probably intended to keep more as emergency rations.","That was the most reasonable explanation.","He must be accounting for the sloth as well.","With another mouth to feed, his supplies would naturally be depleted faster.","Grylls was likely preparing for that.","└ Considering the fully grown Mandrake, there’s a ninety-nine percent chance it’s real.","└ He could’ve coordinated the story with the Heavenly Demon.","└ Then they’d simply be scammers. Hahaha","└ Grylls doesn’t really have any reason to scam people, though. ᄋᄋ","└ Heavenly Demon: Wait here. I shall ask one of my close aides.","└ Wild Grylls: Thank you. If it’s difficult, you don’t have to do it.","└ Heavenly Demon: It is a request from my benefactor. I cannot simply refuse. If it cannot be done, then I shall make it possible.","└ Wild Grylls: That’s kind of burdensome. Still, don’t pressure them too much if they say it’s difficult. I don’t want them to hate me for no reason.","└ Heavenly Demon: What will you do if they say it is impossible?","└ Wild Grylls: I’ll trade with someone else. Or list it in the auction house.","└ The auction house is about to explode. Kek.","└ Is that thing really an inner core?","A strange sense of anticipation was already spreading through the Gallery.","Hadn’t the incident involving the fully grown Mandrake happened only two days ago?","Naturally, posts flooded in claiming that the inner core must also be real and begging to receive it themselves.","Getting excited over nothing.","Yu Sowol snorted as she read them.","No one had even said they would give it away, yet they were already getting their hopes up.","Seeing those comments only strengthened her resolve.","She would exchange the inner core for fasting pills no matter what.","Coincidentally, the Demonic Brain was a master standing between the Peak and Supreme Peak Realms, making it a fair trade.","[Demonic Brain, are you listening?]","Yu Sowol summoned the Demonic Brain through a voice transmission.","He was probably busy at the moment, so calling him in this manner was more convenient.","[There is something I require. Come to me.]","No answer came back.","The audience hall was far from the place where the Demonic Brain currently was.","Ever since Yu Sowol entered the Profound Realm, her senses had long since surpassed the boundaries of humanity.","She no longer saw merely through her eyes.","Her perception was closer to looking down upon the world from the heavens.","Even with all this, the Forest of Four Seasons remains difficult. Nature truly is mysterious.","At the same time, she realized once again how extraordinary nature was.","The closer one drew to it, the farther away it seemed.","That perfectly described Yu Sowol’s impression of nature.","Putting that aside...","Until the Demonic Brain arrived, the Heavenly Demon continued browsing the Gallery.","Her reverence for nature was not the only thing that had grown after reaching the Profound Realm.","Is it truly impossible to interfere with the Gallery?","She had begun questioning whether she could interfere with it directly.","Aside from the Moderator, no user was capable of altering the Gallery’s structure.","She wanted to interfere with it somehow, but attempting to do so was like smashing her head against an unyielding wall.","Accessing it itself is not difficult. Just who created this strange civilization?","The origins of the Continental Integrated Gallery were unclear.","Some claimed that it had existed since ancient times, while others said it had appeared only recently.","Watching posts appear in real time, Yu Sowol thought,","In order to aid my benefactor...","Normally, this was not something she would have cared about.","But things had changed after receiving Grylls’s help.","The Heavenly Demon—the exalted sky of the Demonic Cult seated upon her throne—could now face him through the Gallery.","\"I greet the heavens of the Demonic Cult.\"","\"Take it.\"","Yu Sowol skipped over the trivial formalities and tossed the inner core.","As though he had anticipated her action, the Demonic Brain caught it easily without raising his bowed head.","He then slowly looked up, revealing his confusion.","\"Heavens, this is...?\"","\"It is an inner core. Though somewhat lacking, it belonged to a spirit beast that lived for several centuries.\"","She would find some way to interfere with the Gallery and aid Grylls.","Although she had yet to understand its basic structure, interference was not necessarily impossible.","Was it called... a Vice Moderator?","Just as Yu Sowol reached toward an unknown realm she should perhaps never have touched—","[Heavens, I have answered your summons.]","The Demonic Brain’s respectful greeting sounded from outside.","The moment Yu Sowol heard him, she closed the Gallery and spoke calmly.","\"Enter.\"","It was not the command of Yu Sowol the human.","It was the command of Yu Sowol the Heavenly Demon.","At her words, the tightly sealed doors of the audience hall slowly opened.","A young man dressed in the traditional attire of the Demonic Cult appeared beyond them.","The Demonic Brain.","Perhaps nervous, his expression was slightly stiff as he slowly raised his head.","Confusion soon became evident on his face.","He examined the red inner core from various angles before speaking in a reluctant tone.","\"It certainly is an inner core. Where did you obtain it?\"","\"I received it through a trade. Therefore, I have something to ask you.\"","\"Please give your command.\"","\"The fasting pills that were prepared for my cultivation. How many more can you produce?\"","Yu Sowol went straight to the point.","It meant that no further explanation was necessary.","The Demonic Brain thought for a moment before carefully answering.","\"The fasting pills produced for the heavens were made using precious medicinal herbs.\"","\"I know.\"","\"If you are referring to those, then it is possible.\"","\"How many days will it take?\"","\"We must prepare the ingredients, and you appear to require a large quantity. It will take approximately one week.\"","\"Good. Begin preparing them at once. You may consume the inner core.\"","\"I am grateful for your grace, Heavens.\"","The Demonic Brain bowed deeply in gratitude.","It was fortunate that his head was lowered.","Otherwise, Yu Sowol might have noticed the corners of his lips twitching upward.","The Demonic Brain soon turned around and departed from the audience hall, leaving Yu Sowol alone once more.","The moment she sensed that he had gone outside, she immediately accessed the Gallery.","[Ah. Fuck, why is my body heating up?]","\"Hm?\"","The instant she entered the Gallery, a certain title caught her eye.","It had been posted by Grylls.","Yu Sowol hurriedly opened it.","Title: Ah. Fuck, Why Is My Body Heating Up?","Wild Grylls","(Photo of a fish that had been eaten clean, with even the bones picked bare)","My body started heating up the moment I ate this. What’s going on?","Don’t tell me it was poisonous?","\"Oh no.\"","Yu Sowol realized her mistake the moment she saw the post.","The energy of a spirit beast was not necessarily concentrated solely within its inner core.","The spirit beast itself was essentially another inner core.","Every piece of its flesh would contain powerful energy.","I was careless.","Yu Sowol hurriedly left a comment.","She was deeply worried that something might happen to Grylls."]},{"title":"Chapter 32","paragraphs":["Inner Core (3)","There was something I had realized over the course of my life.","The loneliest and most miserable moment in the world was when you were sick.","After my parents passed away, I once spent several days bedridden with illness.","I couldn’t remember how much I had cried back then.","Had even one of them still been alive, they would have taken care of me.","Loneliness and fever were the perfect combination for wearing a person down.","That was exactly how I felt now.","I’d finally eaten my fill for the first time in ages, only to collapse with a fever immediately afterward.","\"Kyuu.\"","At least I had the adorable Wonmo with me.","Without him, I think it would’ve hurt even more.","Perhaps the Speed Sloth could read the mood, because it climbed off my back the moment I began suffering.","\"You should just leave.\"","But because of its natural expression, it wasn’t comforting at all.","Its relaxed face was normally fine, but right now, it almost looked like it was mocking me.","Surely not.","I felt bad for taking my frustration out on an innocent Speed Sloth.","The sudden fever was clouding my judgment.","I panted from the heat burning throughout my entire body.","Every breath carried scorching air out of my mouth.","At this rate, I might start breathing fire like a dragon.","I don’t understand why this is happening.","It was ridiculous that eating a single fish had given me a fever.","I wondered whether I’d been infected by a parasite, but that was unlikely.","I’d cooked it thoroughly just in case.","The first possibility that came to mind was poison.","Could it have contained toxins like a pufferfish?","I took the medicine immediately, but I don’t know if it’ll work.","Just in case, I had swallowed the pill Allfather gave me.","Normally, I should’ve immediately circulated it using the internal cultivation technique, but I was in no condition to do so.","I could probably do it after the fever subsided a little.","Before that, I should check the Gallery.","I’d made a post just before the fever began, so there should be comments by now.","Title: Ah, Fuck. Why Is My Body Heating Up?","Wild Grylls","(Photo of a fish eaten completely clean, with even the bones picked bare)","My body started heating up the moment I ate this. What’s going on?","Don’t tell me it was poisonous?","└ Is there even a poison that raises your body temperature?","└ There are some. I’ve heard of poisons that kill by causing a severe fever.","└ Allfather: Did you take the medicine I gave you?","└ Wild Grylls: I did, just in case.","└ Allfather: If it were poison, you should have recovered immediately. Strange. It probably isn’t poison.","└ Heavenly Demon: You should regulate your internal energy immediately. Since you consumed a spirit beast, your body must now be filled with energy.","└ Wild Grylls: But I didn’t eat the inner core.","└ Heavenly Demon: A spirit beast is called a spirit beast for a reason. Even without the inner core, its flesh would still contain a considerable amount of energy.","└ SwordMaster: Nothing works better than a mana cultivation technique when you’re sick. Taking a sip of elixir beforehand helps too.","└ Heavenly Demon: It is an internal cultivation technique, not a mana cultivation technique.","└ SwordMaster: Same thing, really. Hehe. Until you teach him the mnemonic formula, aren’t they all basically identical?","└ Heavenly Demon: I feel like tearing out that wicked tongue of yours.","└ SwordMaster: Go ahead and try. Kek.","└ Heavenly Demon: What an ugly sight, hiding in your room and doing nothing but running your mouth. I can practically see you wasting away with age and idleness.","└ SwordMaster: What did you just say?","└ Heavenly Demon: Hmm. Perhaps I should begin becoming more active myself. I would hate to become as unsightly as you.","└ Why did the Heavenly Demon suddenly attack all of us too?","└ That was some wide-area provocation. Fucking hell. Hahahaha","└ Suddenly, I want to support SwordMaster.","Come to think of it, I had an elixir.","The sudden fever had made me completely forget about it.","Enduring the steadily rising heat, I crawled forward.","Eventually, I reached into the storage box and grabbed one of the elixirs.","A brilliantly glowing golden liquid filled the bottle.","Different grades had different colors, but I was in too much pain to care which one I picked.","I’ll just take one sip first...","Even removing the cork was difficult.","Should I buy some fever medicine from the auction house?","I struggled to pull out the cork and drank a mouthful of the elixir.","A strangely bitter yet refreshing sensation flowed down my throat.","Now all that remained was the breathing technique.","Before beginning, I checked the comments again.","Just before closing the Gallery, I’d seen the Heavenly Demon and SwordMaster start arguing.","└ Heavenly Demon: Struggle all you wish. I am the one who will teach my benefactor his internal cultivation technique. Now begone.","└ SwordMaster: What if Grylls can’t understand the mnemonic formula?","└ Heavenly Demon: That will not happen. I shall explain every detail to him one by one.","└ SwordMaster: Sorry, but that’s realistically difficult. You’re not beside him. It’s hard to learn the practical nuances of a mana cultivation technique through a mnemonic formula alone.","└ Heavenly Demon: Does the same not apply to you? If he can understand merely from written explanations, then my benefactor is already a genius.","└ SwordMaster: Have you even read my posts? Do you have any idea how good I am at explaining things?","└ Her explanations really are good. The continent’s average combat strength rose because of her.","└ She covers everything from the basics to advanced applications, so both beginners and experienced fighters can use them.","└ The Heavenly Demon only posts garbage anyway. Hahaha","I should probably stop them here.","Perhaps thanks to the elixir, some of my dizziness had subsided.","└ Wild Grylls: SwordMaster, that’s enough. It’s true that your posts have helped me, but I don’t want to break my promise to the Heavenly Demon.","└ SwordMaster: I’m sorry. I got carried away.","└ Heavenly Demon: Pay no heed to someone who seeks to break trust with her wicked tongue.","└ Wild Grylls: SwordMaster was only trying to help me too.","SwordMaster’s posts really were useful.","Even someone like me, who knew absolutely nothing, had managed to grasp the basics because of them.","Perhaps that was why most people were more sympathetic toward SwordMaster than the Heavenly Demon.","The Heavenly Demon only kept replying because she marched entirely to the beat of her own drum.","An ordinary person would’ve had their spirit crushed by now.","Thankfully, the argument seemed mostly settled.","Had I not intervened, my entire post might have been buried beneath their fight.","Besides, SwordMaster had started it this time.","Though the Heavenly Demon had certainly taken the bait.","I should sit down now...","Even the elixir hadn’t completely brought the fever down.","Its pain-relieving effect had only reduced the suffering.","I forced my increasingly hot body upright and assumed the lotus position.","Before beginning the breathing exercise, I asked the Heavenly Demon for guidance.","└ Wild Grylls: I’m about to start cultivating. Could you teach me that mnemonic formula or whatever it’s called?","└ Heavenly Demon: I can, but as a precaution, I shall teach you only the first formula. A mistake could cause you to suffer qi deviation.","└ Wild Grylls: Understood. Please post it as a private comment.","└ Heavenly Demon: The heavens are the supreme existence revered by all creation. Reach out your hand and grasp them within it. If you look upward, then look downward. That is the nature of the heavens...","I had expected some ordinary piece of advice, only for a poem to suddenly appear.","It was archaic and, in a way, perfectly suited to a martial arts world.","Which meant I couldn’t understand it at all.","There was a reason SwordMaster had criticized internal cultivation formulas as poetry rather than practical guidance.","How is this supposed to help me?","Besides, the mnemonic formula wasn’t just a single line. It was fairly long.","The Heavenly Demon’s comments continued appearing one after another.","After feeling bewildered for a moment, I memorized every line she had posted.","My head was spinning from the fever, but not so badly that I couldn’t memorize it.","\"Hoo...\"","I began by controlling my breathing, imagining that I was gathering the heat inside my body.","I also repeated the Heavenly Demon’s formula in my head.","I just had to picture it somehow.","This was closer to emotion and intuition than actual interpretation.","Still better than Gwandong Byeolgok.","It was far better than that dreadful poem.","Imagining the mnemonic formula the Heavenly Demon had taught me, I began circulating my internal energy.","The heat scattered throughout my body seemed to gather in my lower abdomen.","The heavens are the supreme existence revered by all creation...","And after continuing the internal cultivation technique while reciting the formula—","\"Khrrr...\"","I fell asleep without even realizing it.","\"Ugh!\"","The sensation of falling from a great height made me bolt upright.","It felt like suddenly jerking awake after dozing off in class.","Except this sensation was several times more intense.","I became fully alert in an instant.","\"...\"","I blinked.","What kind of dream had I just been having?","I remembered flying freely through the sky, but nothing after that.","It was difficult to explain.","It almost felt as though my soul and body had separated.","Still, it had been a pleasant dream.","For the first time in a long while, I had experienced genuine freedom.","\"Kyuu...\"","While I sat there in a daze, a sorrowful sound reached my ears.","I turned toward it and saw a fluffy ball of fur staring at me.","It was Wonmo, the baby owlbear.","Wonmo gazed at me with sorrowful eyes.","Grrrrumble—","At the same time, an alarm sounded from his stomach.","I’m hungry. Feed me because I’m hungry. I’m sad because I’m hungry.","That was roughly what his expression seemed to say.","Feeling awkward, I checked the time.","No.","There was no need to check.","Looking outside the cave was enough.","...It’s already night?","The outside world was filled with complete darkness.","It had been around lunchtime when the fever struck after I ate the fish.","That meant I had slept for at least six hours.","No wonder Wonmo looked so miserable.","\"Wonmo, I’m sorry. I’ll feed you right away.\"","\"Kyuu!\"","\"Wonmo aside, where did Speedy go...?\"","The moment I turned my head, Speedy was right there.","The creature stared at me with its now-familiar expression.","Judging by the way its mouth was moving, it had eaten some fasting pills while I slept.","...It didn’t eat too many, did it?","With a growing sense of unease, I counted the remaining pills.","Thankfully, the number hadn’t decreased much.","In that case, feeding Wonmo came first.","I accessed the Gallery.","As always, it was noisy, but Wonmo’s meal was more important right now.","\"Here you go.\"","\"Kyuoooo!\"","The moment I bought him a chunk of meat, his eyes lit up with delight.","When I stroked his head because he was so adorable, he became even happier.","How could I possibly dislike him?","Just looking at him made me smile.","The fever seems to be gone, and nothing feels wrong with my body. I should be fine.","As expected, sleeping deeply was the best cure for a fever.","Still, my body felt damp from all the sweat.","That couldn’t be helped.","Since it was already late, I thought I should at least wash myself quickly.","The iron barrel still contained the fish, so taking a proper bath would be difficult.","\"Hm?\"","Just as I removed my clothes and stepped outside the cave, I noticed something strange.","I could see far too clearly.","My night vision had always been fairly good, but this was on an entirely different level.","It wasn’t as clear as daylight, but I could move around without any difficulty.","What’s going on?","I wondered about it briefly, then finished removing my clothes so I could wash.","There was no need to light a campfire.","Why would I need one when I could see perfectly well?","I would still need it when sleeping, though.","I could still feel the cold.","Flake.","Before washing, I ran a hand over my body and heard a strange sound.","I looked down and found myself facing something unexpected.","A layer of skin had peeled away.","It was different from the peeling caused by sunburn.","The skin underneath was soft and even slightly glossy.","I frowned when I saw it.","There was only one possible explanation.","How did I accumulate this much grime?","I’d thought I was washing myself properly, but apparently not.","I would have to be more thorough from now on.","For today, I could wash quickly and take a proper bath tomorrow.","If I soaked in warm water, the grime would probably come off more easily.","I can cook the fish for breakfast while I’m at it.","Surely eating it wouldn’t give me another fever.","Then the next morning came, and when I cleaned the second fish—","\"This came out again.\"","Another inner core appeared among its organs."]},{"title":"Chapter 33","paragraphs":["Inner Core (4)","The Heavenly Demon had told me that an Inner Core was one of the greatest treasures in existence.","She said that if even a single one appeared on the market, it would shake the entire world.","Martial artists devoted countless years to reaching the next realm.","Unless they possessed extraordinary talent, it was nearly impossible to obtain power that transcended the limits of time.","That was why everyone coveted Inner Cores.","With just one, they could leap straight into the next realm.","***","Title: Got Another Inner Core","Wild Grylls","(Photo of a red Inner Core.)","I slept like a log yesterday because I was sick.","Woke up, cleaned myself up, and started preparing today’s fish. Then this popped out.","Another Inner Core? Should I just put it up for auction?","Heavenly Demon: Have you awakened? You hadn’t posted for quite some time yesterday, so I was worried.","Wild Grylls: The moment I finished memorizing the cultivation verse, I blacked out and fell asleep. Is that normal?","Heavenly Demon: That is the first time I have heard such a thing. If I had to guess, your body was unable to withstand the internal energy and instinctively protected itself.","Wild Grylls: Well, my body’s completely fine now, so I guess everything worked out.","Heavenly Demon: If you say you are well, then I shall believe you. What do you intend to do with that Inner Core?","How much do you want for it?","Gimme gimme gimme gimme gimme.","How do we even know it’s real? I’ll eat it and confirm it.","Heavenly Demon: You treat an Inner Core so casually. Have you truly reached such a lofty realm?","SwordMaster: Yep.","Heavenly Demon: ...You’re so confident that I have nothing more to say.","SwordMaster refused it because he didn’t want to become healthy.","Then what about everyone else?","I waited for the others to reply.","That was the problem.","Who should I give this Inner Core to?","Ideally, I wanted to give it to one of the familiar regulars.","But even that wasn’t easy.","Wild Grylls: I should prioritize the people who’ve helped me.","SwordMaster: I’m fine.","Wild Grylls: Except you, SwordMaster.","SwordMaster: ?","Wild Grylls: Just kidding lol. So... do you want it?","SwordMaster: I don’t want to get healthier. The Mandrake can go to someone else, but an Inner Core isn’t something I can pass along, so don’t bother.","Wild Grylls: The regulars that come to mind are Passing Dwarf, Starlight Princess, Princess Chaenggu, Praisethesun, and Allfather.","Starlight Princess: I’ve already received so much from you... I think someone else should have it.","Starlight Princess was the first to comment.","She wasn’t as active as the Heavenly Demon, but she was one of the regulars who consistently left comments.","After reading that she didn’t need the Inner Core, I replied.","Wild Grylls: Are you sure? Don’t you want to improve your health even more?","Starlight Princess: I’m already more than satisfied. Taking care of my body is more important than increasing my mana.","Wild Grylls: Taking care of your body?","Starlight Princess: Yes. I started working out yesterday. It’s something I’ve never really been able to do before, and I think I’m going to get completely hooked.","She’d wanted to name Wonmo \"Gym Newbie,\" and now it looked like she was turning into a gym fanatic herself.","She’d said she’d spent most of her life confined to a bed, so it made sense she’d be eager to exercise.","Anyway, after Starlight Princess declined, I waited for the others.","Princess Chaenggu: I’m not really interested either. It’s awkward to sell, and it’s awkward to give to someone else.","Wild Grylls: You’re not going to use it yourself?","Princess Chaenggu: I don’t really need it. If anything, I’d rather give it to the Chaeyu players.","You might actually get arrested if you do that.","Wouldn’t an Inner Core count as performance-enhancing drugs?","Not exactly. But if someone suddenly experiences a huge jump in mana, they’ll probably be investigated.","But aren’t Inner Cores legal?","Princess Chaenggu: They’re legal, but it wouldn’t be ethically right. Besides, what good is more mana? Using mana is prohibited in sports.","She’s right. More mana isn’t automatically a good thing.","Haven’t there been athletes who awakened and then went into a terrible slump?","Why would getting stronger make them worse?","Because it throws off their body’s balance. Some athletes have even been disqualified after unconsciously using mana during competitions.","Wild Grylls: Then... could you at least give me some clothes?","Princess Chaenggu: I don’t really have a use for it anyway. Sorry. I’ll just give you the clothes.","Wild Grylls: Do you happen to have any long pants...?","Princess Chaenggu: Not right now, but I can get some if you want. Do you want something made from uniform fabric?","Wild Grylls: Yeah. Then let’s trade for that.","Princess Chaenggu: Just cheering for Chaeyu is enough.","Wild Grylls: Go, Chaeyu! Wishing you the championship!","Princess Chaenggu: Perfect! Haha.","Chaeyu winning? LOL.","King Leor: LMAO.","King Leor: Wild Grylls, do you even know what place Chaeyu is in right now?","Wild Grylls: What place?","Princess Chaenggu: Be quiet before I come over there and beat you up.","King Leor: Ooooh, scary. Anyway, what place is Chaeyu in? Eighth!","Wild Grylls: That’s a bit low. How many matches are left?","Princess Chaenggu: Five. It’s okay, though. We probably won’t make the Champions League, but we’ll at least qualify for the Master Cup.","King Leor: Talk after you actually make the Champions League lol.","There they went again.","Those two argued surprisingly often.","King Leor especially seemed to pick a fight every time Princess Chaenggu showed up.","Personally, I didn’t like it.","She’d helped me before, after all.","Allfather: I’d rather receive another rare creature than the Inner Core.","Praisethesun: Just auction it off. And don’t think about squeezing money out of me.","Wild Grylls: I wasn’t planning to...","Praisethesun: Relax, I’m joking. I’m not interested anyway. The mature Mandrake you gave me before is more than enough.","Wild Grylls: Got it. So you really don’t need it, Princess Chaenggu?","Princess Chaenggu: Nope. I can’t give it to the players anyway.","Wild Grylls: Understood. Go, Chaenggu!","Princess Chaenggu: Thank you. Haha.","King Leor: Cheer for Leor too!","Wild Grylls: I’m not the type to play both sides. Haha.","Princess Chaenggu: I like you even more now. I’ll go find those pants as soon as I can.","Since Princess Chaenggu also turned it down, I moved on to the others.","Allfather: As I mentioned before, my body isn’t capable of making use of an Inner Core. Please give it to someone else.","Wild Grylls: Understood.","Both Allfather and Praisethesun refused.","They were the type who only asked for things they truly needed.","That left only Passing Dwarf.","Passing Dwarf: Just give me more Mandrakes. I wanna brew more liquor.","Wild Grylls: Yeah... Asking you was my mistake. Almost finished making the barricades?","Passing Dwarf: We’ll trade at lunch. If you’re short, let me know.","Wild Grylls: You don’t want the Inner Core as payment?","Passing Dwarf: I said bring me booze.","Wild Grylls: ;_;","The dwarf was hopeless.","Maybe it was because he was a dwarf, but he absolutely loved alcohol.","In the end, every regular I knew turned it down.","The Heavenly Demon said she didn’t need another one since I’d already given her one before.","Apparently she’d already received too much from me.","Whatever.","I didn’t think about it for long.","I listed the Inner Core in the auction house.","The fish were more important than the Inner Core right now.","I gave the head and innards to Wonmo, then cleaned the fish thoroughly like I had yesterday.","Today the hose wasn’t clogged, and water poured out freely.","It did taste good.","I’d eat a hearty breakfast, then use that energy to reinforce my base.","At lunchtime, I’d install the barricades the dwarf had given me.","Sizzle—","The fish browned nicely in the cast-iron pan I’d bought from the auction house.","I’d removed all the scales and seasoned it with salt.","I also cut the meat into bite-sized pieces.","Eating it whole yesterday had been a pain.","\"Here, Wonmo. Eat up.\"","I didn’t keep it all to myself.","I picked up a few pieces of the freshly cooked fish with my chopsticks and handed them to Wonmo.","I didn’t just shove the whole pan in front of him.","Being Korean, chopsticks felt far more natural than a fork.","\"Kyuu!\"","Wonmo’s eyes sparkled as he eagerly devoured the fish.","Considering his size, this was nowhere near enough.","For a human, it would’ve barely counted as an appetizer.","I’d give him some meat later.","\"Want some too?\"","I held out a piece of the well-cooked fish toward the Swift Sloth.","I knew it was a herbivore...","But maybe it’d still be interested.","Nod.","The Swift Sloth slowly nodded and accepted.","I thought it only ate plants, but apparently not.","Then again, it had originally tried to steal the fish, so it wasn’t entirely surprising.","I picked up a well-cooked piece of fish with my chopsticks and held it near its mouth.","Slowly... ever so slowly...","\"Could you eat a little faster?\"","How could even opening its mouth be that slow?","And yet this same creature had threatened me at the fastest speed imaginable.","No matter how hard I tried, I simply couldn’t understand it.","Now that I’d given both of them some fish, all that remained was filling my own stomach.","\"...\"","After dividing it evenly, there was much less left than yesterday.","But that was fine.","Yesterday, while I had been feasting alone, the two of them had stared at me.","Their gazes seemed to say, You’re really eating all that delicious food by yourself?","It had made me feel guilty.","There’s plenty anyway.","The fish was so large that I had to wrap both arms around it.","Giving away a few pieces wasn’t going to leave me short.","Maybe yesterday’s fever had actually been caused by overeating.","Though, as the Heavenly Demon had said, it was probably because too much energy had surged into me at once.","\"Delicious.\"","After finishing the fish, my stomach felt comfortably full.","Instead of a toothpick, I used a fish bone to remove the bits of food stuck between my teeth.","Not a single part went to waste.","Disposing of the remains was a little troublesome, but all I had to do was bury them.","Time to get moving.","I couldn’t afford to relax too much.","I wasn’t planning to live here forever. It would be a problem if I became lazy already.","But first, I should circulate the cultivation method.","Since I’d eaten a hearty breakfast, I used the internal-energy cultivation method to refine my mana.","I also remembered to recite the verse the Heavenly Demon had taught me yesterday.","The poetic language made it difficult to understand, but imagining the imagery made it somewhat easier.","If the first verse is already this bad, how difficult will the second one be?","Surely all of them together wouldn’t form a poem as long and complicated as Gwandong Byeolgok .","If they did, even memorizing it would be an ordeal.","Still, I’ll have to learn it.","I focused while guiding the mana inside my body with the cultivation method.","It might have been my imagination, but the energy felt stronger and more domineering than yesterday.","Rather than a calm river, it felt like waves rushing violently forward.","That wasn’t necessarily a bad thing.","Thanks to that powerful force, the circulation speed had increased dramatically.","\"...\"","After completing the entire circulation, I slowly opened my eyes.","The first thing I saw was the Swift Sloth’s drowsy face directly in front of me.","\"Whoa! You scared me!\"","\"...\"","\"Seriously... Don’t sneak up on people like that.\"","I nearly had a heart attack.","I let out a sigh.","It was good that it hadn’t disturbed me, but anyone would be startled to find it sitting right in front of them.","Wonmo is... already asleep.","Our adorable ball of fur was deep into his afternoon nap.","Since he was still a baby, it seemed all he knew how to do was eat, sleep, and poop.","Fortunately, he did the last one outside the cave, so it wasn’t a problem.","Crawl... crawl...","When I prepared to move, the Swift Sloth climbed onto my back.","I was gradually becoming used to it, but then I suddenly remembered its hygiene.","This thing hasn’t taken a bath, has it?","I needed to heat some bathwater immediately.","Otherwise, it might make me sick.","Allfather had said that while it didn’t have any ticks, various other insects lived in its fur.","He had even said there was a high chance that mold was growing on it.","It needed to be scrubbed clean just as thoroughly as Wonmo.","I’ve finished eating the fish, and the timing is perfect.","I immediately cleaned the iron tub and filled it with water.","Now all I had to do was wait for it to heat up.","I could worry about adjusting the temperature later.","While waiting, I used a shovel to dig out the places where I intended to install the barricades.","I planned to surround the cave entrance with barricades in a square formation.","Thud! Thud!","Why is this so easy to dig?","I’d noticed it while logging, but shoveling didn’t feel exhausting at all.","Normally, even the shovel itself should have felt somewhat heavy, but I couldn’t feel its weight.","This had to be thanks to the internal-energy cultivation method.","Manual labor would be easy from now on.","\"...I’m already finished?\"","The problem was that it had become too easy.","Less than thirty minutes had passed, yet the groundwork was already complete.","All I had to do was place the barricades inside the neatly dug trenches and fill them back in with soil.","A few trees were in the way, but I could gradually cut those down.","Bang! Bang! Crack!","Even the logging was finished within thirty minutes.","It was unbelievably fast.","Before, it had felt like I was chopping trees.","Now it was closer to smashing them apart.","Once I destroyed the center, the trees lost their balance and easily toppled over.","All I had to do was break the middle and push them with my foot.","I was more bewildered than pleased by how suddenly I’d become stronger.","Well, there’s no point complaining about something good.","I scratched my head while looking at the devastated trees, then shrugged.","I listed all but one of the felled trees in the auction house.","The remaining one would be used as firewood.","Thinking about firewood reminded me of the bathwater I had heated earlier.","I worried that it might be boiling, but fortunately, only gentle steam was rising from it.","\"All right. It’s your turn to wash.\"","Crawl... crawl...","Perhaps it understood me, because the Swift Sloth climbed down from my back.","At first, I thought it was going to enter the bath on its own.","But instead, it headed into the cave.","It seemed to be running away because it didn’t want a bath.","Despite being so ridiculously slow.","\"Hey. Not that way. Come over here.\"","\"...\"","In the end, I picked it up myself and tried to place it inside the iron tub.","No.","More precisely, I attempted to place it inside.","Grip!","Before I could, it clung tightly to my arm as though refusing to let go.","It was even trembling.","It seemed frightened.","That made even less sense, considering it could see an arrow coming and snatch it out of the air.","\"...Hey.\"","\"Do you hate baths?\"","There was no response.","It couldn’t speak in the first place.","But the fact that it refused to budge made its feelings perfectly clear.","Even so, I couldn’t simply give up on hygiene.","I tried forcing the Swift Sloth into the tub.","Whoosh! Whoosh! Whoosh!","Each time, it darted across different parts of my body with lightning-fast movements.","It slipped around me as though my body were a tree.","And it did so at an astonishing speed, as if entering the tub would kill it.","\"Ah, seriously! Do whatever you want! I’ll take the bath myself!\"","\"...\"","I finally gave up.","Only after hearing my declaration of surrender did the Swift Sloth begin moving slowly again.","\"...Did you really think I’d say that and mean it?\"","\"?!\"","It was a fake-out, you bastard.","I seized the Swift Sloth’s arm while its guard was down.","Now that I’d restrained one arm, it would have no choice but to enter quietly.","Sure, it still had one arm free, but there was no way it could do anything with just that.","Splash!","I had been completely mistaken.","The Swift Sloth swung its remaining arm toward the iron tub.","The tub was cleanly sliced into several pieces, spilling the warm water everywhere.","It wasn’t that it couldn’t do anything.","It absolutely could.","In the silence that followed, I stared at the Swift Sloth.","It stared back at me.","Its expression seemed to say:","—What exactly do you think you can do about it?","Another defeat for me today."]},{"title":"Chapter 34","paragraphs":["Assistant Moderator (1)","After suffering yet another defeat at the hands of the Swift Sloth, I finished cleaning up the mess.","Losing the iron tub was a shame, but they were everywhere in the auction house, so replacing it wouldn’t be difficult.","Besides, I had sold the owlbear’s corpse and the logs, so my finances were in fairly good shape.","I’d just listed the Inner Core as well, so my wallet would probably be even fuller tomorrow.","I wonder how much the Inner Core will sell for.","The Heavenly Demon had said that it was difficult to put a price on one.","That might actually cause people to underestimate its value.","After all, an Inner Core was an incredibly rare elixir.","People regularly posted about being scammed in the auction house, so naturally, buyers would be even more suspicious of an Inner Core.","It was fortunate that I’d built up some credibility by now. Otherwise, I couldn’t have complained if people accused me of being a scammer.","It’s not like I personally tested the Inner Core’s effects.","The benefits I’d experienced had come from eating the fish, not the Inner Core itself.","Even that wasn’t completely certain.","I had only just taken my first step into the worlds of mana and internal energy.","The Heavenly Demon and several other regulars possessed expertise, but none of them were here beside me.","Something even they didn’t understand was happening inside my body, so it was difficult to draw a definite conclusion.","Still, I’m certain that it had some effect.","In less than a single day, my strength and stamina had increased dramatically.","Even simple physical labor like logging and digging had become effortless.","I didn’t know the exact reason, but I had undoubtedly grown stronger through that process.","That much, I could guarantee.","I still have some time. Should I explore the surrounding area?","The repairs to my base were complete.","All that remained was receiving the barricades from the dwarf.","Before then, I planned to decide which area to explore next.","I entered the cave.","Inside, Wonmo was sleeping soundly.","How could even his sleeping form be so adorable and lovable?","I had to take a picture and upload it.","***","Title: A Round Ball of Fur","Wild Grylls","(Photo of Wonmo sleeping while curled into a ball.)","(Video of Wonmo sleeping peacefully.)","Seriously, every time I look at him, I feel completely at peace.","How can something be this cute?","Wow. He really is adorable.","I’ll admit he’s cute if you still say that after he grows up lol.","Don’t animals grow really quickly?","Most of them are probably fully grown within a year.","Wild Grylls: Hey, you bastards. Are you telling me to stay here for an entire year?","This is the Forest of Four Seasons. Can you even escape? Lol.","Wild Grylls: I have to try. I’m planning to start exploring now.","You’re going to leave Wonmo here alone? What if something attacks him?","That was a good point.","It would be dangerous to leave Wonmo alone while I explored.","Ideally, I wanted to take him with me, but Wonmo was weaker than I was.","Even the last time I’d gone to the river, the Swift Sloth had suddenly appeared.","It had been fine because I’d returned quickly, and the Swift Sloth wasn’t actually hostile.","Should I take Wonmo with me?","There was another option.","I could leave the Swift Sloth in the cave.","Honestly, that was probably the best solution.","The downside was that I would be putting myself in greater danger.","The Swift Sloth had saved me when the chameleon viper nearly got me last time.","Its overwhelming visual acuity and agility would also make it incredibly useful during exploration.","This is difficult.","Should I leave Wonmo alone and go exploring?","Or should I leave the Swift Sloth here with him?","After thinking about it for some time, I spoke to the creature hanging from my back.","\"Swiftie.\"","The Swift Sloth slowly tilted its head at my call.","\"You’ll have to guard the cave.\"","\"If you protect it until I return, I’ll give you a fasting pill.\"","Upon hearing that, the Swift Sloth slowly climbed down from my back.","It definitely understood what I was saying.","It was truly fascinating.","There was absolutely nothing strange about me, so the Swift Sloth had to be the unusual one.","Wonmo could also understand me, but I decided not to think about that.","Questions and their answers were luxuries for times when one had room to spare.","When survival was the priority, they were nothing more than meaningless distractions.","\"When Wonmo wakes up, tell him where I went. Understood?\"","Nod, nod.","The Swift Sloth nodded to show that it accepted my request.","Now that I had assigned him a reliable bodyguard, all that remained was preparing for the expedition.","As always, I brought the Heavenly Demon’s sword and the golden shield.","I also wore clean clothes.","They were the ones I’d washed when I bathed Wonmo earlier.","Princess Chaenggu said she’d give me long clothes later, right?","I didn’t know how long that would take, but it probably wouldn’t be long.","She had been willing to give me a high-quality uniform without hesitation, after all.","I also packed an elixir and some fasting pills in case of an emergency.","Now all that remained was setting out.","Should I try going this way today?","I had been gradually exploring in all four directions around the cave.","The river where the Golden Poison Frog appeared was to the northeast, while the mature Mandrake habitat was to the northwest.","Of course, I didn’t have a compass, so I couldn’t be certain those directions were accurate.","They were based entirely on my sense of direction.","This time, I planned to travel toward what I believed was west.","I should return before lunch.","After exploring, I planned to receive the barricades from Passing Dwarf and reinforce the base.","In less than a week, my overall physical abilities had improved dramatically.","Manual labor was no longer particularly difficult.","Exploration would probably become my main daily activity before long.","\"I’m heading out. Guard the house properly.\"","\"...\"","As I left the cave, the Swift Sloth slowly waved its hand at me.","It was clearly telling me to have a safe trip.","No matter how I looked at it, it seemed more like a person than an animal.","Chirp, chirp— Chirp, chirp—","I headed in a completely new direction, away from both the river and the Mandrake habitat.","The deafening sounds of insects pierced my ears and heightened my tension.","To avoid getting lost, I marked the path at regular intervals.","I can’t trust everything I see.","The chameleon viper had taught me that I could never let my guard down.","From time to time, I struck tree trunks with the back of my blade or swept aside bushes.","I moved as cautiously as possible.","It might slow my progress, but it was safer.","Even though I had an elixir, I needed to conserve it.","\"Hm?\"","I had been advancing little by little when something on the ground caught my eye.","It was completely black, so at first I thought it was charcoal.","But judging by the flies swarming around it, it definitely wasn’t.","It’s poop.","Animal droppings.","I had no idea what kind of animal had left them.","In the civilized world, people would simply dismiss feces as something filthy.","But things were completely different in the wild.","Animals often used their droppings to mark their territory.","It was essentially a warning:","This is my territory. Enter, and you’ll die.","The flies make it look fairly old. Could it belong to the owlbear?","I wasn’t an expert, so I couldn’t tell what animal it came from.","For now, I guessed it belonged to the owlbear that had been sent to America.","Wonmo’s droppings were different in size, but their overall appearance was similar.","Still, asking the Gallery was the best option.","I should add a content warning, right?","I needed to be careful, or I might get banned.","Without lowering my guard, I wrote a post on the Gallery.","***","Title: Mildly Graphic—Whose Is This?","Wild Grylls","(Photo of animal droppings.)","Found this while exploring today.","Does anyone know what animal left it?","If it’s from the owlbear, I’ll keep exploring. If it belongs to something else, I’ll reconsider.","Ugh, that’s fucking disgusting.","Damn, it really left a massive pile lol.","Mix some rice into that and you’ve got yourself a full meal lol.","Fuck this. I’m blocking you. That’s disgusting.","Wild Grylls: Enough nonsense. Does it belong to an owlbear or not?","Looks like it. Aren’t owlbears the only ones that leave poop that black?","Don’t normal bears also leave droppings like that?","Allfather: It is indeed owlbear excrement. Judging from its size, I believe it came from the specimen you killed previously.","As expected of Fatheremon.","He was the only intelligent person among this crowd of idiots.","Since it was Allfather saying it, I could trust the answer.","I thanked him and continued walking.","Just in case, I deleted the post afterward.","The Moderator might see it and ban me.","Maybe it would have been fine if he were flexible, but he had a tendency to follow the rules rather strictly.","It was better to be safe.","I’m surprised the Heavenly Demon didn’t leave a comment.","The Heavenly Demon probably disliked filthy things too.","Understandable.","In any case, now that the droppings had been confirmed to belong to the owlbear, it should be safe to continue exploring.","Oh. Are those wild raspberries?","While exploring, I discovered some delicious-looking berries.","They were red and plump, unmistakably resembling wild raspberries.","But this was the Forest of Four Seasons—a demonic hell where even ordinary plants could be poisonous.","Even before coming here, I had been highly susceptible to rashes from poisonous plants, so I decided to ask the Gallery before gathering them.","I wanted to avoid dropping dead after thoughtlessly eating something.","***","Title: Is This Safe to Eat?","Wild Grylls","(Photo of berries resembling wild raspberries.)","They look delicious. Can I eat them?","Aren’t those wild raspberries?","Do wild raspberries even grow in this forest?","Aren’t raspberries usually round? Why are those so long?","Try one. Eat it and tell us how it tastes.","Wild Grylls: I don’t trust anything you bastards say.","Then why did you ask?","Wild Grylls: Give me a proper explanation.","Allfather: Do not eat them. They are jack-in-the-pulpit berries, which are sometimes used for suicide. They contain a deadly poison.","Wild Grylls: Thank you. ;;","Allfather: Wild raspberries are round, so they should be fairly easy to distinguish.","Damn, that was close lol.","What a shame.","You seriously deserve to get banned.","I stared at the raspberry-like berries before crushing them underfoot.","It would serve as a directional marker.","A sign showing that I had already passed through this path.","Every little marker mattered.","Should I buy some paint?","That wasn’t a bad idea.","It would be useful when I traveled farther away like this.","I continued making my way through the forest, pushing aside vegetation and weaving between the trees.","I never forgot to be careful not to lose my way.","I wandered around for some time before finally encountering something that could serve as a proper landmark.","\"Wow. That’s enormous.\"","I looked up in amazement.","The sight naturally made my jaw drop.","A massive mushroom stood directly in front of me.","It was no ordinary mushroom.","Even its height far exceeded mine.","Calling it gigantic didn’t seem sufficient.","It was a colossal mushroom.","What the hell was this thing?","It looks like a matsutake mushroom, though.","I could probably use this mushroom as a landmark from now on.","I could explore the surrounding area using it as a reference point.","There’s quite a lot of open space around it. Why?","Before approaching the mushroom, I examined the surroundings.","No matter how large it was, the fact that it stood completely alone was suspicious.","Perhaps it had absorbed the nutrients meant for all the nearby plants.","I first needed to identify it, so I uploaded a post to the Gallery.","Wow. It’s as big as my dick.","Wanna see?","You fucking lunatic.","Allfather: You should be careful around that mushroom. It may be a Mushroom Man.","Wild Grylls: A Mushroom Man?","Allfather: Yes. It is a creature formed from the fusion of a monster and a mushroom. They do not normally grow anywhere near that large, but I suppose this is the Forest of Four Seasons.","Wild Grylls: Is it strong?","Allfather: Honestly, not particularly. However, it scatters spores, so you will need fire.","***","Title: Found a Fucking Huge Mushroom","Wild Grylls","(Photo of the colossal mushroom.)","It’s taller than me. You can estimate its size by comparing it to the trees beside it.","Does anyone know what this thing is?","Fire, huh?","I nodded.","I had the ignition stone the Heavenly Demon had given me, but there was no reason to provoke it unnecessarily.","It wasn’t like I planned to eat it.","There was no need to waste my strength.","I was about to circle around the mushroom when—","\"Hm?\"","I noticed a cave behind it.","The mushroom completely blocked the cave entrance, making it impossible to enter.","I suddenly became curious about what might be inside.","It’s like some kind of dungeon gatekeeper.","Curiosity aside, I valued my life.","Having already survived several life-threatening situations, I was able to abandon the idea without hesitation.","Rrrrrumble!","But the world refused to leave me alone.","I was startled by the sudden vibration, but quickly realized where it was coming from.","The colossal mushroom was shaking violently, as though it were about to rip itself out of the ground.","Ah, shit.","This always happened.","I slowly backed away.","I didn’t have fire prepared, but I planned to gauge how strong it was before fleeing.","Even if I fought it, the only reward would be getting to see the inside of that cave.","Crack! Craaack!","The earth split apart, revealing the mushroom’s true form.","Allfather had described the body shape of a Mushroom Man like this:","Extremely short limbs that looked disproportionately tiny compared to its bloated body.","He had said that even if it grew larger, its proportions should remain roughly the same.","\"Kuuk.\"","He was completely wrong.","Its arms and legs were long, almost like a human’s.","Long limbs alone would have been manageable.","But they were also packed with bulging muscles like those of a bodybuilder.","Its body was long and mushroom-like, while its limbs resembled those of a muscular human.","It was bizarre beyond words.","No, bizarre wasn’t enough.","It was grotesque.","The Mushroom Man kicked off the ground and closed the distance between us in an instant.","It seemed to take only one step, yet suddenly it was right in front of my face.","That much was manageable.","It wasn’t particularly fast.","I could see it move and react.","It was far slower than the Swift Sloth.","Let’s try blocking one hit.","The Mushroom Man’s right fist shot toward my abdomen.","I raised the golden shield.","Considering the shield’s performance and my recently increased strength, I should have been able to withstand it.","\"Kuooooh!\"","The Mushroom Man let out a powerful roar.","BOOOOM!","\"Guh?!\"","A tremendous impact struck the shield, sending my body flying backward.","***","Wow. Of all the things I’ve experienced...","After fleeing back to the cave, I lamented inwardly and stared at the front of the golden shield.","A clear fist-shaped dent had been left in it.","I had only escaped unharmed because of the shield.","Without it, that single punch would have killed me.","Afterward, I had fled without even looking back.","Fortunately, the Mushroom Man didn’t pursue me.","Why the hell does a Mushroom Man know the One-Inch Punch?","Its muscular limbs had given me some idea of what to expect, but I hadn’t imagined it would be that powerful.","Had I taken the punch directly, it would have punched straight through my stomach.","Either that, or everything inside me would have come bursting out of my mouth.","I sighed in relief and uploaded another post to the Gallery.","***","Title: Got Hit by a Mushroom Man’s One-Inch Punch","Wild Grylls","(Photo of the shield with a distinct fist-shaped dent.)","That bastard used a One-Inch Punch on me and did this to my shield.","Thank God I had it, or I would’ve been completely fucked. ;;","Damn. Look how clear that dent is. If you’d taken that barehanded, it would’ve punched through your stomach.","A Mushroom Man is that strong? What the hell did it look like?","Wild Grylls: Its limbs were seriously muscular. They were completely jacked.","I can’t picture it. Upload a photo.","Wild Grylls: (Photo of the muscular Mushroom Man.)","LMAOOOOO, what the hell is that?!","Holy shit lol. Its body is better than mine.","That thing looks fucking strong lol.","Can that truly be called a Mushroom Man?","Praisethesun: What the hell happened to my shield? That thing is seriously high-quality. ;;","Wild Grylls: You mean I would’ve died without it, right? Thank you so much, brother.","Praisethesun: You don’t need to thank me. Still, that’s surprising. What the hell did you fight?","Wild Grylls: A mushroom.","Praisethesun: The world truly is a strange place.","Allfather: Fascinating. Did you notice anything else unusual?","Wild Grylls: No. All I know is that it was ridiculously strong.","Allfather: Hmm... I do not know. I genuinely have no idea. What kind of place is that forest?","While I was organizing my thoughts, one particular comment caught my eye.","Heavenly Demon: What an intriguing tale. A fist powerful enough to dent a shield, even one made of gold... Its strength would not be inferior even when compared to mine.","Even Allfather didn’t know what it was.","The other users could do little more than express their amazement.","Apparently, this was abnormal even by the standards of the people in this world.","That showed just how far outside common sense the Forest of Four Seasons truly was.","Though a sloth that could see a fired arrow and snatch it out of the air was equally absurd.","Why was that thing blocking the entrance to the cave?","The way it stood guard like a guardian deity only made me more curious.","But the Mushroom Man was far too strong.","A direct confrontation was impossible.","I would need to use some kind of trick to get past it.","The Heavenly Demon.","She was normally the regular who replied first to nearly every one of my posts.","The fact that she was late today suggested she had something else to do.","But something else caught my attention even more.","Wild Grylls: Hello, Heavenly Demon. But... you are the Heavenly Demon, right?","Heavenly Demon: If you are asking whether this is indeed me, then yes. Why do you ask?","Huh? Why did her name suddenly turn blue?","Why the hell is she blue now?","Wait. Why did she suddenly turn blue?","Users who noticed it before I did flooded the post with comments.","Most of them were confused.","Naturally so.","Beside the Heavenly Demon’s username was a blue badge that had never been there before.","Heavenly Demon: Ah. I nearly forgot. From now on, you may address me as the Assistant Moderator.","The Heavenly Demon had returned as an Assistant Moderator."]}]);
